5. Entities must frame their activity in only one application and, in the event of support being granted, the respective contract constitutes the sole support instrument for the period to which it is intended, except as provided for in paragraph 4 of Article 26 of Decree-Law No. 103/2017, of 24 August, in its current wording.",Conforme aviso publicado na 2.ª série do Diário da República de 24 de agosto,2027-08-24,2026-09-23 12:37:19.600724+00:00
dgartes_portugal_9958967f7dcb,dgartes_portugal,http://www.dgartes.gov.pt/sites/default/files/avisodeabertura_bv2027.pdf,,Direção-Geral das Artes (DGARTES),"A Direção-Geral das Artes (DGARTES) torna público, através do presente aviso, a abertura do concurso limitado para a apresentação de candidaturas no âmbito do Programa de Apoio a Projetos – Representação Oficial Portuguesa, na 20.ª Exposição Internacional de Arquitetura – La Biennale di Venezia 2027, para seleção do projeto curatorial e expositivo, conforme o disposto no Decreto -Lei n.º 103/2017, de 24 de agosto, na redação atual e no Regulamento dos Programas de Apoio às Artes aprovado em anexo à Portaria n.º 345-A/2026/1, de 14 de agosto, nos termos seguintes:",Arquitetura,concurso limitado,Itália,Veneza,"1. Dotação financeira disponível: 1. 500.000,00€ (quinhentos mil euros), com a seguinte distribuição anual: a) 2026 – 300.000,00€ (trezentos mil euros); b) 2027 – até 200.000,00€ (duzentos mil euros). 2. O montante máximo a ser solicitado em candidatura é de 497.000,00€ (quatrocentos e noventa e sete mil euros).",,,"The Directorate-General for the Arts (DGARTES) hereby makes public, through this notice, the opening of the restricted call for the submission of applications within the scope of the Project Support Program – Portuguese Official Representation, at the 20th International Architecture Exhibition – La Biennale di Venezia 2027, for the selection of the curatorial and exhibition project, as provided for in Decree-Law No. 103/2017, of 24 August, in its current wording and in the Regulation of the Arts Support Programs approved in annex to Ordinance No. 345-A/2026/1, of 14 August, under the following terms:",architecture,limited competition,,Italy,Venice,['Design/Architecture'],['Competition/Prize'],[],['Italy'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 497000.0, 'amount_max': 497000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'maximum amount that can be requested in the application; annual distribution of the programme budget also listed'}]",2026-09-24 08:56:55.545057+00:00,,,,,pt,Programa de Apoio a Projetos – Representação Oficial Portuguesa na 20.ª Exposição Internacional de Arquitetura – La Biennale di Venezia 2027,"E. Destinatários: Nos termos do Aviso n.º 15360/2026/2, de 22 de junho, foram selecionadas as seguintes propostas a convidar para integrar o concurso limitado: − Analog Twins, de Alice Clanet-Hallard, Edgar Brito, Francisco Lobo e Romea Muryn − Mãos ao Chão (Hands to the Ground), de Joanna Alice Helm, Remígio Van Eyes Chilaule e Samuel de Brito Gonçalves − Matéria Viva — Os materiais da construção portuguesa e o saber que resiste, de Helena Botelho",Support Program for Projects – Official Portuguese Representation at the 20th International Architecture Exhibition – La Biennale di Venezia 2027,"E. Recipients: Under Notice No. 15360/2026/2, of 22 June, the following proposals were selected to be invited to take part in the restricted competition: − Analog Twins, by Alice Clanet-Hallard, Edgar Brito, Francisco Lobo and Romea Muryn − Mãos ao Chão (Hands to the Ground), by Joanna Alice Helm, Remígio Van Eyes Chilaule and Samuel de Brito Gonçalves − Matéria Viva — Os materiais da construção portuguesa e o saber que resiste, by Helena Botelho",6 de outubro de 2026,2026-10-06,2026-09-23 12:37:21.058425+00:00
dgartes_portugal_c966cce2ccf0,dgartes_portugal,https://www.dgartes.gov.pt/pt/apoio/10166,https://apoios.dgartes.gov.pt/,Direção-Geral das Artes (DGARTES),"a abertura do concurso limitado para a apresentação de candidaturas no âmbito do Programa de Apoio a Projetos – Representação Oficial Portuguesa, na 20.ª Exposição Internacional de Arquitetura – La Biennale di Venezia 2027, para seleção do projeto curatorial e expositivo",Arquitetura,concurso limitado,Portugal,Lisboa,Apoio Financeiro: €500.000,,,"the opening of the limited competition for the submission of applications within the scope of the Project Support Program – Portuguese Official Representation, at the 20th International Architecture Exhibition – La Biennale di Venezia 2027, for the selection of the curatorial and exhibition project",architecture,limited competition,,Portugal,Lisbon,['Design/Architecture'],['Competition/Prize'],[],['Portugal'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 500000.0, 'amount_max': 500000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'funding amount stated without further detail'}]",2026-09-24 08:56:55.545159+00:00,,,,,pt,[Concurso Limitado] Programa de Apoio a Projetos - Representação Oficial Portuguesa na 20.ª Exposição Internacional de Arquitetura - La Biennale di Venezia 2027,"a apresentação de candidaturas no âmbito do Programa de Apoio a Projetos – Representação Oficial Portuguesa, na 20.ª Exposição Internacional de Arquitetura – La Biennale di Venezia 2027, para seleção do projeto curatorial e expositivo",[Limited Competition] Project Support Program - Official Portuguese Representation at the 20th International Architecture Exhibition - La Biennale di Venezia 2027,"applications under the Project Support Program – Official Portuguese Representation, for the 20th International Architecture Exhibition – La Biennale di Venezia 2027, for the selection of the curatorial and exhibition project",às 17h59m59s do dia 6 de outubro de 2026,2026-09-25,2026-09-23 12:37:22.307414+00:00
dgartes_portugal_b0e4ca961b8e,dgartes_portugal,http://www.dgartes.gov.pt/sites/default/files/aviso_abertura_orquestra_regional_alentejo_2026.pdf,,DGARTES,Concurso para criação de Orquestra Regional do Alentejo,música erudita,Concurso,Portugal,Alentejo,"O montante global disponível é de 1.620.000 € (um milhão seiscentos e vinte mil euros ), a atribuir por um período de dois anos: 2027: 810.000 € 2028: 810.000 €",,,Competition for the creation of the Regional Orchestra of Alentejo,classical music,competition,,Portugal,Alentejo,['Music'],['Competition/Prize'],[],['Portugal'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 1620000.0, 'amount_max': 1620000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'total programme budget over two years, not per applicant; distributed as 810,000 EUR in 2027 and 810,000 EUR in 2028'}]",2026-09-24 08:56:55.545186+00:00,,,,,pt,Concurso para criação de Orquestra Regional do Alentejo,"Pessoas coletivas de direito privado sem fins lucrativos, com sede na região do Alentejo , doravante designadas entidades promotoras das orquestras regionais.
Não são admitidas ao procedimento concursal as fundações privadas ou as fundações públicas de direito privado que tenham outro tipo de financiamento continuado, assegurado pelo programa orçamental da área da cultura, bem como empresas do setor público empresarial do Estado. 
2. Estão impedidas de apresentar candidaturas ao presente programa de apoio  as entidades beneficiárias de Apoio Sustentado.   

3. Os órgãos sociais das entidades promotoras das orquestras regionais devem incluir  um número mínimo de cinco municípios na circunscrição territorial ( NUTS II) do Alentejo. 
4. Os órgãos sociais podem incluir ainda outros agentes locais ou regionais da região onde se insere a Orquestra Regional, para além do número de municípios mencionados no n.º 3.",Call for the creation of the Alentejo Regional Orchestra,"Private legal entities without profit-making purposes, with headquarters in the Alentejo region, hereinafter referred to as promoting entities of the regional orchestras.
Private foundations or public foundations under private law that have another type of ongoing funding ensured by the budget programme of the culture area, as well as companies of the State public business sector, are not admitted to the competitive procedure.
2. Entities benefiting from Sustained Support are barred from submitting applications to this support programme.

3. The governing bodies of the promoting entities of the regional orchestras must include a minimum number of five municipalities in the territorial circumscription (NUTS II) of Alentejo.
4. The governing bodies may also include other local or regional agents of the region where the Regional Orchestra is located, in addition to the number of municipalities mentioned in point 3.",Conforme aviso publicado na 2.ª série do Diário da República de 15 de julho,2027-07-15,2026-09-23 12:37:23.908569+00:00
dgartes_portugal_cc9be82e728f,dgartes_portugal,https://www.dgartes.gov.pt/pt/apoio/10064,https://www.dgartes.gov.pt/sites/default/files/formulario_concurso_orquestra_regional_alentejo_2026.xlsx,Direção-Geral das Artes (DGARTES),"a abertura de concurso para criação da Orquestra Regional do Alentejo, com o montante financeiro global disponível de 1.620.000,00 € (um milhão seiscentos e vinte mil euros), com a seguinte distribuição anual: 2027: 810.000,00 € (oitocentos e dez mil euros); 2028: 810.000,00 € (oitocentos e dez mil euros).",Artes / música,concurso,Portugal,,"com o montante financeiro global disponível de 1.620.000,00 € (um milhão seiscentos e vinte mil euros), com a seguinte distribuição anual: 2027: 810.000,00 € (oitocentos e dez mil euros); 2028: 810.000,00 € (oitocentos e dez mil euros).",,,"the open call for the creation of the Alentejo Regional Orchestra, with the total financial amount available of €1,620,000.00 (one million six hundred and twenty thousand euros), with the following annual distribution: 2027: €810,000.00 (eight hundred and ten thousand euros); 2028: €810,000.00 (eight hundred and ten thousand euros).",arts / music,competition,,Portugal,,['Music'],['Competition/Prize'],[],['Portugal'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 1620000.0, 'amount_max': 1620000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'total programme budget over two years, not per applicant; distributed as 810,000 EUR in 2027 and 810,000 EUR in 2028'}]",2026-09-24 08:56:55.545251+00:00,,,,,pt,CONCURSO PARA CRIAÇÃO DA ORQUESTRA REGIONAL DO ALENTEJO,As candidaturas estão abertas até ao dia 9 de setembro de 2026.,OPEN CALL FOR THE CREATION OF THE ALENTEJO REGIONAL ORCHESTRA,"Applications are open until September 9, 2026.",Novo prazo: a apresentação de candidaturas termina às 17:59:59 do dia 25 de setembro de 2026.,2026-09-24,2026-09-23 12:37:24.916519+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_ad15a329abd7,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/culture-helps-solidarity-%d0%ba%d1%83%d0%bb%d1%8c%d1%82%d1%83%d1%80%d0%b0-%d0%b4%d0%be%d0%bf%d0%be%d0%bc%d0%b0%d0%b3%d0%b0%d1%94-open-call-for-collaboration-grants/second-culture-helps-solidarity-call-for-collaboration-grants/,https://culture-of-solidarity-fund.grantplatform.com/,Culture Helps Solidarity,"Culture Helps Solidarity is launching its second and final call for Collaboration Grants . This call supports international projects that use arts and culture to aid the integration of displaced Ukrainians into host communities, with a strong focus on mental well-being, vulnerable groups, and veterans . The fund prioritises cross-border partnerships between at least one Ukrainian-led organisation (operating in Ukraine or in exile) and at least one organisation based in a Creative Europe country . Grants of up to €20,000 are available for partnerships of two organisations, and up to €30,000 for partnerships involving three or more partners . The projects should foster intercultural dialogue, professional exchange, and long-term solidarity .",arts and culture,Collaboration Grants,,,"Grants of up to €20,000 are available for partnerships of two organisations, and up to €30,000 for partnerships involving three or more partners .",,,"Culture Helps Solidarity is launching its second and final call for Collaboration Grants . This call supports international projects that use arts and culture to aid the integration of displaced Ukrainians into host communities, with a strong focus on mental well-being, vulnerable groups, and veterans . The fund prioritises cross-border partnerships between at least one Ukrainian-led organisation (operating in Ukraine or in exile) and at least one organisation based in a Creative Europe country . Grants of up to €20,000 are available for partnerships of two organisations, and up to €30,000 for partnerships involving three or more partners . The projects should foster intercultural dialogue, professional exchange, and long-term solidarity .",arts and culture,Collaboration Grants,,,,['Multidisciplinary'],['Grant/Funding'],[],[],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 20000.0, 'amount_max': 20000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'up to for partnerships of two organisations'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 30000.0, 'amount_max': 30000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'up to for partnerships involving three or more partners'}]",2026-09-24 08:56:55.545317+00:00,,,,,en,Second Culture Helps Solidarity call for Collaboration Grants,The fund prioritises cross-border partnerships between at least one Ukrainian-led organisation (operating in Ukraine or in exile) and at least one organisation based in a Creative Europe country .,Second Culture Helps Solidarity call for Collaboration Grants,The fund prioritises cross-border partnerships between at least one Ukrainian-led organisation (operating in Ukraine or in exile) and at least one organisation based in a Creative Europe country .,"November 10, 2026, at 13:00 Amsterdam time / 14:00 Kyiv time",2026-11-10,2026-09-23 12:37:24.930215+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_f1e9b1c26c84,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/second-culture-helps-solidarity-call-for-project-grants/,https://culture-of-solidarity-fund.grantplatform.com/,Culture Helps Solidarity,"The second call for Projects Grants of Culture Helps Solidarity focuses on memory and commemoration projects that work responsibly with the lived experiences of people affected byRussia’s war against Ukraine. The call will support cultural and community-based initiatives that create meaningful forms of remembrance, documentation (both analog and digital), public reflection, and commemoration while respecting the dignity, safety, and agency of thosewhose stories and losses are represented. This call supports small-scale cultural projects that engage with the experiences, memories, and histories of people directly affected by Russia’s war against Ukraine, including but not limited to women veterans, families of the fallen, displaced communities, local residents,people who have experienced loss, captivity, injury, or displacement, and witnesses of wartime events. We invite cultural workers, artists, researchers, community organisers, memory practitioners, and civil society initiatives based in Ukraine and across Europe to develop projects that approach remembrance as a careful, inclusive, and community-led practice. Through artistic, educational, research-based, or participatory formats, projects should create meaningful opportunities for reflection, strengthen local and collective memory across generations, amplify diverse voices, and help people feel seen and heard. Ultimately, the call seeks to support cultural practices that contribute to a more responsible public conversation about theongoing impact and aftermath of Russia’s war against Ukraine, both within Ukraine and across Europe.","cultural, artistic, educational, research-based, or participatory",Project Grants,Ukraine and across Europe,,Project Grants,,,"The second call for Projects Grants of Culture Helps Solidarity focuses on memory and commemoration projects that work responsibly with the lived experiences of people affected byRussia’s war against Ukraine. The call will support cultural and community-based initiatives that create meaningful forms of remembrance, documentation (both analog and digital), public reflection, and commemoration while respecting the dignity, safety, and agency of thosewhose stories and losses are represented. This call supports small-scale cultural projects that engage with the experiences, memories, and histories of people directly affected by Russia’s war against Ukraine, including but not limited to women veterans, families of the fallen, displaced communities, local residents,people who have experienced loss, captivity, injury, or displacement, and witnesses of wartime events. We invite cultural workers, artists, researchers, community organisers, memory practitioners, and civil society initiatives based in Ukraine and across Europe to develop projects that approach remembrance as a careful, inclusive, and community-led practice. Through artistic, educational, research-based, or participatory formats, projects should create meaningful opportunities for reflection, strengthen local and collective memory across generations, amplify diverse voices, and help people feel seen and heard. Ultimately, the call seeks to support cultural practices that contribute to a more responsible public conversation about theongoing impact and aftermath of Russia’s war against Ukraine, both within Ukraine and across Europe.","cultural, artistic, educational, research-based, or participatory",Project Grants,,Ukraine and across Europe,,['Multidisciplinary'],['Grant/Funding'],[],"['Ukraine', 'Europe (unspecified)']",[],2026-09-24 08:56:55.545383+00:00,,,,,en,Second Culture Helps Solidarity call for Project Grants,"We invite cultural workers, artists, researchers, community organisers, memory practitioners, and civil society initiatives based in Ukraine and across Europe to develop projects that approach remembrance as a careful, inclusive, and community-led practice.",Second Culture Helps Solidarity call for Project Grants,"We invite cultural workers, artists, researchers, community organisers, memory practitioners, and civil society initiatives based in Ukraine and across Europe to develop projects that approach remembrance as a careful, inclusive, and community-led practice.",,,2026-09-23 12:37:24.930266+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_80ce5461aa91,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/new-fellowship-programme-to-research-the-ecf-historical-archives/,https://ecf-fellowship.grantplatform.com/,European Cultural Foundation,"This ECF Fellowship aims to foster new research and creative work engaging with the history of the European Cultural Foundation and the broader role of culture in shaping Europe as a shared space of imagination, cooperation, and solidarity.",research and creative work,Fellowship programme,,Florence,"Academic Research Fellowship includes a grant of €5,000 to support a research stay at the HAEU, including travel, accommodation, and living expenses. Artistic Research Fellowship includes a grant of €10,000 to support a research stay at the HAEU, including travel, accommodation, and living expenses, as well as artistic production.",,,"This ECF Fellowship aims to foster new research and creative work engaging with the history of the European Cultural Foundation and the broader role of culture in shaping Europe as a shared space of imagination, cooperation, and solidarity.",research and creative work,Fellowship programme,,,Florence,['Other/Non-Arts'],['Fellowship'],[],[],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 5000.0, 'amount_max': 5000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'Academic Research Fellowship'}, {'category': 'Travel Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'included in the fellowship grant'}, {'category': 'Accommodation/Housing', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'included in the fellowship grant'}, {'category': 'Other/Unspecified Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'living expenses included in the fellowship grant'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:00.110344+00:00,,,,,en,New Fellowship Programme to Research the ECF Historical Archives,"Fellows are expected to work substantially with the ECF archival holdings – primarily in English, with significant material in French, German, and Dutch, and additional languages occasionally represented.",New Fellowship Programme to Research the ECF Historical Archives,"Fellows are expected to work substantially with the ECF archival holdings – primarily in English, with significant material in French, German, and Dutch, and additional languages occasionally represented.",30 September 2026 at 17:00 CET,2026-09-30,2026-09-23 12:37:24.938042+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_a246059c820a,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/culture-helps-solidarity-open-call-for-individual-grants-4th-round/,https://qr1.be/8KS5J3,European Cultural Foundation,"The fourth round of Culture Helps Solidarity Individual Grants is now open . The programme offers flexible grants of up to €1,200 to Ukrainian cultural professionals working with displaced people, refugees and other vulnerable communities, including veterans, in Ukraine and across Creative Europe countries. Rather than funding projects, these grants are designed to support the individuals behind the work.",cultural professionals,Individual Grants,Ukraine,,"flexible grants of up to €1,200",,,"The fourth round of Culture Helps Solidarity Individual Grants is now open . The programme offers flexible grants of up to €1,200 to Ukrainian cultural professionals working with displaced people, refugees and other vulnerable communities, including veterans, in Ukraine and across Creative Europe countries. Rather than funding projects, these grants are designed to support the individuals behind the work.",cultural professionals,Individual Grants,,Ukraine,,['Other/Non-Arts'],['Grant/Funding'],[],['Ukraine'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': 1200.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'flexible grants of up to'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:00.110413+00:00,,,,,en,Culture Helps Solidarity: Open Call for Individual Grants (4th Round),"to Ukrainian cultural professionals working with displaced people, refugees and other vulnerable communities, including veterans, in Ukraine and across Creative Europe countries.",Culture Helps Solidarity: Open Call for Individual Grants (4th Round),"to Ukrainian cultural professionals working with displaced people, refugees and other vulnerable communities, including veterans, in Ukraine and across Creative Europe countries.",29 June 2026,2026-06-29,2026-09-23 12:37:24.944339+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_67a05c59b453,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/culture-helps-solidarity-%d0%ba%d1%83%d0%bb%d1%8c%d1%82%d1%83%d1%80%d0%b0-%d0%b4%d0%be%d0%bf%d0%be%d0%bc%d0%b0%d0%b3%d0%b0%d1%94-open-call-for-individual-care-grants-round-2/,https://qr1.be/BXQZDY,European Cultural Foundation,"The call supports Ukrainian cultural workers who need time and resources to focus on well-being, recovery and the conditions needed to continue their cultural work.","artists, cultural practitioners and creative professionals",Individual Care Grants,Ukraine,Kyiv,"Across the programme, more than €1.4 million will support over 200 individuals and organisations, alongside opportunities for learning, mentoring and exchange that strengthen professional capacity and cross-border connection.",,,"The call supports Ukrainian cultural workers who need time and resources to focus on well-being, recovery and the conditions needed to continue their cultural work.","artists, cultural practitioners and creative professionals",Individual Care Grants,,Ukraine,Kyiv,['Multidisciplinary'],['Grant/Funding'],[],['Ukraine'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'total programme budget; no per-applicant cap stated'}, {'category': 'Mentorship/Training', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'learning, mentoring and exchange opportunities'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:00.110435+00:00,,,,,en,Culture Helps Solidarity / Культура допомагає: Open Call for Individual Care Grants Round 2,"The grants are open to artists, cultural practitioners and creative professionals from Ukraine, whether they remain in the country or are temporarily displaced elsewhere.",Culture Helps Solidarity / Культура допомагає: Open Call for Individual Care Grants Round 2,"The grants are open to artists, cultural practitioners and creative professionals from Ukraine, whether they remain in the country or are temporarily displaced elsewhere.",6 April 2026 at 13:00 (Amsterdam time),2026-04-06,2026-09-23 12:37:24.949138+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_cf66f32bd199,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/culture-helps-solidarity-%d0%ba%d1%83%d0%bb%d1%8c%d1%82%d1%83%d1%80%d0%b0-%d0%b4%d0%be%d0%bf%d0%be%d0%bc%d0%b0%d0%b3%d0%b0%d1%94-%d1%81%d0%be%d0%bb%d1%96%d0%b4%d0%b0%d1%80%d0%bd%d1%96%d1%81%d1%82/,https://qr1.be/93Y8G0,"Insha Osvita in Kyiv, zusa in Berlin, the Veteranka Movement in Kyiv and the European Cultural Foundation in Amsterdam","Culture Helps Solidarity / Культура допомагає: Солідарність is opening a round of Individual Care Grants from 2 to 23 February 2026 to support creative professionals and veterans in maintaining their mental health and wellbeing, helping them sustain the care and cultural work they provide to others. The programme is delivered by Insha Osvita in Kyiv, zusa in Berlin, the Veteranka Movement in Kyiv and the European Cultural Foundation in Amsterdam. Support focuses on personal well-being rather than project delivery. It may include counselling, trauma-informed coaching, restorative care, or participation in cultural and therapeutic activities that help individuals recover balance and resilience.",arts and culture,Individual Care Grants,Ukraine,Kyiv,"Grants of up to €1,200",,,"Culture Helps Solidarity / Культура допомагає: Солідарність is opening a round of Individual Care Grants from 2 to 23 February 2026 to support creative professionals and veterans in maintaining their mental health and wellbeing, helping them sustain the care and cultural work they provide to others. The programme is delivered by Insha Osvita in Kyiv, zusa in Berlin, the Veteranka Movement in Kyiv and the European Cultural Foundation in Amsterdam. Support focuses on personal well-being rather than project delivery. It may include counselling, trauma-informed coaching, restorative care, or participation in cultural and therapeutic activities that help individuals recover balance and resilience.",arts and culture,Individual Care Grants,,Ukraine,Kyiv,['Multidisciplinary'],['Grant/Funding'],[],['Ukraine'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': 1200.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'grants of up to'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:00.110440+00:00,,,,,en,Culture Helps Solidarity / Культура допомагає: Солідарність Individual Care Grants Open,"individuals working in arts and culture who support displaced Ukrainians, particularly vulnerable groups such as veterans, and who have themselves been affected by war or displacement.",Culture Helps Solidarity / Культура допомагає: Солідарність Individual Care Grants Open,"individuals working in arts and culture who support displaced Ukrainians, particularly vulnerable groups such as veterans, and who have themselves been affected by war or displacement.",from 2 to 23 February 2026,2026-02-23,2026-09-23 12:37:24.952675+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_7395e3ac9c32,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/civitates-media-open-call/,https://civitates-eu.org/funding-opportunity/call-for-proposals-strengthening-independent-public-interest-journalism-in-europe/,Civitates,"Applications are now open for Civitates ’ Media open call for proposals , aimed at supporting independent public interest journalism across Europe. This is an opportunity for non-profit media organizations to secure core funding to strengthen their sustainability, build resilience, and enhance their contributions to a balanced and respectful public dialogue. The call focuses on helping independent media outlets: Strengthen their organizational sustainability and operational stability. Innovate with new business models and editorial strategies. Deepen audience engagement and expand public outreach.",public interest journalism,open call for proposals,Europe,,"Eligible organisations can apply for up to €160,000 in core funding, distributed over two years, to support mid-term goals and operational growth.",,,"Applications are now open for Civitates ’ Media open call for proposals , aimed at supporting independent public interest journalism across Europe. This is an opportunity for non-profit media organizations to secure core funding to strengthen their sustainability, build resilience, and enhance their contributions to a balanced and respectful public dialogue. The call focuses on helping independent media outlets: Strengthen their organizational sustainability and operational stability. Innovate with new business models and editorial strategies. Deepen audience engagement and expand public outreach.",public interest journalism,open call for proposals,,Europe,,['Other/Non-Arts'],['Open Call'],[],['Europe (unspecified)'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 160000.0, 'amount_max': 160000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'per year', 'note': 'core funding distributed over two years'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:00.110461+00:00,,,,,en,Civitates Media Open Call,"Civitates invites applications from independent media outlets registered in Hungary, Poland, Italy, Spain, Bulgaria, Slovakia, and Croatia.",Civitates Media Open Call,"Civitates invites applications from independent media outlets registered in Hungary, Poland, Italy, Spain, Bulgaria, Slovakia, and Croatia.",,,2026-09-23 12:37:24.952720+00:00
fundacao_gulbenkian_641becbe2421,fundacao_gulbenkian,https://gulbenkian.pt/en/bolsas-lista/short-term-conference-and-travel-grant/,,Gulbenkian,"These short-term scholarships enable qualified students, early-career academics and researchers based in Armenia to take part in international conferences, seminars, short courses and research trips abroad related to their field of study. The programme aims to encourage academic exchange and the sharing of knowledge and ideas.",all fields of research,scholarships,Armenia,,"The scholarship amount is fixed; please refer to the table in the Requirements, Criteria and Conditions document for details. All scholarships are awarded and paid in euros.",,"graduate students, early-career academics and researchers","These short-term scholarships enable qualified students, early-career academics and researchers based in Armenia to take part in international conferences, seminars, short courses and research trips abroad related to their field of study. The programme aims to encourage academic exchange and the sharing of knowledge and ideas.",all fields of research,scholarships,"graduate students, early-career academics and researchers",Armenia,,['Other/Non-Arts'],['Grant/Funding'],['Emerging/Early-Career'],['Armenia'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'fixed scholarship amount; paid in euros, amount not specified'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:00.110482+00:00,,,,,en,Short Term Conference and Travel Scholarships,"Applicants must be: Studying or based in Armenia. Under 35 years old at the time of the application. A Master’s or PhD student, or a researcher from Armenia, wishing to attend international conferences, seminars, short-term courses or undertake research trips related to their field of study.",Short Term Conference and Travel Scholarships,"Applicants must be: Studying or based in Armenia. Under 35 years old at the time of the application. A Master’s or PhD student, or a researcher from Armenia, wishing to attend international conferences, seminars, short-term courses or undertake research trips related to their field of study.",End date 04 Dec 2026 / 23:59 Lisbon time,2026-12-04,2026-09-23 12:37:24.956685+00:00
fundacao_gulbenkian_9db5c1bb86df,fundacao_gulbenkian,https://gulbenkian.pt/en/bolsas-lista/visiting-professorships-in-the-humanities/,,Gulbenkian,The Gulbenkian Visiting Professorships in the Humanities aim to strengthen the quality and internationalisation of teaching and research in Portugal by hosting distinguished foreign scholars.,Humanities,Visiting Professorships,Portugal,,"Monthly stipend: €4,000 One-time allowance for travel and relocation: €4,000",,senior researchers with a well-established scientific track record,The Gulbenkian Visiting Professorships in the Humanities aim to strengthen the quality and internationalisation of teaching and research in Portugal by hosting distinguished foreign scholars.,Humanities,Visiting Professorships,senior researchers with a well-established scientific track record,Portugal,,['Other/Non-Arts'],['Other'],['Established/Professional'],['Portugal'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 4000.0, 'amount_max': 4000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'per month', 'note': 'monthly stipend'}, {'category': 'Travel Support', 'amount_min': 4000.0, 'amount_max': 4000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'travel and relocation allowance'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:00.110486+00:00,,,,,en,Visiting Professorships in the Humanities,"Only Portuguese Higher Education Institutions (HEIs) are eligible, and the proposed academic activities must take place in Portugal. Applications must be submitted by the professor responsible for coordinating the visit, on behalf of the Portuguese HEI. The visiting professor is not eligible to apply directly.",Visiting Professorships in the Humanities,"Only Portuguese Higher Education Institutions (HEIs) are eligible, and the proposed academic activities must take place in Portugal. Applications must be submitted by the professor responsible for coordinating the visit, on behalf of the Portuguese HEI. The visiting professor is not eligible to apply directly.",30 Sep 2026 / 17:00 Lisbon time,2026-09-30,2026-09-23 12:37:24.963267+00:00
fundacao_gulbenkian_86e33a273257,fundacao_gulbenkian,https://gulbenkian.pt/en/bolsas-lista/gulbenkian-new-talents-scholarships/,https://gulbenkian.pt/my/login?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fgulbenkian.pt%2F,Gulbenkian Foundation,"The Gulbenkian New Talents Scholarships programme seeks to identify and support exceptionally talented students and foster their first steps into research in core scientific disciplines such as biology, geology, physics, mathematics and chemistry, as well as in any field of the humanities, arts or social sciences.","biology, geology, physics, mathematics and chemistry, as well as in any field of the humanities, arts or social sciences",scholarships,Portugal,,"The annual scholarship amount is made up of three components: Research and study support – €1,000

Talent development support – €1,500

Supplementary social support – €2,000",,students,"The Gulbenkian New Talents Scholarships programme seeks to identify and support exceptionally talented students and foster their first steps into research in core scientific disciplines such as biology, geology, physics, mathematics and chemistry, as well as in any field of the humanities, arts or social sciences.","biology, geology, physics, mathematics and chemistry, as well as in any field of the humanities, arts or social sciences",scholarships,students,Portugal,,['Other/Non-Arts'],['Grant/Funding'],['Student'],['Portugal'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 1000.0, 'amount_max': 1000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'per year', 'note': 'research and study support'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 1500.0, 'amount_max': 1500.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'per year', 'note': 'talent development support'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 2000.0, 'amount_max': 2000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'per year', 'note': 'supplementary social support'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:00.110527+00:00,,,,,en,Gulbenkian New Talents Scholarships,"Applications are open to students who:
Will be enrolled in the 2nd, 3rd or 4th year of a bachelor’s degree or integrated master’s programme, or in the 1st year of a master’s degree, during the 2026/2027 academic year at a higher education institution in Portugal.
Have an average grade of 16.5 or above (on a 20-point scale) in the curricular units completed in the bachelor’s program to date.",Gulbenkian New Talents Scholarships,"Applications are open to students who:
