Have an average grade of 16.5 or above (on a 20-point scale) in the curricular units completed in the bachelor’s program to date.",30 Sep 2026 / 15:00,2026-09-30,2026-09-23 12:37:24.973719+00:00
fundacao_gulbenkian_0089a729f2c8,fundacao_gulbenkian,https://gulbenkian.pt/en/bolsas-lista/gulbenkian-merit-scholarships/,,Gulbenkian,These scholarships are intended to support high-potential young students applying for the first year of higher education who demonstrate limited financial resources.,higher education,scholarships,Portugal,Lisbon,"The scholarship amounts to €2,000 per academic year and includes an additional one-time grant of €2,000 for participation in an international mobility period, such as Erasmus or another similar programme offered by each higher education institution.",,young students,These scholarships are intended to support high-potential young students applying for the first year of higher education who demonstrate limited financial resources.,higher education,scholarships,young students,Portugal,Lisbon,['Other/Non-Arts'],['Grant/Funding'],"['Student', 'Emerging/Early-Career']",['Portugal'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 2000.0, 'amount_max': 2000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': None, 'note': 'scholarship amount'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 2000.0, 'amount_max': 2000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'international mobility period grant'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:00.110609+00:00,,,,,en,Gulbenkian Merit scholarships,"Admission grade for higher education equal to or higher than 170 points through the general access and admission competition for the 2026/27 academic year, in the programme in which the applicant is enrolled. Proof of application for a social action grant from the Directorate-General for Higher Education (DGES). In order to enable verification of household income, applying for a DGES grant is a mandatory condition for applying for the Gulbenkian Merit Scholarship, regardless of household income level. Scholarships will only be awarded to selected applicants whose annual per capita income, as verified by the Social Services of the respective higher education institution, does not exceed €14,000. Only applicants to legally recognised Portuguese higher education institutions and duly accredited and registered study programmes will be considered. Applications from holders of a higher education degree will not be accepted.",Gulbenkian Merit scholarships,"Admission grade for higher education equal to or higher than 170 points through the general access and admission competition for the 2026/27 academic year, in the programme in which the applicant is enrolled. Proof of application for a social action grant from the Directorate-General for Higher Education (DGES). In order to enable verification of household income, applying for a DGES grant is a mandatory condition for applying for the Gulbenkian Merit Scholarship, regardless of household income level. Scholarships will only be awarded to selected applicants whose annual per capita income, as verified by the Social Services of the respective higher education institution, does not exceed €14,000. Only applicants to legally recognised Portuguese higher education institutions and duly accredited and registered study programmes will be considered. Applications from holders of a higher education degree will not be accepted.",30 Oct 2026 / 15:00 Lisbon time,2026-10-30,2026-09-23 12:37:24.977840+00:00
kunst_dk_denmark_28c59766a0db,kunst_dk_denmark,https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/exhibition-of-danish-art-abroad,https://portal.slks.dk//TAS_Dashboard/application/CreateApplication?poolId=7062179a8b2e49e1835fe8c4cd354c60,Danish Arts Foundation,"International Grants for the production, dissemination, and exhibition of contemporary art in Denmark and abroad.",Visual arts,grant,Denmark,,,,,"International Grants for the production, dissemination, and exhibition of contemporary art in Denmark and abroad.",Visual arts,grant,,Denmark,,['Visual Arts'],['Grant/Funding'],[],['Denmark'],[],,,,,,en,Exhibition of Danish Art Abroad,"Who may apply? You can apply if you plan to produce an art piece to be exhibited in Denmark or abroad And You can apply if you shall exhibit and/or promote the work of living visual artists in Denmark or abroad. Is your project interdisciplinary? Find out more about how to apply if your project combines different art forms . The grant does NOT cover: Exhibitions that open before the deadline. Gallery exhibitions: Artists may apply for grants for the production of new works. Other expenses for the exhibition are only covered if the committee assesses them as a special investment by the gallery Permanent works in public space – here defined as art projects that are publicly accessible in a period of more than 12 months. These are funded through other programs. Studio rent Per diem allowance Invitations, meals, etc. in connection with exhibition previews Travel and accommodation for assistants (generally not covered) Travel and accommodation in connection with exhibitions in galleries where the artist has a permanent affiliation Local transport Projects already reviewed by the committee. Costs from previous calendar years.",Exhibition of Danish Art Abroad,"Who may apply? You can apply if you plan to produce an art piece to be exhibited in Denmark or abroad And You can apply if you shall exhibit and/or promote the work of living visual artists in Denmark or abroad. Is your project interdisciplinary? Find out more about how to apply if your project combines different art forms . The grant does NOT cover: Exhibitions that open before the deadline. Gallery exhibitions: Artists may apply for grants for the production of new works. Other expenses for the exhibition are only covered if the committee assesses them as a special investment by the gallery Permanent works in public space – here defined as art projects that are publicly accessible in a period of more than 12 months. These are funded through other programs. Studio rent Per diem allowance Invitations, meals, etc. in connection with exhibition previews Travel and accommodation for assistants (generally not covered) Travel and accommodation in connection with exhibitions in galleries where the artist has a permanent affiliation Local transport Projects already reviewed by the committee. Costs from previous calendar years.","24.09.2026, 2:00 PM",2026-09-24,2026-09-23 12:37:24.987219+00:00
kunst_dk_denmark_83c3b68dac03,kunst_dk_denmark,https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/visual-arts-international-research-programme,https://portal.slks.dk/Dashboard/application/CreateApplication?poolId=14cde2fa1f14488ea90a43972c3a47d5,Danish Arts Foundation,"International Funding for curatorial research travels for curators, directors of art institutions, art critics, and other art professionals.",Visual arts,funding,Denmark,,"Grants of up to DKK 15,000 per person for travel and accommodation.",,,"International Funding for curatorial research travels for curators, directors of art institutions, art critics, and other art professionals.",Visual arts,funding,,Denmark,,['Visual Arts'],['Grant/Funding'],[],['Denmark'],"[{'category': 'Travel Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': 15000.0, 'currency': 'DKK', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'per person; travel and accommodation'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:00.110738+00:00,,,,,en,Curatorial Research Programme,"Curators, directors of exhibition venues, art critics and art mediators working with contemporary art. Danish art institutions or other Danish art professionals can apply on behalf of one or more foreign curators, provided that the Danish actor undertakes programming and hosting the foreign curator's visit to Denmark. Applicants with Danish CVR/CPR/ NemKonto must apply via the Danish version of this pool The programme is primarily aimed at applicants who already have contacts on the Danish art scene or candidates who wish to develop a project involving specific Danish artists or institutions. Applicants must be able to organize meetings and studio visits on their own.",Curatorial Research Programme,"Curators, directors of exhibition venues, art critics and art mediators working with contemporary art. Danish art institutions or other Danish art professionals can apply on behalf of one or more foreign curators, provided that the Danish actor undertakes programming and hosting the foreign curator's visit to Denmark. Applicants with Danish CVR/CPR/ NemKonto must apply via the Danish version of this pool The programme is primarily aimed at applicants who already have contacts on the Danish art scene or candidates who wish to develop a project involving specific Danish artists or institutions. Applicants must be able to organize meetings and studio visits on their own.","24.09.2026, 2:00 PM",2026-09-24,2026-09-23 12:37:24.990730+00:00
kunst_dk_denmark_823c0bbbc582,kunst_dk_denmark,https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/performing-arts-international-activities,https://portal.slks.dk//TAS_Dashboard/application/CreateApplication?poolId=2f02cef278c24c4b80a20035ff8119a1,Danish Arts Foundation,"International Smaller theatres, performing arts groups, independent performing artists and operators organising or working with performing arts activities can apply for grants of max. DKK 100,000 for international performing arts activities.",Performing arts,grants,Denmark,,"grants of max. DKK 100,000",,,"International Smaller theatres, performing arts groups, independent performing artists and operators organising or working with performing arts activities can apply for grants of max. DKK 100,000 for international performing arts activities.",Performing arts,grants,,Denmark,,['Performing Arts'],['Grant/Funding'],[],['Denmark'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': 100000.0, 'currency': 'DKK', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'max. grant'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:00.110758+00:00,,,,,en,Performing arts: International activities,"Smaller theatres, performing arts groups, independent performing artists and operators organising or working with performing arts activities can apply for grants of max. DKK 100,000 for international performing arts activities.

Who may apply? Smaller theatres, performing arts groups, independent performing artists and operators organising or working with performing arts activities.

Who may not apply? Support cannot be granted for projects, which are carried out exclusively by the large institutional theatres. By large institutional theatres we mean The Royal Danish Theatre, the Danish regional theatres, the Jutland Opera, and the theatres in the Copenhagen theatre association may not apply. You cannot receive funding for the following purposes activities initiated ahead of the deadline educational purposes for individuals",Performing arts: International activities,"Smaller theatres, performing arts groups, independent performing artists and operators organising or working with performing arts activities can apply for grants of max. DKK 100,000 for international performing arts activities.

Who may apply? Smaller theatres, performing arts groups, independent performing artists and operators organising or working with performing arts activities.

Who may not apply? Support cannot be granted for projects, which are carried out exclusively by the large institutional theatres. By large institutional theatres we mean The Royal Danish Theatre, the Danish regional theatres, the Jutland Opera, and the theatres in the Copenhagen theatre association may not apply. You cannot receive funding for the following purposes activities initiated ahead of the deadline educational purposes for individuals","01.10.2026, 2:00 PM",2026-01-10,2026-09-23 12:37:24.994349+00:00
kunst_dk_denmark_091f95df035c,kunst_dk_denmark,https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/nordic-translations,https://portal.slks.dk/Dashboard/application/CreateApplication?poolId=e6330c53cf004a46b91c8f2972825f37,Danish Arts Foundation,"Funding for Nordic publishers to cover fees for translators, translating a work from Danish into another Nordic language.",Litteratur Internationalt Literature International,funding,Denmark,,Funding for Nordic publishers to cover fees for translators,,,"Funding for Nordic publishers to cover fees for translators, translating a work from Danish into another Nordic language.",Litteratur Internationalt Literature International,funding,,Denmark,,['Literature/Writing'],['Grant/Funding'],[],['Denmark'],"[{'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'fees for translators'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:00.110778+00:00,,,,,en,Nordic translations,"Who may apply? Nordic publishers wishing to publish a work translated from Danish into another Nordic language. Non-Nordic publishers: please apply to the fund ‘Literary production and translation’. Applications should be made in the Nordic country in which the work was originally published. For the translation of works from Danish, you should therefore submit your application to the Danish Arts Foundation's Committee for Literary Project Funding. Before submitting the application, the applicant must have acquired the copyrights for the literary work and signed a contract with a translator. Projects may not be finished before the expiry of the application deadline. You can apply for: Fiction for adults, children and young adults General cultural literature and non-fiction Essays Comics and graphic novels You cannot receive funding for: translation of works within the areas of research, education, regional and local history, handbooks, hobby books, self-help books, and catalogues translation of your own works and text revision Furthermore, funding is typically not awarded to Danish publishers for publication of Danish works in translation.",Nordic translations,"Who may apply? Nordic publishers wishing to publish a work translated from Danish into another Nordic language. Non-Nordic publishers: please apply to the fund ‘Literary production and translation’. Applications should be made in the Nordic country in which the work was originally published. For the translation of works from Danish, you should therefore submit your application to the Danish Arts Foundation's Committee for Literary Project Funding. Before submitting the application, the applicant must have acquired the copyrights for the literary work and signed a contract with a translator. Projects may not be finished before the expiry of the application deadline. You can apply for: Fiction for adults, children and young adults General cultural literature and non-fiction Essays Comics and graphic novels You cannot receive funding for: translation of works within the areas of research, education, regional and local history, handbooks, hobby books, self-help books, and catalogues translation of your own works and text revision Furthermore, funding is typically not awarded to Danish publishers for publication of Danish works in translation.","12.02.2027, 2:00 PM",2027-12-02,2026-09-23 12:37:24.998213+00:00
kunst_dk_denmark_be0b1bc26009,kunst_dk_denmark,https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/literary-production-and-translation,https://portal.slks.dk/Dashboard/application/CreateApplication?poolId=6710d33dda9c469aa7c4ad376579223f,Danish Arts Foundation,"Publishing and translation support for literary works (books, e-books, drama, literary podcasts etc.) for adults, children and young adults.",Literature,support,Denmark,,"Publications: DKK 15,000 in contribution towards the total costs of the publication of books and translations up to 100 pages. DKK 30,000 in contribution towards the total costs of the publication of books and translations up to 300 pages. DKK 50,000 in contribution towards the total costs of the publication of books and translations with more than 300 pages. DKK 100,000 in contribution towards the total costs of especially complex and expensive works. Other media: Literary podcasts: DKK 15,000 – at least 90 minutes, DKK 30,000 – at least 180 minutes, DKK 50,000 – at least 300",no fee,,"Publishing and translation support for literary works (books, e-books, drama, literary podcasts etc.) for adults, children and young adults.",Literature,support,,Denmark,,['Literature/Writing'],['Grant/Funding'],[],['Denmark'],"[{'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': 15000.0, 'amount_max': 15000.0, 'currency': 'DKK', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'publications up to 100 pages'}, {'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': 30000.0, 'amount_max': 30000.0, 'currency': 'DKK', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'publications up to 300 pages'}, {'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': 50000.0, 'amount_max': 50000.0, 'currency': 'DKK', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'publications with more than 300 pages'}, {'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': 100000.0, 'amount_max': 100000.0, 'currency': 'DKK', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'especially complex and expensive works'}, {'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': 15000.0, 'amount_max': 15000.0, 'currency': 'DKK', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'literary podcasts at least 90 minutes'}, {'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': 30000.0, 'amount_max': 30000.0, 'currency': 'DKK', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'literary podcasts at least 180 minutes'}, {'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': 50000.0, 'amount_max': 50000.0, 'currency': 'DKK', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'literary podcasts at least 300 minutes'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:00.110782+00:00,False,,,,en,Literary production and translation,"Who may apply? Publishing houses and other publishers of Danish literary works in translation, (organisations etc.) Nordic publishers: please apply to the fund ‘Nordiske oversættelser/Nordic translations’ YOU CAN APPLY FOR GRANTS FOR: Publication of literature in various formats translated from Danish. If you are applying for grants to cover both production and translation costs, you must apply in a single, combined application per work. You can only apply when you have acquired the rights to the work and signed a contract with the translator named in the application. YOU CANNOT APPLY FOR GRANTS FOR: Individuals cannot apply for support for translation. The support must be applied for by the publishing publisher. Translation of Danish titles to other Nordic languages. Nordic publishers may apply to the Fund for Nordic Translations/ puljen Nordiske Oversættelser for funding to cover fees for translators who translate a work from Danish into another Nordic language Publication of works in which the literature belongs to the realm of research, education, regional and local history, handbooks, self-help and lifestyle books, dictionaries, catalogues, or similar literature. The work must not have been published before the application deadline. Publishers based in Denmark that apply must be able to render probable that the translation will reach its target group through partnerships or a professional distribution network.",Literary production and translation,"Who may apply? Publishing houses and other publishers of Danish literary works in translation, (organisations etc.) Nordic publishers: please apply to the fund ‘Nordiske oversættelser/Nordic translations’ YOU CAN APPLY FOR GRANTS FOR: Publication of literature in various formats translated from Danish. If you are applying for grants to cover both production and translation costs, you must apply in a single, combined application per work. You can only apply when you have acquired the rights to the work and signed a contract with the translator named in the application. YOU CANNOT APPLY FOR GRANTS FOR: Individuals cannot apply for support for translation. The support must be applied for by the publishing publisher. Translation of Danish titles to other Nordic languages. Nordic publishers may apply to the Fund for Nordic Translations/ puljen Nordiske Oversættelser for funding to cover fees for translators who translate a work from Danish into another Nordic language Publication of works in which the literature belongs to the realm of research, education, regional and local history, handbooks, self-help and lifestyle books, dictionaries, catalogues, or similar literature. The work must not have been published before the application deadline. Publishers based in Denmark that apply must be able to render probable that the translation will reach its target group through partnerships or a professional distribution network.","12.02.2027, 2:00 PM",2027-12-02,2026-09-23 12:37:25.001907+00:00
kunst_dk_denmark_92d5217dc912,kunst_dk_denmark,https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/sample-translations-from-danish,https://portal.slks.dk/Dashboard/application/CreateApplication?poolId=bf0a14e4c53a42ae856ca862b96a669e,Danish Arts Foundation,"Grants for sample translations from Danish of works for adults, children and young adults.",Litteratur Internationalt International Literature,Grants,Denmark,,"A fixed grant of DKK 8,000 is awarded for a 40-page sample translation when the original work is 100 pages or longer. A fixed grant of DKK 3,000 is awarded for sample translations of illustrated literature or when the original work is fewer than 100 pages.",,,"Grants for sample translations from Danish of works for adults, children and young adults.",Litteratur Internationalt International Literature,Grants,,Denmark,,['Literature/Writing'],['Grant/Funding'],[],['Denmark'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 8000.0, 'amount_max': 8000.0, 'currency': 'DKK', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': '40-page sample translation when original work is 100 pages or longer'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 3000.0, 'amount_max': 3000.0, 'currency': 'DKK', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'sample translations of illustrated literature or when original work is fewer than 100 pages'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:00.111305+00:00,,,,,en,Sample translations from Danish,"Who may apply? Danish and foreign publishers and agencies. Note: In order to ensure the spreading of art support, you may apply for support for a total of four sample translations. YOU CAN APPLY FOR GRANTS FOR: Sample translation of a Danish work into a foreign language. YOU CANNOT APPLY FOR GRANTS FOR: Sample translations of works that the committee assesses belong to the realm of research, education, regional and local history, handbooks, self-help and lifestyle books, dictionaries, catalogues, or similar literature. Sample translations of your own works or text revisions. Projects that were carried out and finished before the expiry of the application deadline.",Sample translations from Danish,"Who may apply? Danish and foreign publishers and agencies. Note: In order to ensure the spreading of art support, you may apply for support for a total of four sample translations. YOU CAN APPLY FOR GRANTS FOR: Sample translation of a Danish work into a foreign language. YOU CANNOT APPLY FOR GRANTS FOR: Sample translations of works that the committee assesses belong to the realm of research, education, regional and local history, handbooks, self-help and lifestyle books, dictionaries, catalogues, or similar literature. Sample translations of your own works or text revisions. Projects that were carried out and finished before the expiry of the application deadline.","12.02.2027, 2:00 PM",2027-12-02,2026-09-23 12:37:25.005467+00:00
kunst_dk_denmark_028cc37c2d3b,kunst_dk_denmark,https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/literary-events-and-projects,https://portal.slks.dk/Dashboard/application/CreateApplication?poolId=78e6b196a2b54016bb4b860d421031db,Danish Arts Foundation,"Support for literary events and projects that focus on Danish literature and authors, as well as mentor support and network support for translators.",Litteratur Internationalt International Literature,Support,Denmark,,"mentor support for translators (a fixed amount of DKK 6,000)",,,"Support for literary events and projects that focus on Danish literature and authors, as well as mentor support and network support for translators.",Litteratur Internationalt International Literature,Support,,Denmark,,['Literature/Writing'],['Grant/Funding'],[],['Denmark'],"[{'category': 'Mentorship/Training', 'amount_min': 6000.0, 'amount_max': 6000.0, 'currency': 'DKK', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'mentor support for translators'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:00.111372+00:00,,,,,en,Literary events and projects,"Organisers of literary events, initiatives and literature presentation projects for children, young adults and adults. The project must be based on Danish literature. Translators and publishers may apply for mentor support for translators, and translators may apply for network support.

The authors, illustrators and translators involved must have published at least one work in Danish. Events with audiences must be available to the public and they must be clearly announced. With regard to applications for mentor support, the translator or publisher may apply for a fixed amount of DKK 6,000 for the course of a concrete translation project. With regard to applications for network support, the committee supports activities in local networks of translators who translate from Danish.",Literary events and projects,"Organisers of literary events, initiatives and literature presentation projects for children, young adults and adults. The project must be based on Danish literature. Translators and publishers may apply for mentor support for translators, and translators may apply for network support.

The authors, illustrators and translators involved must have published at least one work in Danish. Events with audiences must be available to the public and they must be clearly announced. With regard to applications for mentor support, the translator or publisher may apply for a fixed amount of DKK 6,000 for the course of a concrete translation project. With regard to applications for network support, the committee supports activities in local networks of translators who translate from Danish.","12.02.2027, 2:00 PM",2027-12-02,2026-09-23 12:37:25.008677+00:00
kunst_dk_denmark_64e7cbaea368,kunst_dk_denmark,https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/craft-and-design-projects-in-denmark-and-abroad,https://portal.slks.dk/Dashboard/Login/?returnUrl=/Dashboard/,Danish Arts Foundation,Funding for projects for and with Danish craft and design in Denmark and abroad.,Crafts & Design,Funding,Denmark,,,,,Funding for projects for and with Danish craft and design in Denmark and abroad.,Crafts & Design,Funding,,Denmark,,"['Craft', 'Design/Architecture']",['Grant/Funding'],[],['Denmark'],[],,,,,,en,Craft and design projects in Denmark and abroad,"The Committee for Craft and Design Project Funding funds artists, designers, curators, authors, promoters, museums, galleries and others with an interest in developing and promoting craft and design in Denmark and Danish craft and design abroad in the form of projects. You can read more about how the committee defines a project under the ""What is the purpose of the programme"" section of this page. Examples of projects that the committee may fund include: Exhibitions and dissemination projects as well as exhibition series and annual programmes that involve works by contemporary artists and designers in Denmark and/or abroad. Residencies and exchange/work stays Production of works Projects that show aesthetic potential and a thorough understanding of a craft, materials and sensuousness Projects that are centered on concrete design solutions to specific problems or projects that are more immaterial or critical in nature. Presentations and all types of dissemination (verbal, written, visual, digital and printed) of the works of contemporary Danish artists and designers to a relevant audience, this includes travel funding and residencies in connection with specific exhibitions and tasks Funding for establishing a business and international cooperation on the production of new types of Danish craft and design products that contribute to demonstrating the special identity and profile of the craft or design Editorial content production for different media: reviews, articles, dissemination of academic research projects etc. Find out more about how to apply if your project combines different art forms. You cannot receive funding for: Activities completed before the application deadline Courses of study/training courses Projects that the committee have previously supported Capital investments and operating expenses Expenses from previous calendar years. That is, only expenses from either the same or upcoming calendar year can be entered into the budget",Craft and design projects in Denmark and abroad,"The Committee for Craft and Design Project Funding funds artists, designers, curators, authors, promoters, museums, galleries and others with an interest in developing and promoting craft and design in Denmark and Danish craft and design abroad in the form of projects. You can read more about how the committee defines a project under the ""What is the purpose of the programme"" section of this page. Examples of projects that the committee may fund include: Exhibitions and dissemination projects as well as exhibition series and annual programmes that involve works by contemporary artists and designers in Denmark and/or abroad. Residencies and exchange/work stays Production of works Projects that show aesthetic potential and a thorough understanding of a craft, materials and sensuousness Projects that are centered on concrete design solutions to specific problems or projects that are more immaterial or critical in nature. Presentations and all types of dissemination (verbal, written, visual, digital and printed) of the works of contemporary Danish artists and designers to a relevant audience, this includes travel funding and residencies in connection with specific exhibitions and tasks Funding for establishing a business and international cooperation on the production of new types of Danish craft and design products that contribute to demonstrating the special identity and profile of the craft or design Editorial content production for different media: reviews, articles, dissemination of academic research projects etc. Find out more about how to apply if your project combines different art forms. You cannot receive funding for: Activities completed before the application deadline Courses of study/training courses Projects that the committee have previously supported Capital investments and operating expenses Expenses from previous calendar years. That is, only expenses from either the same or upcoming calendar year can be entered into the budget","01.03.2027, 2:00 PM",2027-01-03,2026-09-23 12:37:25.012351+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_1fb6db149626,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/21st-bucharest-international-jazz-competition-2027/,,jmEvents,Open for: instrumentalists and vocalists of all nationalities,jazz,competition,Romania,Bucharest,The total amount of the prizes is 10.000 Euro: cash and concerts engagements. Grand Prize Winner 1.500 Euro Best Band 500 Euro Best Vocalist 500 Euro Best Jam Session 250 Euro 2 – 3 concerts engagements for one or two finalist bands,The registration fee for one application / group is 140 Euro,,Open for: instrumentalists and vocalists of all nationalities,jazz,competition,,Romania,Bucharest,['Music'],['Competition/Prize'],[],['Romania'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 1500.0, 'amount_max': 1500.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'Grand Prize Winner'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 500.0, 'amount_max': 500.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'Best Band'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 500.0, 'amount_max': 500.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'Best Vocalist'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 250.0, 'amount_max': 250.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'Best Jam Session'}, {'category': 'Exhibition/Presentation Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': '2–3 concert engagements for one or two finalist bands'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:04.557020+00:00,True,140.0,140.0,EUR,en,21st Bucharest International Jazz Competition 2027,"Open for: instrumentalists and vocalists of all nationalities NEW! Age limit: up to 45 years old ( born after the 1st of July 1982 ). The leader can be older than 45. Bands may have up to 6 performing musicians and they may include: instrumentalists and vocalists instrumentalists vocalists Individual musicians can apply for the Jam Session section. Registration in the competition will be made based on digital documents: Application form – Annex A ( for band ), Annex B ( for each member ), Annex C audio recordings for the competition – mp3 / mp4 format two different group photos, color, landscape format, min 1MB copy of the bank confirmation for the payment of the registration fee short presentation of the group – max. 10 lines, word document copy of passport |identity card for EU citizens, for each group’s member technical rider All digital documents will be sent using https://www.transfernow.net/ as follows: make a folder and name it as your band copy all digital documents in the folder archive / compress the folder ( .zip ) send the folder by https://www.transfernow.net/ to email office@jmevents.ro and jmevents.ro@gmail.com please mention: “Application – band’s name”",21st Bucharest International Jazz Competition 2027,"Open for: instrumentalists and vocalists of all nationalities NEW! Age limit: up to 45 years old ( born after the 1st of July 1982 ). The leader can be older than 45. Bands may have up to 6 performing musicians and they may include: instrumentalists and vocalists instrumentalists vocalists Individual musicians can apply for the Jam Session section. Registration in the competition will be made based on digital documents: Application form – Annex A ( for band ), Annex B ( for each member ), Annex C audio recordings for the competition – mp3 / mp4 format two different group photos, color, landscape format, min 1MB copy of the bank confirmation for the payment of the registration fee short presentation of the group – max. 10 lines, word document copy of passport |identity card for EU citizens, for each group’s member technical rider All digital documents will be sent using https://www.transfernow.net/ as follows: make a folder and name it as your band copy all digital documents in the folder archive / compress the folder ( .zip ) send the folder by https://www.transfernow.net/ to email office@jmevents.ro and jmevents.ro@gmail.com please mention: “Application – band’s name”",01 Mar 2027,2027-03-01,2026-09-23 12:37:25.015247+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_a923281df709,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/kooperativa-x-fai-mobility-programme-immerse-yourself-in-the-southeastern-european-arts-sector/,https://www.are.na/login?redirectTo=%2Fward-bosmans%2Fflanders-see-hangout%2Finvite%2Fl05x6flkHjoMWA8_8hRjuw,"Flanders Arts Institute, Kooperativa","From June 2026 to September 2027, Flanders Arts Institute will support artists and arts professionals who wish to immerse themselves in the South-Eastern European arts sector . Together with Kooperativa we’re starting this mobility programme, aiming to deepen our understanding of each other’s sector and practices, to build bridges of exchange and solidarity, and to share the gained experiences with our own arts sectors.","visual arts, performing arts, music and sound",mobility programme,Flanders,,The mobility funding covers: travel; accommodation; per diems; a support of up to 300 euros for the host to cover any costs they might incur. The budgets will be calculated according to Erasmus+ formulas.,,,"From June 2026 to September 2027, Flanders Arts Institute will support artists and arts professionals who wish to immerse themselves in the South-Eastern European arts sector . Together with Kooperativa we’re starting this mobility programme, aiming to deepen our understanding of each other’s sector and practices, to build bridges of exchange and solidarity, and to share the gained experiences with our own arts sectors.","visual arts, performing arts, music and sound",mobility programme,,Flanders,,"['Visual Arts', 'Performing Arts', 'Music']",['Other'],[],['Belgium'],"[{'category': 'Travel Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'travel'}, {'category': 'Accommodation/Housing', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'accommodation'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'per diems'}, {'category': 'Other/Unspecified Support', 'amount_min': 300.0, 'amount_max': 300.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'support for the host to cover incidental costs'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:04.557323+00:00,,,,,en,Kooperativa x FAI mobility programme: Immerse yourself in the South-Eastern European arts sector,"This call is for Flemish artists and arts professionals in the fields of visual arts, performing arts, music and sound.",Kooperativa x FAI mobility programme: Immerse yourself in the South-Eastern European arts sector,"This call is for Flemish artists and arts professionals in the fields of visual arts, performing arts, music and sound.",1 March 2027,2027-03-01,2026-09-23 12:37:25.018597+00:00
