kunsten_be_flanders_af582d66dc91,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/mic-music-industry-showcases/,https://www.musicindustrycompass.com/showcases,kunsten.be,"On 3 and 4 September , the MIC Music Industry Showcase spotlights rising talent in front of an exclusive audience of peers and top industry professionals , including record labels, bookers, artist managers, and venue representatives from across the European music scene. The showcases happen during the MIC Music Industry Compass, the European music summit where you learn about the business of music and make sure to navigate your way through the industry.",music,showcase,,,As a showcase artist you receive a free combi pass to attend the summit.,,,"On 3 and 4 September , the MIC Music Industry Showcase spotlights rising talent in front of an exclusive audience of peers and top industry professionals , including record labels, bookers, artist managers, and venue representatives from across the European music scene. The showcases happen during the MIC Music Industry Compass, the European music summit where you learn about the business of music and make sure to navigate your way through the industry.",music,showcase,,,,['Music'],['Exhibition/Showcase'],[],[],"[{'category': 'Fee Waiver', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'free combi pass to attend the summit'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:13.755128+00:00,,,,,en,MIC Music Industry Showcases,"spotlights rising talent in front of an exclusive audience of peers and top industry professionals , including record labels, bookers, artist managers, and venue representatives from across the European music scene.",MIC Music Industry Showcases,"spotlights rising talent in front of an exclusive audience of peers and top industry professionals , including record labels, bookers, artist managers, and venue representatives from across the European music scene.",31 May 2026,2026-05-31,2026-09-23 12:37:25.203046+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_78924c51339e,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/experience-lab/,https://ohme.be/projects/open-call-consciousness-en/,Ohme,"Ohme is launching an open call for artists on the theme of consciousness, in collaboration with EXPERIENCE, an ERC-funded research project at the Université libre de Bruxelles (ULB).",digital visual artists,"Open call, Residency",Belgium,Brussels,"Artist fee: €5,300, corresponding approximately to 20 working days based on CP 304 salary scales (at maximum 10 years of experience). The amount can be invoiced excl. VAT (HTVA) via an independent status (e.g. Smart), or paid as a salary through the Ohme ASBL social secretariat Production budget: up to €2,000 for production costs",,,"Ohme is launching an open call for artists on the theme of consciousness, in collaboration with EXPERIENCE, an ERC-funded research project at the Université libre de Bruxelles (ULB).",digital visual artists,"Open call, Residency",,Belgium,Brussels,"['Digital/New Media Arts', 'Visual Arts']","['Open Call', 'Residency']",[],['Belgium'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 5300.0, 'amount_max': 5300.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'artist fee; approx. 20 working days based on CP 304 salary scales'}, {'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': 2000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'production budget, up to'}, {'category': 'Other/Unspecified Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'can be invoiced excl. VAT via independent status or paid as salary through social secretariat'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:21.537312+00:00,,,,,en,Experience Lab,"This call is for digital visual artists connected to the contemporary art field of the Fédération Wallonie-Bruxelles – that is, artists who live, work, or have a professional practice within the French-speaking art community of Belgium.

The call is open to individual artists or collectives (hereinafter “the artist”).

We are looking for artists with an established practice in data visualisation, information design, or related computational and digital fields, who are curious about – and willing to engage critically with – questions at the intersection of science, knowledge production, and subjective experience. We are not looking for artists who already work on consciousness or neuroscience. Rather, we are interested in practitioners whose existing methods, research sensibilities, and design approaches could be meaningfully mobilised within this scientific context – and who are drawn to the challenge of working with empirical data produced by cutting-edge research on the mind.

The artist should:
Demonstrate an established professional practice in digital art, data visualisation, information design, or a related field
Show experience working with data as creative material – through code, custom tools, or creative use of platforms and languages (e.g. Processing, p5.js, openFrameworks, TouchDesigner, Max/MSP, or equivalent)
Demonstrate a critical engagement with the tools, systems and processes underlying the production, collection and dissemination of information – treating visualisation not as neutral representation but as a site of interpretation, choice and potential critique
Show an interest in questions relating to the mind, perception, cognition, neuroscience or the nature of experience – whether through previous projects, research, or a clearly articulated curiosity
Be willing to engage actively with the EXPERIENCE programme, both theoretically and practically, and to work in genuine interdisciplinary dialogue with the research team",Experience Lab,"This call is for digital visual artists connected to the contemporary art field of the Fédération Wallonie-Bruxelles – that is, artists who live, work, or have a professional practice within the French-speaking art community of Belgium.

The call is open to individual artists or collectives (hereinafter “the artist”).

We are looking for artists with an established practice in data visualisation, information design, or related computational and digital fields, who are curious about – and willing to engage critically with – questions at the intersection of science, knowledge production, and subjective experience. We are not looking for artists who already work on consciousness or neuroscience. Rather, we are interested in practitioners whose existing methods, research sensibilities, and design approaches could be meaningfully mobilised within this scientific context – and who are drawn to the challenge of working with empirical data produced by cutting-edge research on the mind.

The artist should:
Demonstrate an established professional practice in digital art, data visualisation, information design, or a related field
Show experience working with data as creative material – through code, custom tools, or creative use of platforms and languages (e.g. Processing, p5.js, openFrameworks, TouchDesigner, Max/MSP, or equivalent)
Demonstrate a critical engagement with the tools, systems and processes underlying the production, collection and dissemination of information – treating visualisation not as neutral representation but as a site of interpretation, choice and potential critique
Show an interest in questions relating to the mind, perception, cognition, neuroscience or the nature of experience – whether through previous projects, research, or a clearly articulated curiosity
Be willing to engage actively with the EXPERIENCE programme, both theoretically and practically, and to work in genuine interdisciplinary dialogue with the research team",31 May 2026,2026-05-31,2026-09-23 12:37:25.206058+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_fa7c8503285a,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/call-for-proposals-symposium-the-performer-composer-in-the-21st-century/,https://performercomposersymposium.wordpress.com/,Organized by the Co-Creation in Music research cluster,"We are looking for proposals in a variety of formats, including talks, performances, workshops, and other formats that illuminate aspects of current performer-composer identity and practice. We especially welcome reflections emerging from first-hand compositional, performative, and improvisational work.",Performing and composing,Call for proposals,Belgium,Leuven,,,,"We are looking for proposals in a variety of formats, including talks, performances, workshops, and other formats that illuminate aspects of current performer-composer identity and practice. We especially welcome reflections emerging from first-hand compositional, performative, and improvisational work.",Performing and composing,Call for proposals,,Belgium,Leuven,['Music'],['Open Call'],[],['Belgium'],[],,,,,,en,Call for proposals – Symposium: The Performer-Composer in the 21st Century,"We are looking for proposals in a variety of formats, including talks, performances, workshops, and other formats that illuminate aspects of current performer-composer identity and practice. We especially welcome reflections emerging from first-hand compositional, performative, and improvisational work. Proposals should be sent to julie.michael@kuleuven.be, with the following information: Presenter’s name and affiliated institution A description of the proposed topic and format, max. 500 words CV, max 1 page Technical requirements",Call for proposals – Symposium: The Performer-Composer in the 21st Century,"We are looking for proposals in a variety of formats, including talks, performances, workshops, and other formats that illuminate aspects of current performer-composer identity and practice. We especially welcome reflections emerging from first-hand compositional, performative, and improvisational work. Proposals should be sent to julie.michael@kuleuven.be, with the following information: Presenter’s name and affiliated institution A description of the proposed topic and format, max. 500 words CV, max 1 page Technical requirements",31 May 2026,2026-05-31,2026-09-23 12:37:25.208855+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_f21d7f38a567,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-for-artists-capsules/,https://wkf.ms/4dmhXFc,Luxembourg Art Week and artcontemporain.lu asbl,"Luxembourg Art Week and artcontemporain.lu asbl are launching the third edition of Capsules , inviting contemporary artists to submit proposals for ephemeral installations in the heart of the city.",visual and digital arts practices,Open Call,Luxembourg,Luxembourg,selected artists will receive comprehensive support for their participation including an artist fee and/or production contribution of €950 (incl. VAT) along with covered travel expenses and accommodation. The organisers additionally cover: Artwork transport (round trip within Europe) Scenography and technical installation,No application fee is required.,Both emerging and established artists,"Luxembourg Art Week and artcontemporain.lu asbl are launching the third edition of Capsules , inviting contemporary artists to submit proposals for ephemeral installations in the heart of the city.",visual and digital arts practices,Open Call,Both emerging and established artists,Luxembourg,Luxembourg,"['Visual Arts', 'Digital/New Media Arts']",['Open Call'],"['Emerging/Early-Career', 'Established/Professional']",['Luxembourg'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 950.0, 'amount_max': 950.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'artist fee and/or production contribution, incl. VAT'}, {'category': 'Travel Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'covered travel expenses; artwork transport within Europe included'}, {'category': 'Accommodation/Housing', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'accommodation covered'}, {'category': 'Exhibition/Presentation Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'scenography and technical installation covered'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:21.537435+00:00,False,,,,en,Open Call for Artists | Capsules,"Both emerging and established artists with a consistent professional practice, active in professional networks, and with a track record of exhibitions. The call is open to: artists of all nationalities and ages, visual and digital arts practices. No application fee is required. Proposals may include existing works adapted specifically for storefront window installation. Submitted works must be available for transport and installation within Europe. Given their placement in the public realm, proposed works must be suitable for unrestricted viewing.",Open Call for Artists | Capsules,"Both emerging and established artists with a consistent professional practice, active in professional networks, and with a track record of exhibitions. The call is open to: artists of all nationalities and ages, visual and digital arts practices. No application fee is required. Proposals may include existing works adapted specifically for storefront window installation. Submitted works must be available for transport and installation within Europe. Given their placement in the public realm, proposed works must be suitable for unrestricted viewing.",24 May 2026,2026-05-24,2026-09-23 12:37:25.212069+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_c810c7444b72,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-for-leuven-based-black-creatives/,,Black Lens Archive (BLA),"Frames of Us is coming to Leuven! We’re looking for 4 Black creatives (18–26) based in or connected to Leuven who want to document their lives and perspectives through (analog) photography. From May to November, you’ll take part in a creative trajectory where you’ll develop your own visual language, guided by artists and professionals in photography, storytelling, and exhibition-making. The project will culminate in a public exhibition in Leuven, where your work will be shared with a wider audience.",(analog) photography,Open call,Belgium,Leuven,,,18–26,"Frames of Us is coming to Leuven! We’re looking for 4 Black creatives (18–26) based in or connected to Leuven who want to document their lives and perspectives through (analog) photography. From May to November, you’ll take part in a creative trajectory where you’ll develop your own visual language, guided by artists and professionals in photography, storytelling, and exhibition-making. The project will culminate in a public exhibition in Leuven, where your work will be shared with a wider audience.",(analog) photography,Open call,18–26,Belgium,Leuven,['Photography'],['Open Call'],['Any/Open to All'],['Belgium'],[],,,,,,en,Open Call for Leuven-Based Black Creatives,"We’re looking for 4 Black creatives (18–26) based in or connected to Leuven who want to document their lives and perspectives through (analog) photography. No prior experience with photography is required. We’re looking for people with a perspective, a sensitivity, and story to share. You can apply in Dutch, French, or English.",Open Call for Leuven-Based Black Creatives,"We’re looking for 4 Black creatives (18–26) based in or connected to Leuven who want to document their lives and perspectives through (analog) photography. No prior experience with photography is required. We’re looking for people with a perspective, a sensitivity, and story to share. You can apply in Dutch, French, or English.",May 23rd,2027-05-23,2026-09-23 12:37:25.214755+00:00
