kunsten_be_flanders_45954c0f1127,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-for-full-contact-2026/,http://www.scan.cat/,SCAN Tarragona,"Full Contact is a professional meeting space aimed at photographers and visual creators working with photography who wish to present their projects to international experts . It offers a valuable opportunity to receive feedback, expand professional networks, and explore new opportunities within the contemporary photography scene.","photography, visual creators",open call,any European Union country or the United Kingdom,,"A solo exhibition in 2027 as part of the official SCAN programme A fee of €900 (taxes included) for exhibition and communication rights Curatorial advice and support from the SCAN team, according to the festival’s technical and financial resources",,emerging artists,"Full Contact is a professional meeting space aimed at photographers and visual creators working with photography who wish to present their projects to international experts . It offers a valuable opportunity to receive feedback, expand professional networks, and explore new opportunities within the contemporary photography scene.","photography, visual creators",open call,emerging artists,any European Union country or the United Kingdom,,"['Photography', 'Visual Arts']",['Open Call'],['Emerging/Early-Career'],['United Kingdom'],"[{'category': 'Exhibition/Presentation Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'solo exhibition in 2027 as part of the official SCAN programme'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 900.0, 'amount_max': 900.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'fee for exhibition and communication rights, taxes included'}, {'category': 'Mentorship/Training', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'curatorial advice and support from the SCAN team'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:21.537595+00:00,,,,,en,Open call for Full Contact 2026,"Eligibility: Persons of legal age residing in any European Union country or the United Kingdom Project type: The festival aims to promote visual storytelling among emerging artists. Any photographic series that tells a story may be submitted, regardless of subject",Open call for Full Contact 2026,"Eligibility: Persons of legal age residing in any European Union country or the United Kingdom Project type: The festival aims to promote visual storytelling among emerging artists. Any photographic series that tells a story may be submitted, regardless of subject",10 May 2026,2026-05-10,2026-09-23 12:37:25.228003+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_0607d3ccd703,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/e10000-transitional-justice-grant-fellowship/,https://afield.us8.list-manage.com/track/click?u=793163623749ff92bce4091cd&id=8944611f3e&e=787e6c9df5,"AFIELD, Arts of the Working Class, and Framer Framed","Within a context marked by nationalism, climate displacement, and systemic discrimination, AFIELD, Arts of the Working Class, and Framer Framed invite artists, cultural practitioners, and collectives working with communities affected by human rights violations to apply for a €10,000 grant and a six-month fellowship . The Transitional Justice with Artists (TJA) program supports six Europe-based artists or practitioners with initiatives that engage deeply with truth, memory, repair, and accountability, to imagine justice beyond legal frameworks.",artists and cultural practitioners,grant and a six-month fellowship,EU Member State or Creative Europe associated country,Amsterdam,"€10,000 per fellow (€9,000 unrestricted funding + €1,000 for travel).",,,"Within a context marked by nationalism, climate displacement, and systemic discrimination, AFIELD, Arts of the Working Class, and Framer Framed invite artists, cultural practitioners, and collectives working with communities affected by human rights violations to apply for a €10,000 grant and a six-month fellowship . The Transitional Justice with Artists (TJA) program supports six Europe-based artists or practitioners with initiatives that engage deeply with truth, memory, repair, and accountability, to imagine justice beyond legal frameworks.",artists and cultural practitioners,grant and a six-month fellowship,,EU Member State or Creative Europe associated country,Amsterdam,['Multidisciplinary'],"['Grant/Funding', 'Fellowship']",[],"['Europe (unspecified)', 'International/Global']","[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 10000.0, 'amount_max': 10000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'per fellow; €9,000 unrestricted funding + €1,000 for travel'}, {'category': 'Travel Support', 'amount_min': 1000.0, 'amount_max': 1000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'included in per-fellow amount'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:21.537624+00:00,,,,,en,"€10,000 Transitional Justice Grant & Fellowship","Applicants must be: Legal residents (including refugees/asylum seekers) in an EU Member State or Creative Europe associated country . Part of an initiative operationally active for at least two years . Using artistic methodologies as the central component of their work. Available for all fellowship components , including the residency and online thematic meetings.","€10,000 Transitional Justice Grant & Fellowship","Applicants must be: Legal residents (including refugees/asylum seekers) in an EU Member State or Creative Europe associated country . Part of an initiative operationally active for at least two years . Using artistic methodologies as the central component of their work. Available for all fellowship components , including the residency and online thematic meetings.",02 May 2026,2026-05-02,2026-09-23 12:37:25.231021+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_bf616e30e784,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/2026-visureal%c2%b7international-image-art-festival-viiaf-call-for-artists-and-art-organizations-worldwide/,https://viiaf.com/call-for-submissions/,VISUREAL·International Image Art Festival (VIIAF),The 2026 VISUREAL·International Image Art Festival (VIIAF) invites submissions from artists and art organizations worldwide.,image-based art,Festival,China,Chengdu,,,,The 2026 VISUREAL·International Image Art Festival (VIIAF) invites submissions from artists and art organizations worldwide.,image-based art,Festival,,China,Chengdu,['Visual Arts'],['Other'],[],['China'],[],,,,,,en,2026 VISUREAL·International Image Art Festival (VIIAF): Call for Artists and Art Organizations Worldwide,submissions from artists and art organizations worldwide,2026 VISUREAL·International Image Art Festival (VIIAF): Call for Artists and Art Organizations Worldwide,submissions from artists and art organizations worldwide,01 May 2026,2026-05-01,2026-09-23 12:37:25.233634+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_e9cea19ce978,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/call-for-individual-mobility-2025-2026/,https://culture.ec.europa.eu/culture-moves-europe/call-for-individual-mobility-2025-2026,Culture Moves Europe,The call for individual mobility allows applications from individuals and groups of up to 5 people.,"architecture, cultural heritage, design and fashion design, literature, music, performing arts, and visual arts",Open call,,,"Daily allowance 85€ per day of project implementation. Travel allowance travel distance under 5 000 km -> 400€ travel distance from 5 000 km -> 800€ The travel distance is calculated automatically in the application form, based on a one-way straight line. The grant offers additional funding, if applicable: Top-ups Green mobility top-up: 400€ Overseas countries and territories / Outermost regions top-up: 175€ Family top-up: 200€ per child Visa top-up: 120€ Accessibility support 30€ per day of project implementation Either the actual cost or a fixed allowance for personal assistance or sign language interpretation, depending on the assistant’s professional status",,,The call for individual mobility allows applications from individuals and groups of up to 5 people.,"architecture, cultural heritage, design and fashion design, literature, music, performing arts, and visual arts",Open call,,,,"['Design/Architecture', 'Cultural Heritage', 'Literature/Writing', 'Music', 'Performing Arts', 'Visual Arts']",['Open Call'],[],[],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 85.0, 'amount_max': 85.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'per day', 'note': 'daily allowance for project implementation'}, {'category': 'Travel Support', 'amount_min': 400.0, 'amount_max': 400.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'travel distance under 5,000 km'}, {'category': 'Travel Support', 'amount_min': 800.0, 'amount_max': 800.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'travel distance from 5,000 km'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 400.0, 'amount_max': 400.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'green mobility top-up'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 175.0, 'amount_max': 175.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'overseas countries and territories / outermost regions top-up'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 200.0, 'amount_max': 200.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'family top-up per child'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 120.0, 'amount_max': 120.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'visa top-up'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 30.0, 'amount_max': 30.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'per day', 'note': 'accessibility support; fixed allowance for personal assistance or sign language interpretation may alternatively cover actual cost depending on assistant status'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:21.537676+00:00,,,,,en,Call for individual mobility 2025-2026,"Artists and cultural professionals, who are: legally residing in one of the Creative Europe countries, including the overseas countries and territories and outermost regions 18 years of age or older active in one of the following sectors: architecture, cultural heritage, design and fashion design, literature, music, performing arts, and visual arts; No specific level of experience is required The call for individual mobility allows applications from individuals and groups of up to 5 people.",Call for individual mobility 2025-2026,"Artists and cultural professionals, who are: legally residing in one of the Creative Europe countries, including the overseas countries and territories and outermost regions 18 years of age or older active in one of the following sectors: architecture, cultural heritage, design and fashion design, literature, music, performing arts, and visual arts; No specific level of experience is required The call for individual mobility allows applications from individuals and groups of up to 5 people.",30 Apr 2026,2026-04-30,2026-09-23 12:37:25.236940+00:00
