le connection to Czech culture. Residents may come from a wide range of creative fields, including visual arts, design, research, literature, performance, music, technology, or other interdisciplinary practices.",30 Apr 2026,2026-04-30,2026-09-23 12:37:25.240403+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_b2bef0511012,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-for-residencies/,https://www.imal.org/en/events/appel-a-residences-ipo-2026-extra,iMAL,"iMAL Project Office is our yearly open call for residencies, aimed at artists based in Belgium. We announced our first three iPO 2026 calls last October. Now we can finally reveal the fourth, dedicated to a two-month co-creation residency in collaboration with Antre Peaux (Bourges, FR), and taking place in the framework of EXTRA RESIDENCIES.","visual arts, digital art and experimental video games",residency,Belgium,Brussels,,,emerging artists,"iMAL Project Office is our yearly open call for residencies, aimed at artists based in Belgium. We announced our first three iPO 2026 calls last October. Now we can finally reveal the fourth, dedicated to a two-month co-creation residency in collaboration with Antre Peaux (Bourges, FR), and taking place in the framework of EXTRA RESIDENCIES.","visual arts, digital art and experimental video games",residency,emerging artists,Belgium,Brussels,"['Visual Arts', 'Digital/New Media Arts']",['Residency'],['Emerging/Early-Career'],['Belgium'],[],,,,,,en,Open call for residencies,"The call is open to emerging artists engaged in a professional practice. An “emerging artist” is understood as any artist active for a few years but still in the process of establishing their career, particularly regarding their involvement with various artistic and cultural institutions. Their practice remains precarious and relies on institutional support or partnerships for the production of their works. Candidates must reside in France or Belgium.

Option 1: Duos to be formed
• Artists apply individually to the call without having a predefined partner. Applications will be pre-selected to verify the eligibility of candidates, then shared via Google Drive with all candidates on May 4.
• This stage will allow artists to review applications and connect with other candidates to explore the possibility of collaborating on a joint project. Candidates will have from May 4 to May 22 to engage in these exchanges.
• The pairs formed will be invited to complete a second questionnaire by May 22, with the name of their partner and a letter of intent regarding their co-creation project.

Option 2: Existing duos
• It is possible to apply directly with another artist for a co-creation project. The only prerequisite is that one artist must reside in France and the other in Belgium. Both artists are invited to respond individually to the call for applications, specifying that they are working on a joint project and providing the name of the artist they’re partnering with.
• Please note: Existing duos should only answer the first application form, which closes on April 24. They must therefore submit their letter of intent detailing their joint project using this form. Applications will be pre-selected to verify the eligibility of candidates.",Open call for residencies,"The call is open to emerging artists engaged in a professional practice. An “emerging artist” is understood as any artist active for a few years but still in the process of establishing their career, particularly regarding their involvement with various artistic and cultural institutions. Their practice remains precarious and relies on institutional support or partnerships for the production of their works. Candidates must reside in France or Belgium.

Option 1: Duos to be formed
• Artists apply individually to the call without having a predefined partner. Applications will be pre-selected to verify the eligibility of candidates, then shared via Google Drive with all candidates on May 4.
• This stage will allow artists to review applications and connect with other candidates to explore the possibility of collaborating on a joint project. Candidates will have from May 4 to May 22 to engage in these exchanges.
• The pairs formed will be invited to complete a second questionnaire by May 22, with the name of their partner and a letter of intent regarding their co-creation project.

Option 2: Existing duos
• It is possible to apply directly with another artist for a co-creation project. The only prerequisite is that one artist must reside in France and the other in Belgium. Both artists are invited to respond individually to the call for applications, specifying that they are working on a joint project and providing the name of the artist they’re partnering with.
• Please note: Existing duos should only answer the first application form, which closes on April 24. They must therefore submit their letter of intent detailing their joint project using this form. Applications will be pre-selected to verify the eligibility of candidates.",24 Apr 2026,2026-04-24,2026-09-23 12:37:25.243981+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_a97a4eca3212,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-international-fikva-award-for-painters-2026/,https://fikva.art/submission-form/,FiKVA Foundation,"The FiKVA Foundation proudly presents the 4th International FiKVA Award for Representational & Figurative Painters – a remarkable opportunity for artists worldwide to gain international recognition, share their talent globally, and earn substantial financial rewards. Best of all, the entire process is online – no need to ship your work or part with it!",painters / representational & figurative painting,award,,,"First Prize: €3500 cash prize + Art supplies package, courtesy of M. Graham (12 color paints, valued at €300) + Digital and social media marketing, valued at €300 + Certificate of Achievement + Participation in the online group exhibition of finalists + Published interview with the FiKVA Foundation + Permanent display of the submitted artwork on the FiKVA website + 6-month online gallery representation for a selected artwork; Second Prize: €1500 cash prize + Certificate of Achievement + Participation in the online group exhibition of finalists + Published interview with the FiKVA Foundation + Permanent display of the submitted artwork on the FiKVA website + 6-month online gallery representation for a selected artwork + Digital and social media marketing, valued at €300; Third Prize: €500 cash prize + Certificate of Achievement + Participation in the online group exhibition of finalists + Published interview with the FiKVA Foundation + Permanent display of the submitted artwork on the FiKVA website + 6-month online gallery representation for a selected artwork + Digital and social media marketing, valued at €300; Purchase Prize (only awarded if a work fits the objectives and possibilities of the FiKVa-collection): Acquisition of one selected artwork for the FiKVA Collection + Certificate of Achievement + Permanent display of the purchased artwork on the FiKVA website + Digital and social media marketing, valued at €300; Honorable Mention (3 will be awarded): Certificate of Achievement + Participation in the online group exhibition of the finalists + Permanent place on the FiKVA website + Digital and social media marketing, valued at €300; Top 35: Participation in the online group exhibition of the finalists + Permanent display on the FiKVA website + Digital and social media marketing, valued at €200; Gallery Representation Prize: Up to 10 outstanding artworks from the Top 100 will be handpicked for a 6-month gallery representation with the FiKVA Online Gallery. This exclusive opportunity is by invitation only, with no obligation to the artist.",Participation in the FiKVA Award with just one work: €36,,"The FiKVA Foundation proudly presents the 4th International FiKVA Award for Representational & Figurative Painters – a remarkable opportunity for artists worldwide to gain international recognition, share their talent globally, and earn substantial financial rewards. Best of all, the entire process is online – no need to ship your work or part with it!",painters / representational & figurative painting,award,,,,['Visual Arts'],['Competition/Prize'],[],[],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 3500.0, 'amount_max': 3500.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'cash prize'}, {'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': 300.0, 'amount_max': 300.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'art supplies package (12 color paints)'}, {'category': 'Exhibition/Presentation Support', 'amount_min': 300.0, 'amount_max': 300.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'digital and social media marketing'}, {'category': 'Exhibition/Presentation Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'certificate of achievement'}, {'category': 'Exhibition/Presentation Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'participation in the online group exhibition of finalists'}, {'category': 'Exhibition/Presentation Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'published interview with the FiKVA Foundation'}, {'category': 'Exhibition/Presentation Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'permanent display of the submitted artwork on the FiKVA website'}, {'category': 'Exhibition/Presentation Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': '6-month online gallery representation for a selected artwork'}]",2026-09-24 08:59:26.092757+00:00,True,36.0,36.0,EUR,en,OPEN CALL – International FIKVA Award for painters 2026,"The FiKVA Award is open to all artists 18 years of age or older.

ARTIST ELIGIBILITY
The FiKVA Award is open to all painters aged 18 and older, from anywhere in the world.

ARTWORK ELIGIBILITY
The work must be the artist’s original creation, produced solely by the artist, with copyrights exclusively owned by the artist. The work may be signed and may have participated in previous competitions. The work may be sold, provided the copyright of its image remains solely with the artist. Works must have been produced between 2024 and 2026. Works must be available for inclusion in an online exhibition. Works do not need to be available for sale.

ACCEPTED MEDIA
Oil, water-soluble oil paint, acrylic paint, watercolor, ink, gouache, tempera, and all traditional wet mediums on any support – canvas, board, paper, wood, panel, wall, aluminium, glass, etc. All works must be handmade; digital or mechanical works will not be considered.

SUBJECT MATTER & SIZE
No restrictions – submit what you consider your best work from the last two years.

HOW TO PARTICIPATE?
Registration is only possible via the website: www.fikva.art",OPEN CALL – International FIKVA Award for painters 2026,"The FiKVA Award is open to all artists 18 years of age or older.

ARTIST ELIGIBILITY
The FiKVA Award is open to all painters aged 18 and older, from anywhere in the world.

ARTWORK ELIGIBILITY
The work must be the artist’s original creation, produced solely by the artist, with copyrights exclusively owned by the artist. The work may be signed and may have participated in previous competitions. The work may be sold, provided the copyright of its image remains solely with the artist. Works must have been produced between 2024 and 2026. Works must be available for inclusion in an online exhibition. Works do not need to be available for sale.

ACCEPTED MEDIA
Oil, water-soluble oil paint, acrylic paint, watercolor, ink, gouache, tempera, and all traditional wet mediums on any support – canvas, board, paper, wood, panel, wall, aluminium, glass, etc. All works must be handmade; digital or mechanical works will not be considered.

SUBJECT MATTER & SIZE
No restrictions – submit what you consider your best work from the last two years.

HOW TO PARTICIPATE?
Registration is only possible via the website: www.fikva.art",22 Apr 2026,2026-04-22,2026-09-23 12:37:25.247182+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_5d9b2594f95d,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/fellowship-programma-call-2026/,https://framaforms.org/imal-fellowship-programme-2026-1770642755,"iMAL, Cloud Seven","In a cultural landscape seeking new connections, the Fellowship Programme proposes a renewed alliance between artists and those who support the emergence of their work. A new cultural model based on an expanded mecenat: more open, more engaged, and more attentive to the shifts in the creative world.",contemporary art,production residency,Belgium,Brussels,"The artist will receive accommodation, a workspace, and a budget of €8,000 taxes included (€4,000 in fees and €4,000 for production).",,professional artists,"In a cultural landscape seeking new connections, the Fellowship Programme proposes a renewed alliance between artists and those who support the emergence of their work. A new cultural model based on an expanded mecenat: more open, more engaged, and more attentive to the shifts in the creative world.",contemporary art,production residency,professional artists,Belgium,Brussels,['Visual Arts'],['Residency'],['Established/Professional'],['Belgium'],"[{'category': 'Accommodation/Housing', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'accommodation provided'}, {'category': 'Other/Unspecified Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'workspace provided'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 8000.0, 'amount_max': 8000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'taxes included; €4,000 fees + €4,000 production'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:21.539430+00:00,,,,,en,Fellowship programme: call 2026,"This programme is specifically designed for professional artists who wish to shift or deepen their practice through technology. We are looking for candidates who: Have a solid background in contemporary art but limited experience with digital tools. Artists that while rooted in contemporary art, demonstrate an initial exploration of technological tools and show a strong interest in deepening this approach through a committed project requiring curatorial and technical support within iMAL. View this residency as a learning opportunity rather than a standard production slot. Are seeking curatorial mentorship and technical guidance to explore new territories. Note: Artists with extensive experience in digital arts may be considered overqualified, as the programme’s primary goal is to provide a space for growth, experimentation, and the acquisition of new technical and critical skills.",Fellowship programme: call 2026,"This programme is specifically designed for professional artists who wish to shift or deepen their practice through technology. We are looking for candidates who: Have a solid background in contemporary art but limited experience with digital tools. Artists that while rooted in contemporary art, demonstrate an initial exploration of technological tools and show a strong interest in deepening this approach through a committed project requiring curatorial and technical support within iMAL. View this residency as a learning opportunity rather than a standard production slot. Are seeking curatorial mentorship and technical guidance to explore new territories. Note: Artists with extensive experience in digital arts may be considered overqualified, as the programme’s primary goal is to provide a space for growth, experimentation, and the acquisition of new technical and critical skills.","Application Deadline: April 19, 2026",2026-04-19,2026-09-23 12:37:25.250072+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_2fa2a89c4a72,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-raive-ai-summer-school/,https://raive.school/,The Algorithmic Gaze and CREATIE,"The Algorithmic Gaze and CREATIE, both Antwerp-based research groups, will join forces again to organise a summerschool for everyone who’s interested in the topic of performative AI and interdisciplinary creation. After two great editions, RAIVE will take place again between the 31st of August and the 6th of September in the Royal Conservatoire of Antwerp. RAIVE is a laboratory for young artists from diverse disciplines such as dance, music, technology, and visual arts. Artists come together to redefine the boundaries of their craft through the lens of interdisciplinary collaboration. Participants learn to create their own AI systems from basic principles, curating their own datasets through a very “hands-on” artistic approach. As participants, you will be divided into groups in which you will work for one week. During this process you both learn from each other and benefit from the insights of three coaches, skilled in different areas within the arts. The culmination of this week-long journey is a public presentation held in De Gele Zaal of the Royal Conservatoire of Antwerp.","dance, music, technology, and visual arts",summer school,Belgium,Antwerp,"The total price of the summer school is € 300,00 . Included in this price are: lunch, workshops, coachings, working space and technical equipment.","The total price of the summer school is € 300,00 .",young/starting artist,"The Algorithmic Gaze and CREATIE, both Antwerp-based research groups, will join forces again to organise a summerschool for everyone who’s interested in the topic of performative AI and interdisciplinary creation. After two great editions, RAIVE will take place again between the 31st of August and the 6th of September in the Royal Conservatoire of Antwerp. RAIVE is a laboratory for young artists from diverse disciplines such as dance, music, technology, and visual arts. Artists come together to redefine the boundaries of their craft through the lens of interdisciplinary collaboration. Participants learn to create their own AI systems from basic principles, curating their own datasets through a very “hands-on” artistic approach. As participants, you will be divided into groups in which you will work for one week. During this process you both learn from each other and benefit from the insights of three coaches, skilled in different areas within the arts. The culmination of this week-long journey is a public presentation held in De Gele Zaal of the Royal Conservatoire of Antwerp.","dance, music, technology, and visual arts",summer school,young/starting artist,Belgium,Antwerp,"['Dance', 'Music', 'Digital/New Media Arts', 'Visual Arts']",['Workshop/Training'],['Emerging/Early-Career'],['Belgium'],[],2026-09-24 08:57:21.539463+00:00,True,300.0,300.0,EUR,en,Open call – RAIVE AI Summer School,"The open call is open to anyone who considers themselves a young/starting artist, regardless of age. Prior knowledge or experience with digital media isn’t necessary, but of course welcome! We can host a maximum of 12 participants. If the number of applications exceeds this amount we will make a selection.",Open call – RAIVE AI Summer School,"The open call is open to anyone who considers themselves a young/starting artist, regardless of age. Prior knowledge or experience with digital media isn’t necessary, but of course welcome! We can host a maximum of 12 participants. If the number of applications exceeds this amount we will make a selection.",19 Apr 2026,2026-04-19,2026-09-23 12:37:25.253840+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_28639c301034,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/call-portraits-miroir-miroir-biennale-de-limage-possible-bip2026/,https://bip-liege.org/en/exhibition/call-for-portraits/,"Biennale de l'Image Possible, BIP2026","The 14th edition of the Biennale de l’Image Possible, BIP2026, will take place in Liège from 17 October to 13 December 2026. Entitled MIROIR MIROIR, it will bring together several exhibitions at a single venue. One will showcase a composite collection of portraits, created from a variety of figures (human and non-human beings) and using any visual medium (painting, photography, video, drawing, etc.). The aim is to create a heterogeneous collection of fragments, free associations arising from a multitude of disparate elements. The selected portraits will be brought together and staged in a vast, free-flowing space. We are soliciting these portraits from you, visual artists. Whether it is a single image or part of a series, large or small, already produced or yet to be produced, painted, drawn or printed, we will consider all your proposals. Self-portraits are permitted, as are group portraits. We are keen to embrace the unique ways in which artists, from all backgrounds, nationalities and generations, have seen, observed and depicted those living individuals who have returned their gaze or granted their presence as a model, an ideal or a subject.",visual artists,call,Belgium,Liège,,,,"The 14th edition of the Biennale de l’Image Possible, BIP2026, will take place in Liège from 17 October to 13 December 2026. Entitled MIROIR MIROIR, it will bring together several exhibitions at a single venue. One will showcase a composite collection of portraits, created from a variety of figures (human and non-human beings) and using any visual medium (painting, photography, video, drawing, etc.). The aim is to create a heterogeneous collection of fragments, free associations arising from a multitude of disparate elements. The selected portraits will be brought together and staged in a vast, free-flowing space. We are soliciting these portraits from you, visual artists. Whether it is a single image or part of a series, large or small, already produced or yet to be produced, painted, drawn or printed, we will consider all your proposals. Self-portraits are permitted, as are group portraits. We are keen to embrace the unique ways in which artists, from all backgrounds, nationalities and generations, have seen, observed and depicted those living individuals who have returned their gaze or granted their presence as a model, an ideal or a subject.",visual artists,call,,Belgium,Liège,['Visual Arts'],['Open Call'],[],['Belgium'],[],,,,,,en,CALL – PORTRAITS – MIROIR MIROIR – Biennale de l’Image Possible – BIP2026,"We are soliciting these portraits from you, visual artists. Whether it is a single image or part of a series, large or small, already produced or yet to be produced, painted, drawn or printed, we will consider all your proposals. Self-portraits are permitted, as are group portraits. We are keen to embrace the unique ways in which artists, from all backgrounds, nationalities and generations, have seen, observed and depicted those living individuals who have returned their gaze or granted their presence as a model, an ideal or a subject.",CALL – PORTRAITS – MIROIR MIROIR – Biennale de l’Image Possible – BIP2026,"We are soliciting these portraits from you, visual artists. Whether it is a single image or part of a series, large or small, already produced or yet to be produced, painted, drawn or printed, we will consider all your proposals. Self-portraits are permitted, as are group portraits. We are keen to embrace the unique ways in which artists, from all backgrounds, nationalities and generations, have seen, observed and depicted those living individuals who have returned their gaze or granted their presence as a model, an ideal or a subject.",19 Apr 2026,2026-04-19,2026-09-23 12:37:25.256844+00:00
