kunsten_be_flanders_0d6be3a34e4e,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-festival-performance-pragicomedionale-2026/,https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeCbZyBypOKxyCFua0yqgFauoF-ilnVKoaBapphrQmOrUjmKQ/viewform,Pragovka Gallery,"Pragovka Gallery announces an open call for participation in the second edition of the Pragicomedionale Performance Festival, which will take place on Saturday, 12 September 2026 at the Pragovka complex.",performance art,open call,Czech and international,Pragovka complex,coverage of travel and accommodation costs where necessary festival PR and production photo documentation printing of posters and accompanying printed materials graphic design of printed materials artist fees (to be specified according to available funding) props and installation materials (please include an estimated budget in the application form),,,"Pragovka Gallery announces an open call for participation in the second edition of the Pragicomedionale Performance Festival, which will take place on Saturday, 12 September 2026 at the Pragovka complex.",performance art,open call,,Czech and international,Pragovka complex,['Performing Arts'],['Open Call'],[],"['Czech Republic', 'International/Global']","[{'category': 'Travel Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'travel costs covered where necessary'}, {'category': 'Accommodation/Housing', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'accommodation costs covered where necessary'}, {'category': 'Other/Unspecified Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'festival PR, production photo documentation, printing of posters and accompanying printed materials, graphic design of printed materials'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'artist fees to be specified according to available funding'}, {'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'props and installation materials; estimated budget requested in application'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:21.539467+00:00,,,,,en,Open Call Festival Performance Pragicomedionale 2026,The Open Call is open to Czech and international artists. There are no restrictions placed on performers. Applicants may submit any number of performances. The application must include two mandatory attachments: detailed project description the artist’s portfolio and CV / documentation of previous performances Please remember to label all files with the applicant’s name. The size of each file must not exceed 10 MB. Applications that do not meet the above requirements will not be included in the selection process. Files must be submitted exclusively via this form.,Open Call Festival Performance Pragicomedionale 2026,The Open Call is open to Czech and international artists. There are no restrictions placed on performers. Applicants may submit any number of performances. The application must include two mandatory attachments: detailed project description the artist’s portfolio and CV / documentation of previous performances Please remember to label all files with the applicant’s name. The size of each file must not exceed 10 MB. Applications that do not meet the above requirements will not be included in the selection process. Files must be submitted exclusively via this form.,6 April 2026 (23:59),2026-04-06,2026-09-23 12:37:25.264049+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_a851810c4e3c,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-hotel-carrousel/,https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfrOFvLHrIWDp9VWKvSAG0LxmQb5sEQPvi44Xm-E5v8jqgelg/viewform?pli=1,Hotel Carrousel,"Hotel Carrousel is a nomadic exhibition platform dedicated to video and media art, founded in 2024 by artist Lupe Arens.",video and media art,open call,Belgium,Brussels,"Selected artists, duos or collectives will receive a €200 participation fee. Potential production costs are to be discussed upon selection.",,young and emerging artists,"Hotel Carrousel is a nomadic exhibition platform dedicated to video and media art, founded in 2024 by artist Lupe Arens.",video and media art,open call,young and emerging artists,Belgium,Brussels,"['Film/Video', 'Digital/New Media Arts']",['Open Call'],['Emerging/Early-Career'],['Belgium'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 200.0, 'amount_max': 200.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'participation fee'}, {'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'potential production costs to be discussed upon selection'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:21.539472+00:00,,,,,en,Open Call – Hotel Carrousel,"Artists, duos and collectives under 35 years old and based in Belgium can apply.",Open Call – Hotel Carrousel,"Artists, duos and collectives under 35 years old and based in Belgium can apply.","March 29, 2026 23:59",2026-03-29,2026-09-23 12:37:25.267742+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_f8fe9857ed58,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/east-call-curatorial-residency/,https://forms.gle/iK4qbDuEgXQzc9Fg9,East Topics,"East Call Curatorial Residency offers a unique opportunity for emerging curators to gain a comprehensive insight in the Hungarian and Slovenian contemporary art scene by examining its characteristics and understanding them in a broader, regional context. East Call is an intensive 2-week program that focuses on the status and practice of artists, contemporary curatorial conditions, institutional situations and the understanding of issues affecting contemporary art, with a focus on the roles and responsibilities of curators as mediators between audiences and artists, and researchers as theoretical transmitters of knowledge, interpretation and contextualization. East Call aims to foster dialogue on issues surrounding curation and to interrogate what constitutes “the curatorial” in the Central Eastern European region. The East Call program focuses on open, horizontal and conversation-based transfers of knowledge and experience.",contemporary art,curatorial residency,Hungary,Budapest,"The fee includes the use of office facilities, participation in workshops, guest lectures, entry fees of museums and special events, the use of public transport in Budapest, inland transport for provincial venues and regional transport for Bratislava.",Participation fee: 1000 EUROS,emerging curators and curators-to-be still involved in their studies,"East Call Curatorial Residency offers a unique opportunity for emerging curators to gain a comprehensive insight in the Hungarian and Slovenian contemporary art scene by examining its characteristics and understanding them in a broader, regional context. East Call is an intensive 2-week program that focuses on the status and practice of artists, contemporary curatorial conditions, institutional situations and the understanding of issues affecting contemporary art, with a focus on the roles and responsibilities of curators as mediators between audiences and artists, and researchers as theoretical transmitters of knowledge, interpretation and contextualization. East Call aims to foster dialogue on issues surrounding curation and to interrogate what constitutes “the curatorial” in the Central Eastern European region. The East Call program focuses on open, horizontal and conversation-based transfers of knowledge and experience.",contemporary art,curatorial residency,emerging curators and curators-to-be still involved in their studies,Hungary,Budapest,['Visual Arts'],['Residency'],['Emerging/Early-Career'],['Hungary'],"[{'category': 'Other/Unspecified Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'use of office facilities; participation in workshops and guest lectures; entry fees of museums and special events; public transport in Budapest; inland transport for provincial venues; regional transport for Bratislava'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:21.539496+00:00,True,1000.0,1000.0,EUR,en,East Call Curatorial Residency,The program is designed for emerging curators and curators-to-be still involved in their studies who expect to work in the field of contemporary art.,East Call Curatorial Residency,The program is designed for emerging curators and curators-to-be still involved in their studies who expect to work in the field of contemporary art.,27 March 2026,2026-03-27,2026-09-23 12:37:25.270810+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_780119e0d51f,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/high-fest-international-performing-arts-festival-open-call-2/,https://highfest.am/apply/,HIGH FEST,"Register for the 24th edition of HIGH FEST International Performing Arts Festival! HIGH FEST is delighted to announce the opening of registrations for the 24th edition of the HIGH FEST International Performing Arts Festival, which will take place from 1 to 8 October 2026 in Yerevan, Armenia.",Performing Arts,Festival,Armenia,Yerevan,,,,"Register for the 24th edition of HIGH FEST International Performing Arts Festival! HIGH FEST is delighted to announce the opening of registrations for the 24th edition of the HIGH FEST International Performing Arts Festival, which will take place from 1 to 8 October 2026 in Yerevan, Armenia.",Performing Arts,Festival,,Armenia,Yerevan,['Performing Arts'],['Other'],[],['Armenia'],[],,,,,,en,HIGH FEST International Performing Arts Festival – Open Call,Fill in the attached registration form. Send it to: administration@highfest.am,HIGH FEST International Performing Arts Festival – Open Call,Fill in the attached registration form. Send it to: administration@highfest.am,15 Mar 2026,2026-03-15,2026-09-23 12:37:25.274004+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_2c5ed7b40a1d,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/european-media-art-platform-residency-programme-2026/,,European Media Art Platform (EMAP),"European Media Art Platform (EMAP) returns in 2026 with a residency programme for artists and collectives in 15 countries. EMAP invites artists, artist duos, collectives, and artistic collaborations working in digital, media, robotic, and bio art to apply for a two-month production residency in 2026.","digital, media, robotic, and bio art",residency programme,"Austria, France, Slovakia, Portugal, Belgium, The Netherlands, Slovenia, Croatia, Spain, Italy, Cyprus, Greece, Latvia, Germany, Poland","Linz, Marseille, Košice, Braga, Brussels, Utrecht, Ljubljana, Zagreb, Gijón, Milan, Limassol, Athens, Riga, Halle (Saale), Wrocław","4,000 EUR grant
