Access to technical facilities and/or media labs",,PhD candidates and emerging artists of any age and academic background may apply.,"European Media Art Platform (EMAP) returns in 2026 with a residency programme for artists and collectives in 15 countries. EMAP invites artists, artist duos, collectives, and artistic collaborations working in digital, media, robotic, and bio art to apply for a two-month production residency in 2026.","digital, media, robotic, and bio art",residency programme,PhD candidates and emerging artists of any age and academic background may apply.,"Austria, France, Slovakia, Portugal, Belgium, The Netherlands, Slovenia, Croatia, Spain, Italy, Cyprus, Greece, Latvia, Germany, Poland","Linz, Marseille, Košice, Braga, Brussels, Utrecht, Ljubljana, Zagreb, Gijón, Milan, Limassol, Athens, Riga, Halle (Saale), Wrocław","['Digital/New Media Arts', 'Visual Arts']",['Residency'],['Emerging/Early-Career'],"['Austria', 'France', 'Slovakia', 'Portugal', 'Belgium', 'Netherlands', 'Slovenia', 'Croatia', 'Spain', 'Italy', 'Cyprus', 'Greece', 'Latvia', 'Germany', 'Poland']","[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 4000.0, 'amount_max': 4000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': None}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 2000.0, 'amount_max': 2000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'for collaborating artist(s)'}, {'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': 4000.0, 'amount_max': 4000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'project budget'}, {'category': 'Accommodation/Housing', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'provided by host'}, {'category': 'Travel Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': None}, {'category': 'Other/Unspecified Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'access to technical facilities and/or media labs'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:26.760891+00:00,,,,,en,European Media Art Platform Residency Programme 2026,"Applicants must be EU residents or taxpayers in an EU member state, or residents/taxpayers of one of the eligible non-EU countries. Undergraduate and Master’s students are not eligible. PhD candidates and emerging artists of any age and academic background may apply.",European Media Art Platform Residency Programme 2026,"Applicants must be EU residents or taxpayers in an EU member state, or residents/taxpayers of one of the eligible non-EU countries. Undergraduate and Master’s students are not eligible. PhD candidates and emerging artists of any age and academic background may apply.",13 Mar 2026,2026-03-13,2026-09-23 12:37:25.278216+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_28881ec0704a,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/ape-camp-2026-open-call-for-overseas-artists-producers-and-engineers/,,Arts Council Korea (ARKO),"Arts Council Korea (ARKO) invites artists, producers, and engineers aged 39 or under from around the world to APE CAMP 2026. The program aims to nurture creative talent and activate sustainable networks for the convergence of art and technology. Through the camp, participants are supported in developing new ideas and building global networks.","Literature, visual arts, theatre and musical theatre, music, dance, traditional arts, interdisciplinary arts, etc.; technology fields related to art–technology convergence",camp,Republic of Korea,Seoul or Gyeonggi,Round-trip airfare (partial support) Accommodation during the camp period (based on shared rooms for two) Meals during the camp period,Free of charge,Young artists and producers aged 39 or under; Preference will be given to early-career technology professionals.,"Arts Council Korea (ARKO) invites artists, producers, and engineers aged 39 or under from around the world to APE CAMP 2026. The program aims to nurture creative talent and activate sustainable networks for the convergence of art and technology. Through the camp, participants are supported in developing new ideas and building global networks.","Literature, visual arts, theatre and musical theatre, music, dance, traditional arts, interdisciplinary arts, etc.; technology fields related to art–technology convergence",camp,Young artists and producers aged 39 or under; Preference will be given to early-career technology professionals.,Republic of Korea,Seoul or Gyeonggi,"['Literature/Writing', 'Visual Arts', 'Theatre', 'Music', 'Dance', 'Cultural Heritage', 'Multidisciplinary', 'Digital/New Media Arts']",['Other'],['Emerging/Early-Career'],['South Korea'],"[{'category': 'Travel Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'round-trip airfare, partial support'}, {'category': 'Accommodation/Housing', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'during the camp period, based on shared rooms for two'}, {'category': 'Other/Unspecified Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'meals during the camp period'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:26.760993+00:00,False,,,,en,"APE CAMP 2026: Open call for overseas artists, producers and engineers","General (mandatory) Applications must be submitted by individuals only. This open call is for international participants who do not hold Korean nationality. Participants must be able to attend all programs during the camp period from 12 to 16 June 2026. (※ Selection will be cancelled if a participant withdraws after selection or attends only part of the program.) Applicants must be able to communicate in English. Art category (Mandatory) Young artists and producers aged 39 or under who are actively engaged in creative practices related to art–technology convergence Literature, visual arts, theatre and musical theatre, music, dance, traditional arts, interdisciplinary arts, etc. Technology category (Mandatory) Professionals, researchers, and experts in technology fields who possess specialised knowledge applicable to art–technology convergence–based creative practices. The eligible technology fields include, but are not limited to, the areas listed below. Applicants working in other relevant technology fields not listed may also apply.","APE CAMP 2026: Open call for overseas artists, producers and engineers","General (mandatory) Applications must be submitted by individuals only. This open call is for international participants who do not hold Korean nationality. Participants must be able to attend all programs during the camp period from 12 to 16 June 2026. (※ Selection will be cancelled if a participant withdraws after selection or attends only part of the program.) Applicants must be able to communicate in English. Art category (Mandatory) Young artists and producers aged 39 or under who are actively engaged in creative practices related to art–technology convergence Literature, visual arts, theatre and musical theatre, music, dance, traditional arts, interdisciplinary arts, etc. Technology category (Mandatory) Professionals, researchers, and experts in technology fields who possess specialised knowledge applicable to art–technology convergence–based creative practices. The eligible technology fields include, but are not limited to, the areas listed below. Applicants working in other relevant technology fields not listed may also apply.","Thursday, 12 March 2026, 23:59 KST",2026-03-12,2026-09-23 12:37:25.285857+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_8a344b3ec711,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/ga-met-kunstenpunt-naar-classicalnext-in-budapest/,,Flanders Arts Institute & WBM,"From 8 to 11 April Classical:NEXT , an international meeting for the classical music sector with a conference, a fair and a showcase programme, will take place in Budapest. Flanders Arts Institute will once again coordinate our sector’s presence together with Wallonie-Bruxelles Musiques (WBM). Classical:NEXT is the main international gathering for classical music innovation in Europe. As always, we are looking forward to being part of this event again and highlighting our classical music. Want to join Flanders Arts Institute?",classical music,open call,Hungary,Budapest,€ 400 per person enrolled who does not receive an operational subsidy € 200 per registered person for those receiving an operating subsidy of less than €150000,,,"From 8 to 11 April Classical:NEXT , an international meeting for the classical music sector with a conference, a fair and a showcase programme, will take place in Budapest. Flanders Arts Institute will once again coordinate our sector’s presence together with Wallonie-Bruxelles Musiques (WBM). Classical:NEXT is the main international gathering for classical music innovation in Europe. As always, we are looking forward to being part of this event again and highlighting our classical music. Want to join Flanders Arts Institute?",classical music,open call,,Hungary,Budapest,['Music'],['Open Call'],[],['Hungary'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 400.0, 'amount_max': 400.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': None, 'note': 'for enrolled persons who do not receive an operational subsidy'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 200.0, 'amount_max': 200.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': None, 'note': 'for registered persons receiving an operating subsidy of less than €150000'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:26.760999+00:00,,,,,en,Join Flanders Arts Institute at Classical:NEXT in Budapest,"Are you eligible for this extra financial support? If so, please contact Ward Bosmans after you registered.",Join Flanders Arts Institute at Classical:NEXT in Budapest,"Are you eligible for this extra financial support? If so, please contact Ward Bosmans after you registered.",08 Mar 2026,2026-03-08,2026-09-23 12:37:25.288806+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_78c404ddf0fa,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-par-hasard-2/,,Par Hasard,"On May 23, Par Hasard is organizing ‘ Par Hasard x Giftshop ‘ together with Giftshop. We invite audiences to come and nose into the cooking pots of artists. Spectators do not always get the opportunity to get an insight into the whole process that leads to a final performance or show. And that is exactly what we want to change. Through this open call we would like to invite makers, performers, musicians, poets, dancers… to apply to participate in this Par Hasard edition. The idea is to give you the opportunity to show your work-in-progress in simple, clear and appropriate context. You can present your work-in-progress to a wide audience in order to take the next step in the creation process.",performing arts,open call,Belgium,,Travel expenses from countries outside of Belgium cannot be reimbursed.,,,"On May 23, Par Hasard is organizing ‘ Par Hasard x Giftshop ‘ together with Giftshop. We invite audiences to come and nose into the cooking pots of artists. Spectators do not always get the opportunity to get an insight into the whole process that leads to a final performance or show. And that is exactly what we want to change. Through this open call we would like to invite makers, performers, musicians, poets, dancers… to apply to participate in this Par Hasard edition. The idea is to give you the opportunity to show your work-in-progress in simple, clear and appropriate context. You can present your work-in-progress to a wide audience in order to take the next step in the creation process.",performing arts,open call,,Belgium,,['Performing Arts'],['Open Call'],[],['Belgium'],"[{'category': 'Travel Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'travel expenses from countries outside of Belgium cannot be reimbursed'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:26.761049+00:00,,,,,en,Open Call Par Hasard,For who – You have a degree in the arts or relevant experience in the arts sector – you share a work-in-progress or an experiment (max 15min) – your work is suitable for the location (limited technical resources) – your work-in-progress should have a performative character,Open Call Par Hasard,For who – You have a degree in the arts or relevant experience in the arts sector – you share a work-in-progress or an experiment (max 15min) – your work is suitable for the location (limited technical resources) – your work-in-progress should have a performative character,06 Mar 2026,2026-03-06,2026-09-23 12:37:25.292617+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_37a488364201,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-international-young-artists-presentation-iyap-2026/,https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfbckxMMwUyOIEt9jPYq85X8sRl7DhctVu7zjA_dNot4U0iiw/viewform?usp=dialog,Musica & AMUZ (Flanders Festival Antwerp),International Young Artist’s Presentation (IYAP) 2026 offers you a unique platform to shine in front of an international audience and professionals from the sector.,vocal and/or instrumental musicians and ensembles,presentation,Belgium,Antwerp,,There is no registration fee; only travel and accommodation costs are covered by the ensembles themselves.,Young,International Young Artist’s Presentation (IYAP) 2026 offers you a unique platform to shine in front of an international audience and professionals from the sector.,vocal and/or instrumental musicians and ensembles,presentation,Young,Belgium,Antwerp,['Music'],['Other'],['Emerging/Early-Career'],['Belgium'],[],,False,,,,en,OPEN CALL: International Young Artist’s Presentation (IYAP) 2026,Who is it for? Young vocal and/or instrumental musicians and ensembles with a maximum average age of 35. The ensemble focuses on playing historical instruments or using historical sources (up to 1920). A condition for participation is that the entire ensemble must be available and present from August 18 to 22.,OPEN CALL: International Young Artist’s Presentation (IYAP) 2026,Who is it for? Young vocal and/or instrumental musicians and ensembles with a maximum average age of 35. The ensemble focuses on playing historical instruments or using historical sources (up to 1920). A condition for participation is that the entire ensemble must be available and present from August 18 to 22.,01 Mar 2026,2026-03-01,2026-09-23 12:37:25.295631+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_3aeeb0c33c84,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-showcase-emerging-sound-2026/,https://www.stuk.be/en/program/open-call-showcase-emerging-sound-2026,"Q-02, STUK, Musica & C-TAKT","STUK, Q-O2, Musica and C-TAKT present an annual showcase of emerging sound artists in Belgium. The showcase shines a light on the diversity of the Belgian sound art landscape, and gives a boost to an upcoming generation of makers. We are looking for recent, existing sound work in any format: performance, installation, soundwalk, radio piece, intervention or other formats.",sound art,Open call,Belgium,,,,emerging,"STUK, Q-O2, Musica and C-TAKT present an annual showcase of emerging sound artists in Belgium. The showcase shines a light on the diversity of the Belgian sound art landscape, and gives a boost to an upcoming generation of makers. We are looking for recent, existing sound work in any format: performance, installation, soundwalk, radio piece, intervention or other formats.",sound art,Open call,emerging,Belgium,,['Music'],['Open Call'],['Emerging/Early-Career'],['Belgium'],[],,,,,,en,Open Call showcase Emerging Sound 2026,"For whom? You are an emerging sound artist. In other words: in training, recently graduated, at the start of a career or still in need of developing a network within the Belgian or international sound art field. You make sound-based work such as installation, performance, soundwalk, participatory work, radio art or intervention in public space. You are asked to propose only one existing work or work-in-progress that is not older than 2024. Submissions with more than one work will not be considered. You have a link to Belgium: either by residence, education or nationality.",Open Call showcase Emerging Sound 2026,"For whom? You are an emerging sound artist. In other words: in training, recently graduated, at the start of a career or still in need of developing a network within the Belgian or international sound art field. You make sound-based work such as installation, performance, soundwalk, participatory work, radio art or intervention in public space. You are asked to propose only one existing work or work-in-progress that is not older than 2024. Submissions with more than one work will not be considered. You have a link to Belgium: either by residence, education or nationality.",01 Mar 2026,2026-03-01,2026-09-23 12:37:25.299725+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_75bed82de405,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/pitch-je-nieuwe-creatie-tijdens-plateforme-op-kunstenfestivaldesarts-2/,https://form.jotform.com/260133770342348,Flanders Arts Institute and WBTD,"Plat(e)form(e) is a bi-community programme aimed at international professionals. It takes place during Kunstenfestivaldesarts and is organized by Flanders Arts Institute and Wallonie-Bruxelles Théâtre Danse. The programme supports Belgian artists and companies in their search for (inter)national partnerships, co-production opportunities and professional networking, while offering international guests insight into the diversity of the Belgian performing arts field.",performing arts,open call,Belgium,,Artists/companies without a contract or structural subsidies will receive a €250 excl. VAT fee for their presentation. ... Artists/companies without a contract or structural subsidies will receive a €150 excl. VAT fee for their pitch.,,,"Plat(e)form(e) is a bi-community programme aimed at international professionals. It takes place during Kunstenfestivaldesarts and is organized by Flanders Arts Institute and Wallonie-Bruxelles Théâtre Danse. The programme supports Belgian artists and companies in their search for (inter)national partnerships, co-production opportunities and professional networking, while offering international guests insight into the diversity of the Belgian performing arts field.",performing arts,open call,,Belgium,,['Performing Arts'],['Open Call'],[],['Belgium'],"[{'category': 'Exhibition/Presentation Support', 'amount_min': 250.0, 'amount_max': 250.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'excl. VAT, presentation fee for artists/companies without a contract or structural subsidies'}, {'category': 'Exhibition/Presentation Support', 'amount_min': 150.0, 'amount_max': 150.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'excl. VAT, pitch fee for artists/companies without a contract or structural subsidies'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:26.761057+00:00,,,,,en,Pitch your new creation during Plat(e)form(e) at Kunstenfestivaldesarts,"The artist/company is professionally active and based in Belgium
The artist/company and project are supported by at least one Belgian and/or international partner
The project falls within the field of performing arts
The project has international potential
The artist/company is available from 26 to 28 May 2026 (full days)
The artist/company is accompanied by its production/distribution platform or by a representative of one of the project’s partners
Additional criteria – Work in progress showcase
The artist/company can present an excerpt on stage with basic technical support
The project must premiere in the 2026 – 2027 season
A €250 fee is provided for non-structurally funded artists/companies (if more than two people involved, the accompanying production platform is expected to cover additional fees)
Additional criteria – Pitch
The artist/company can clearly present the project within 10 minutes , followed by a 5-minute discussion
Production is foreseen between 2026 – 2027
A €150 fee is provided for non-structurally funded artists/companies (fee applies per presentation / one person)",Pitch your new creation during Plat(e)form(e) at Kunstenfestivaldesarts,"The artist/company is professionally active and based in Belgium
