kunsten_be_flanders_8e81a92d284b,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/kunstenaar-gezocht-voor-participatief-project-in-sint-agatha-berchem/,https://forms.office.com/Pages/ResponsePage.aspx?id=5VYrkWCavke4UrG501iDNIKO_mxb6O5Mq8Tb_x8Xku5UNkpWMUhFQkUyM1lWN05VT1pBWDFJQk9PVC4u,"Gemeenschapscentrum De Kroon, Archipel19","The socio-cultural centres De Kroon and Archipel19 in Sint-Agatha-Berchem are looking for an artist interested in co-creation, who wants to develop an artistic programme that creates connection in the public space, together with local residents.","image, movement and interaction",Commission,Belgium,Sint-Agatha-Berchem,"There is a total budget of €19,500 for the project. This includes all the costs.",,,"The socio-cultural centres De Kroon and Archipel19 in Sint-Agatha-Berchem are looking for an artist interested in co-creation, who wants to develop an artistic programme that creates connection in the public space, together with local residents.","image, movement and interaction",Commission,,Belgium,Sint-Agatha-Berchem,"['Visual Arts', 'Performing Arts', 'Digital/New Media Arts']",['Commission'],[],['Belgium'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 19500.0, 'amount_max': 19500.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'total project budget; no per-applicant amount stated'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:31.816280+00:00,,,,,en,Artist sought for Participatory Project in Sint-Agatha-Berchem,"The socio-cultural centres De Kroon and Archipel19 in Sint-Agatha-Berchem are looking for an artist interested in co-creation, who wants to develop an artistic programme that creates connection in the public space, together with local residents. Are you someone who knows how to harness the power of imagery and nonverbal communication to bring people closer together? Would you like to work with an intergenerational group of residents around Parc Pirsoul? Then this project is for you.

You will develop an artistic programme with and for the neighbourhood. Together with residents, you will work on creating playful, visual installations in the public space .

As an artist, you will design a co-creative programme: You will organise contact sessions with the neighbourhood in the park or in socio-cultural centre De Kroon/Archipel19 during the period March – June 2026. You will be actively engaged in the neighbourhood and work with residents and local partners . From idea to end result, co-creation is the core focus, with essential input from an intergenerational group of participants . Socio-cultural centre De Kroon and Archipel19 will put together this group of residents for the project. Archipel10 and De Kroon will also support you during the process in further empowering this group of neighbourhood residents. You will focus on language-transcending connection through images and action, not (only) through words. Together, you will develop a visible, tangible and sustainable end result that lasts beyond the project. You will work with the target group towards a powerful artistic end result that is supported by the neighbourhood. Along with the socio-cultural worker at the socio-cultural centre, you will generate involvement on the part of the target group and partners, and act with respect for the participants. You will pay special attention to those whose voice is not always heard and will actively seek out these voices. You will work within the specified budget.

The group will grow through the process: everyone is welcome, with no barriers or exclusivity.",Artist sought for Participatory Project in Sint-Agatha-Berchem,"The socio-cultural centres De Kroon and Archipel19 in Sint-Agatha-Berchem are looking for an artist interested in co-creation, who wants to develop an artistic programme that creates connection in the public space, together with local residents. Are you someone who knows how to harness the power of imagery and nonverbal communication to bring people closer together? Would you like to work with an intergenerational group of residents around Parc Pirsoul? Then this project is for you.

You will develop an artistic programme with and for the neighbourhood. Together with residents, you will work on creating playful, visual installations in the public space .

As an artist, you will design a co-creative programme: You will organise contact sessions with the neighbourhood in the park or in socio-cultural centre De Kroon/Archipel19 during the period March – June 2026. You will be actively engaged in the neighbourhood and work with residents and local partners . From idea to end result, co-creation is the core focus, with essential input from an intergenerational group of participants . Socio-cultural centre De Kroon and Archipel19 will put together this group of residents for the project. Archipel10 and De Kroon will also support you during the process in further empowering this group of neighbourhood residents. You will focus on language-transcending connection through images and action, not (only) through words. Together, you will develop a visible, tangible and sustainable end result that lasts beyond the project. You will work with the target group towards a powerful artistic end result that is supported by the neighbourhood. Along with the socio-cultural worker at the socio-cultural centre, you will generate involvement on the part of the target group and partners, and act with respect for the participants. You will pay special attention to those whose voice is not always heard and will actively seek out these voices. You will work within the specified budget.

The group will grow through the process: everyone is welcome, with no barriers or exclusivity.",18 Dec 2025,2025-12-18,2026-09-23 12:37:25.416539+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_962385d3c6bf,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/farm-studio-india-international-artist-residency-in-rural-rajasthan-2/,https://farmingstudio.wordpress.com/art-residency/,Farm Studio India,"Residency Farm Studio International Artist Residency is located in a rural community in India. Residents stay and create in a quiet art centre and beautiful environment where they can develop their artwork free from accustomed distractions. Here, collaboration and experimentation is encouraged. Relationships form between the artists coming from different countries and varied social, cultural, and artistic backgrounds. Many exciting exchanges and dialogues among artists take place, including scheduled artist talks, presentations, works in progress showings, etc. Farm Studio also promotes and celebrates the local community’s artistic and cultural identity while also introducing art and culture of others’ (Indian and International guests) back to the community. This intercultural exchange broadens everyone’s experiences and fosters art appreciation.",Artists of all disciplines creating in any media,Residency,India,Andore Village,,,,"Residency Farm Studio International Artist Residency is located in a rural community in India. Residents stay and create in a quiet art centre and beautiful environment where they can develop their artwork free from accustomed distractions. Here, collaboration and experimentation is encouraged. Relationships form between the artists coming from different countries and varied social, cultural, and artistic backgrounds. Many exciting exchanges and dialogues among artists take place, including scheduled artist talks, presentations, works in progress showings, etc. Farm Studio also promotes and celebrates the local community’s artistic and cultural identity while also introducing art and culture of others’ (Indian and International guests) back to the community. This intercultural exchange broadens everyone’s experiences and fosters art appreciation.",Artists of all disciplines creating in any media,Residency,,India,Andore Village,['Multidisciplinary'],['Residency'],[],['India'],[],,,,,,en,Farm Studio India – International Artist Residency in Rural Rajasthan,Artists of all disciplines creating in any media are welcome to apply.,Farm Studio India – International Artist Residency in Rural Rajasthan,Artists of all disciplines creating in any media are welcome to apply.,15 Dec 2025,2025-12-15,2026-09-23 12:37:25.420032+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_63435520343a,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/ga-op-residentie-bij-morpho-in-antwerpen/,https://morphoantwerp.be/en/open-calls/curatorial-residency-goethe-institut-brussel,Goethe-Institut Brüssel and MORPHO,"The Goethe-Institut Brüssel and MORPHO are delighted to inaugurate their collaboration in 2026 with an international curatorial residency. Goethe-Institut Brüssel supports the participation of one curator based in or from Germany going to Antwerp for a three-month residency, in the framework of a thematic programme that explores curating in times of democratic crisis.",curating,residency,Belgium,Antwerp,Goethe-Institut Brüssel supports the participation of one curator based in or from Germany going to Antwerp for a three-month residency,,,"The Goethe-Institut Brüssel and MORPHO are delighted to inaugurate their collaboration in 2026 with an international curatorial residency. Goethe-Institut Brüssel supports the participation of one curator based in or from Germany going to Antwerp for a three-month residency, in the framework of a thematic programme that explores curating in times of democratic crisis.",curating,residency,,Belgium,Antwerp,['Curating/Art Criticism'],['Residency'],[],['Belgium'],"[{'category': 'Accommodation/Housing', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': 'per month', 'note': 'three-month residency in Antwerp for one curator based in or from Germany'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:31.816320+00:00,,,,,en,Open Call – Curatorial Residency Goethe-Institut Brüssel,"This call is open to German curators and curators based in Germany. You have a proven critical practice dedicated to current democratic processes and opening up visions for the future. You want to focus on curatorial research and to present research results during the residency. You want to engage with the Belgian cultural landscape. You are welcome regardless of age, ethnic-cultural background, gender diversity, neurodiversity, and more. We do our best to accommodate everyone’s needs, but the specific architecture of the building (stairs, no lift) means the residency is not suitable for all conditions. There is only room for 1 adult, possibly with a child (Family top-up: 100 € per month). You are welcome to contact us in advance to discuss your personal situation.",Open Call – Curatorial Residency Goethe-Institut Brüssel,"This call is open to German curators and curators based in Germany. You have a proven critical practice dedicated to current democratic processes and opening up visions for the future. You want to focus on curatorial research and to present research results during the residency. You want to engage with the Belgian cultural landscape. You are welcome regardless of age, ethnic-cultural background, gender diversity, neurodiversity, and more. We do our best to accommodate everyone’s needs, but the specific architecture of the building (stairs, no lift) means the residency is not suitable for all conditions. There is only room for 1 adult, possibly with a child (Family top-up: 100 € per month). You are welcome to contact us in advance to discuss your personal situation.",07 Dec 2025,2025-12-07,2026-09-23 12:37:25.425375+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_22da6aff727f,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/ithaka-26-kunstenfestival-voor-jong-talent/,https://www.loko.be/nl/actualiteit/ithaka-2026-open-call-for-artists-2,LOKO Cultuur,"We are looking for young, emerging artists (students, recent graduates, self-taught) from all disciplines who want to experiment within the theme “Human & Animal”. The theme explores the intimate bond with animals, but also broader societal and academic questions around care, systems, and ecology. Ithaka serves as a crucial springboard for emerging talent. We offer selected artists curatorial and production support, a production budget, and the opportunity to show their work to a large and diverse (student) audience.",all disciplines,Call for Artists,Belgium,Leuven,"We offer selected artists curatorial and production support, a production budget, and the opportunity to show their work to a large and diverse (student) audience.",,"young, emerging artists (students, recent graduates, self-taught)","We are looking for young, emerging artists (students, recent graduates, self-taught) from all disciplines who want to experiment within the theme “Human & Animal”. The theme explores the intimate bond with animals, but also broader societal and academic questions around care, systems, and ecology. Ithaka serves as a crucial springboard for emerging talent. We offer selected artists curatorial and production support, a production budget, and the opportunity to show their work to a large and diverse (student) audience.",all disciplines,Call for Artists,"young, emerging artists (students, recent graduates, self-taught)",Belgium,Leuven,['Multidisciplinary'],['Open Call'],['Emerging/Early-Career'],['Belgium'],"[{'category': 'Exhibition/Presentation Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'opportunity to show work to a large and diverse student audience'}, {'category': 'Mentorship/Training', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'curatorial support'}, {'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'production support and production budget'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:31.816328+00:00,,,,,en,Ithaka ’26: arts festival for young talent,"We are looking for young, emerging artists (students, recent graduates, self-taught) from all disciplines who want to experiment within the theme “Human & Animal”.",Ithaka ’26: arts festival for young talent,"We are looking for young, emerging artists (students, recent graduates, self-taught) from all disciplines who want to experiment within the theme “Human & Animal”.",07 Dec 2025,2025-12-07,2026-09-23 12:37:25.429737+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_b25efb4eb1e8,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/kunstenpunt-zoekt-toekomstdenkers-meerstemmigheid/,https://register.kunsten.be/en/meeting-programmes/detail/185/flanders-arts-institute-seeks-multi-voiced-forward-thinkers/about?preview=cadd170d16f1aa877df29b3a38599f2e55f8ad0a,Flanders Arts Institute,"In 2025 Flanders Arts Institute is launching a three-year project on multi-voicedness in the arts. During this period, we will work together with (hands-on) experts and committed artists, citizens and organisations – inside and outside the arts field – to develop tools to achieve a multi-voiced arts field. In 2025, we will identify barriers and opportunities, which we will then translate into concrete tools. In January and February 2026, we will be organising three days – two intensive days in a small group and a public event – to work on concrete ideas for a multi-voiced arts field.",arts,call,Belgium,Malines,"For participants who are not doing this as part of a paid role at an organisation, we provide fair compensation.",,,"In 2025 Flanders Arts Institute is launching a three-year project on multi-voicedness in the arts. During this period, we will work together with (hands-on) experts and committed artists, citizens and organisations – inside and outside the arts field – to develop tools to achieve a multi-voiced arts field. In 2025, we will identify barriers and opportunities, which we will then translate into concrete tools. In January and February 2026, we will be organising three days – two intensive days in a small group and a public event – to work on concrete ideas for a multi-voiced arts field.",arts,call,,Belgium,Malines,['Multidisciplinary'],['Open Call'],[],['Belgium'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'fair compensation; amount not specified'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:31.816334+00:00,,,,,en,Flanders Arts Institute seeks multi-voiced forward thinkers,"Individuals with expertise and an interest in multi-voicedness and its intersectional approach. Individuals with lived experience in their field of expertise are an advantage. Who are active in the arts (artist, cultural worker, …). Individuals who are available on 19 and 26 January 2026, from 11 am to 4 pm each day. In Malines.",Flanders Arts Institute seeks multi-voiced forward thinkers,"Individuals with expertise and an interest in multi-voicedness and its intersectional approach. Individuals with lived experience in their field of expertise are an advantage. Who are active in the arts (artist, cultural worker, …). Individuals who are available on 19 and 26 January 2026, from 11 am to 4 pm each day. In Malines.",05 Dec 2025,2025-12-05,2026-09-23 12:37:25.433464+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_70e60edf5971,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/oproep-voor-onderzoeksbeurs-voor-curatoren-in-arles/,https://www.rencontres-arles.com/en/bourse-de-recherche-curatoriale-appel-a-candidatures/,The Rencontres d’Arles,The Rencontres d’Arles is delighted to announce the launch of the new edition of the Curatorial Research Fellowship.,exhibition curators,curatorial research fellowship,,Arles,"The maximum € 20,000 grant includes (1) an initial amount of €5,000 in copyright acquired for the winner of the Rencontres d’Arles Curatorial Award ; and (2) a second amount of €15,000 if approval, to produce the project if presented on Les Rencontres d’Arles program.",,,The Rencontres d’Arles is delighted to announce the launch of the new edition of the Curatorial Research Fellowship.,exhibition curators,curatorial research fellowship,,,Arles,['Curating/Art Criticism'],['Fellowship'],[],[],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 5000.0, 'amount_max': 5000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'copyright acquired for the winner of the Rencontres d’Arles Curatorial Award'}, {'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': 15000.0, 'amount_max': 15000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'if approved, to produce the project if presented in Les Rencontres d’Arles program'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:31.816348+00:00,,,,,en,Open call for Curatorial Research Fellowship in Arles,"The Rencontres d’Arles €20,000 curatorial research fellowship is open to all exhibition curators.",Open call for Curatorial Research Fellowship in Arles,"The Rencontres d’Arles €20,000 curatorial research fellowship is open to all exhibition curators.",01 Dec 2025,2025-12-01,2026-09-23 12:37:25.436684+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_77942e92b1c5,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-love-among-the-artists-residency-in-marseille/,https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeU7SWy-9a8OYt9xQvNHk0NnLMkFAy9MZTdsSLQ-3Nf1Oqfww/viewform,Studio Prouvost,"LATA – Love Among The Artists, a project supported by Studio Prouvost, invites you for a self-directed two-week residency in a sunlit apartment by the Mediterranean Sea in Marseille.",artists,Residency,France,Marseille,A fully equipped 45 m² apartment next to Les Catalans beach,,,"LATA – Love Among The Artists, a project supported by Studio Prouvost, invites you for a self-directed two-week residency in a sunlit apartment by the Mediterranean Sea in Marseille.",artists,Residency,,France,Marseille,['Multidisciplinary'],['Residency'],[],['France'],"[{'category': 'Accommodation/Housing', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'fully equipped 45 m² apartment next to Les Catalans beach'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:31.816496+00:00,,,,,en,Open Call – “Love Among The Artists” Residency in Marseille,"We are interested in artists that explore transitions from urban to natural, from concrete to cliffside, from the city’s buzz to the sea’s calm",Open Call – “Love Among The Artists” Residency in Marseille,"We are interested in artists that explore transitions from urban to natural, from concrete to cliffside, from the city’s buzz to the sea’s calm","Sunday, 30 November 2025 (midnight).",2025-11-30,2026-09-23 12:37:25.441455+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_df27ab545c60,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-hosting-as-artistic-practice/,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-hosting-as-artistic-practice/,Globe Aroma,"Globe Aroma is looking for a multidisciplinary artist : a poetic thinker with a practical mind and a social tongue, someone who can gently spark everyone’s imagination. From January to June 2026 , we invite one artist to share a unique time and space with our artistic community in the heart of Brussels. We are looking for a person whose artistic practice is centered around hosting and hospitality, someone who builds an open and curious space where creation can appear unexpectedly. During these six months, you will work with people who feel the desire to create, but who are not artists themselves!",multidisciplinary,open call,Belgium,Brussels,6-month employment via Globe Aroma’s payroll (barema PC 329.01),,,"Globe Aroma is looking for a multidisciplinary artist : a poetic thinker with a practical mind and a social tongue, someone who can gently spark everyone’s imagination. From January to June 2026 , we invite one artist to share a unique time and space with our artistic community in the heart of Brussels. We are looking for a person whose artistic practice is centered around hosting and hospitality, someone who builds an open and curious space where creation can appear unexpectedly. During these six months, you will work with people who feel the desire to create, but who are not artists themselves!",multidisciplinary,open call,,Belgium,Brussels,['Multidisciplinary'],['Open Call'],[],['Belgium'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': 'per month', 'note': '6-month employment via payroll; amount not specified'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:31.816508+00:00,,,,,en,OPEN CALL – HOSTING AS ARTISTIC PRACTICE,"We are looking for a person whose artistic practice is centered around hosting and hospitality, someone who builds an open and curious space where creation can appear unexpectedly.

We are looking for someone who: works across disciplines (textile, movement, ceramics, poetry, cooking, etc.); blends art, hospitality, care, and community; feels comfortable in multilingual settings; is familiar with migration (by lived experience or affinity); can listen, let go, and stay open to the unexpected; prefers process over product; enjoys collaborating with people with no artistic training but strong imagination.

We especially welcome applications from artists with migration backgrounds, artists of color, queer, neurodiverse, and non-binary artists.",OPEN CALL – HOSTING AS ARTISTIC PRACTICE,"We are looking for a person whose artistic practice is centered around hosting and hospitality, someone who builds an open and curious space where creation can appear unexpectedly.

We are looking for someone who: works across disciplines (textile, movement, ceramics, poetry, cooking, etc.); blends art, hospitality, care, and community; feels comfortable in multilingual settings; is familiar with migration (by lived experience or affinity); can listen, let go, and stay open to the unexpected; prefers process over product; enjoys collaborating with people with no artistic training but strong imagination.

We especially welcome applications from artists with migration backgrounds, artists of color, queer, neurodiverse, and non-binary artists.",20 Nov 2025,2025-11-20,2026-09-23 12:37:25.444678+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_77d04e963291,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/dingen-die-niet-verkopen-verkopen-u-dingen/,https://www.dingendienietverkopen.be/calls,Dingen die niet verkopen,"We want to extend this theme to our annual group exhibition, ‘Dingen die niet verkopen, verkopen u dingen’, which will run from December 11th to December 21st of 2025. At a time when reality is stranger than fiction, we’re looking for visual art that actively explores the friction between truth and make-believe. For the occasion, we’re opening a department store stocked with untruths.",visual art,open call,Belgium,Antwerp,"We do not take ownership of your work, and you receive the full amount as agreed upon if sold. We will add an additional 20% to the sales price to cover the costs and communication of this exhibition, which we keep.",,,"We want to extend this theme to our annual group exhibition, ‘Dingen die niet verkopen, verkopen u dingen’, which will run from December 11th to December 21st of 2025. At a time when reality is stranger than fiction, we’re looking for visual art that actively explores the friction between truth and make-believe. For the occasion, we’re opening a department store stocked with untruths.",visual art,open call,,Belgium,Antwerp,['Visual Arts'],['Open Call'],[],['Belgium'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'artist receives full agreed sale amount if sold'}, {'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'an additional 20% of the sales price is added to cover exhibition costs and communication; percentage only'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:31.816514+00:00,,,,,en,Open call Dingen die niet verkopen (‘Stuff that does not sell’),"We are looking for unique objects and/or editions/multiples that tell a false or distorted narrative through text or image. Three-dimensional works and objects, as well as zines and alternative forms of publication, are eligible. We prefer objects that can be displayed on a shelf, newspaper carousel, or table. Works intended for wall mounting are not eligible. Specifics: Your work tells a (fictional) story through text and/or image. We are looking for small works: you can hold them in one hand and they cost no more than €100 (including VAT).",Open call Dingen die niet verkopen (‘Stuff that does not sell’),"We are looking for unique objects and/or editions/multiples that tell a false or distorted narrative through text or image. Three-dimensional works and objects, as well as zines and alternative forms of publication, are eligible. We prefer objects that can be displayed on a shelf, newspaper carousel, or table. Works intended for wall mounting are not eligible. Specifics: Your work tells a (fictional) story through text and/or image. We are looking for small works: you can hold them in one hand and they cost no more than €100 (including VAT).",16 Nov 2025,2025-11-16,2026-09-23 12:37:25.448390+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_85c853ed4180,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/novi-sad-theatre-festival-2026-call-for-performances-for-children-and-young-people-serbia/,https://www.festivalnpi.co.rs/en/festival2024/news/open-call-novi-sad-thatre-festival-2026,"Youth Theatre, Novi Sad","Youth Theatre, Novi Sad, has opened the call for the 5th International Theatre Festival for Children and Youth, which will take place in the second week of May 2026. Professional theatres from around the world are invited to apply with performances for children and young people across all genres – from drama and puppetry to dance, shadow and object theatre. All types of theatre creation for children and youth are represented at the Festival.",Theatre,Call,Serbia,Novi Sad,"the organiser of the festival, provides accommodation and food for the participants as well as travel expenses in the total amount up to 2,000 EUR.",,,"Youth Theatre, Novi Sad, has opened the call for the 5th International Theatre Festival for Children and Youth, which will take place in the second week of May 2026. Professional theatres from around the world are invited to apply with performances for children and young people across all genres – from drama and puppetry to dance, shadow and object theatre. All types of theatre creation for children and youth are represented at the Festival.",Theatre,Call,,Serbia,Novi Sad,['Theatre'],['Open Call'],[],['Serbia'],"[{'category': 'Accommodation/Housing', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'accommodation and food for participants'}, {'category': 'Travel Support', 'amount_min': 2000.0, 'amount_max': 2000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'travel expenses up to this total amount'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:31.816520+00:00,,,,,en,Novi Sad Theatre Festival 2026 Call for Performances for Children and Young People (Serbia),"Professional theatres from around the world are invited to apply with performances for children and young people across all genres – from drama and puppetry to dance, shadow and object theatre.",Novi Sad Theatre Festival 2026 Call for Performances for Children and Young People (Serbia),"Professional theatres from around the world are invited to apply with performances for children and young people across all genres – from drama and puppetry to dance, shadow and object theatre.",15 Nov 2025,2025-11-15,2026-09-23 12:37:25.451952+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_6aad32a7d163,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/werkgroep-advies-module-startende-kunstenaars/,,Kunstenpunt / Flanders Arts Institute,"Through this open call, we want to put together an external working group that will thoroughly review the module for starting artists, gather feedback, and provide input for its rewriting.","visual arts, performing arts, and/or classical music",open call,Belgium,,We offer you compensation of €850 excluding VAT for the entire process. Train tickets will be reimbursed.,,starting artists / emerging artists,"Through this open call, we want to put together an external working group that will thoroughly review the module for starting artists, gather feedback, and provide input for its rewriting.","visual arts, performing arts, and/or classical music",open call,starting artists / emerging artists,Belgium,,"['Visual Arts', 'Performing Arts', 'Music']",['Open Call'],['Emerging/Early-Career'],['Belgium'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 850.0, 'amount_max': 850.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'excluding VAT for the entire process'}, {'category': 'Travel Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'train tickets reimbursed'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:31.816556+00:00,,,,,en,Working group advice: module for starting artists,"You are active in the visual arts, performing arts, and/or classical music. You are not (or no longer) studying. Or you did not follow the traditional path of art education as an artist. You are at the start of your professional career – regardless of age – or you still have vivid memories of what it was like to be a starting artist. Or you have experience in supporting or guiding artists who are at the start of their professional careers. Or you are experiencing social barriers to starting your career. Due to their underrepresentation in the arts, we want to encourage everyone of color, women, people with disabilities or neurodivergence, members of the LGBTQIA+ community, and individuals who experience financial barriers to participate.",Working group advice: module for starting artists,"You are active in the visual arts, performing arts, and/or classical music. You are not (or no longer) studying. Or you did not follow the traditional path of art education as an artist. You are at the start of your professional career – regardless of age – or you still have vivid memories of what it was like to be a starting artist. Or you have experience in supporting or guiding artists who are at the start of their professional careers. Or you are experiencing social barriers to starting your career. Due to their underrepresentation in the arts, we want to encourage everyone of color, women, people with disabilities or neurodivergence, members of the LGBTQIA+ community, and individuals who experience financial barriers to participate.",14 Nov 2025,2025-11-14,2026-09-23 12:37:25.455479+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_937443956cc9,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/art-explora-cite-internationale-des-arts-residency-programme-2026/,https://artexplora.plateformecandidature.com/,Art Explora,"Art Explora, the international foundation that fosters new encounters between arts and audiences, locally, nationally and internationally, is pleased to announce that the call for applications for the Art Explora – Cité internationale des Arts Residency Programme 2026 is now open. Until October 31st 2025 , artists and collectives of artists, researchers and curators from all around the world are invited to apply for this unique residency programme, with projects that question relations between art, science and technology, and address social and ecological issues of our time.","artists, researchers and curators",Residency,Albania,Tirana,"All residents benefit from a fully-furnished studio for 3 or 6 months, production and living grants. ... each year, two artists hosted within the Art Explora Residencies will also benefit from access to Lafayette Anticipations’ production workshops, additional support and a production budget of up to €3,000.",,,"Art Explora, the international foundation that fosters new encounters between arts and audiences, locally, nationally and internationally, is pleased to announce that the call for applications for the Art Explora – Cité internationale des Arts Residency Programme 2026 is now open. Until October 31st 2025 , artists and collectives of artists, researchers and curators from all around the world are invited to apply for this unique residency programme, with projects that question relations between art, science and technology, and address social and ecological issues of our time.","artists, researchers and curators",Residency,,Albania,Tirana,"['Multidisciplinary', 'Curating/Art Criticism']",['Residency'],[],['Albania'],"[{'category': 'Accommodation/Housing', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': 'per month', 'note': 'fully-furnished studio for 3 or 6 months'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': 'per month', 'note': 'production and living grants'}, {'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': 3000.0, 'amount_max': 3000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'additional production budget up to this amount for two artists'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:31.817766+00:00,,,,,en,Art Explora – Cité internationale des arts Residency programme 2026,"artists and collectives of artists, researchers and curators from all around the world are invited to apply for this unique residency programme, with projects that question relations between art, science and technology, and address social and ecological issues of our time.",Art Explora – Cité internationale des arts Residency programme 2026,"artists and collectives of artists, researchers and curators from all around the world are invited to apply for this unique residency programme, with projects that question relations between art, science and technology, and address social and ecological issues of our time.","Applications are open until October 30th, 2025, 11:59pm (GMT+02:00, Europe/Paris)",2025-10-30,2026-09-23 12:37:25.460869+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_c38ccf84a460,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-cinema-canape/,https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeLTGOleELcKlPxI-kfUjgBmHpKCFaJ5kUl_wfanYvPmVnZag/viewform,Call Canapé vzw,"CINEMA CANAPÉ is always looking for people who want to share their work! This open call will serve as a database. So don’t worry if we don’t reach out to you right away, we’ll keep your submission and contact artists who fit upcoming screenings. Whether you’re working on short film, experimental video, documentary, animation, or something in between: all forms and genres are welcome. No experience needed (but very welcome) we want to create an open space for experimentation, trying things out, and sharing with others. Our upcoming curation has a special focus on the spooky, mysterious, and dark","filmmakers, video artists, and moving-image makers",open call,,,,,,"CINEMA CANAPÉ is always looking for people who want to share their work! This open call will serve as a database. So don’t worry if we don’t reach out to you right away, we’ll keep your submission and contact artists who fit upcoming screenings. Whether you’re working on short film, experimental video, documentary, animation, or something in between: all forms and genres are welcome. No experience needed (but very welcome) we want to create an open space for experimentation, trying things out, and sharing with others. Our upcoming curation has a special focus on the spooky, mysterious, and dark","filmmakers, video artists, and moving-image makers",open call,,,,"['Film/Video', 'Visual Arts']",['Open Call'],[],[],[],,,,,,en,Open call Cinema Canapé,"This call is especially for all filmmakers, video artists, and moving-image makers. Whether you’re working on short film, experimental video, documentary, animation, or something in between: all forms and genres are welcome. No experience needed (but very welcome)",Open call Cinema Canapé,"This call is especially for all filmmakers, video artists, and moving-image makers. Whether you’re working on short film, experimental video, documentary, animation, or something in between: all forms and genres are welcome. No experience needed (but very welcome)",20 Oct 2025,2025-10-20,2026-09-23 12:37:25.464190+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_0b695cd43d60,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/invitation-for-members/,https://forms.gle/7gLeM6zVynQNyqBB9,DomestiCity,"DomestiCity is a socially engaged artist-run space based in Laken, Brussels. We open up the basement of our house for neighbours, friends, passerby for artistic and reflective activities and events linked to craft – slowing down – working together – dialogue. In 2025 we will reshape the collective into a living (room) library where we gather and pass on (embodied) knowledge about crafts – commonism – micro-politics.",craft,Call,Belgium,Brussels,,,,"DomestiCity is a socially engaged artist-run space based in Laken, Brussels. We open up the basement of our house for neighbours, friends, passerby for artistic and reflective activities and events linked to craft – slowing down – working together – dialogue. In 2025 we will reshape the collective into a living (room) library where we gather and pass on (embodied) knowledge about crafts – commonism – micro-politics.",craft,Call,,Belgium,Brussels,['Craft'],['Open Call'],[],['Belgium'],[],,,,,,en,Invitation for Members*,"Housemate/member : You participate in the project from within the house. You join meetings and engage with the public gatherings in our basement twice a month. You give input in the gatherings- what would you like to do? You help to shape the always-evolving collective.You live in our house and can use the project space as a collective atelier/work space. (If you want more info about the house (democratic rent, photos, housemates) or would like to visit it, please contact domesticitybrussels@gmail.com

Participative member : You engage with the public gatherings in our basement twice a month (+-8h per month). You give input in the gatherings – what would you like to do? You can use the project space as a collective atelier/working space. You help to shape the always-evolving collective.

Volunteer : You would like to help out with one of the gatherings that interests you. On this link , you can find more information about the specific questions we would like to have an answer on.",Invitation for Members*,"Housemate/member : You participate in the project from within the house. You join meetings and engage with the public gatherings in our basement twice a month. You give input in the gatherings- what would you like to do? You help to shape the always-evolving collective.You live in our house and can use the project space as a collective atelier/work space. (If you want more info about the house (democratic rent, photos, housemates) or would like to visit it, please contact domesticitybrussels@gmail.com

Participative member : You engage with the public gatherings in our basement twice a month (+-8h per month). You give input in the gatherings – what would you like to do? You can use the project space as a collective atelier/working space. You help to shape the always-evolving collective.

Volunteer : You would like to help out with one of the gatherings that interests you. On this link , you can find more information about the specific questions we would like to have an answer on.",12 Oct 2025,2025-10-12,2026-09-23 12:37:25.467257+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_6f9b625b869d,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/word-een-rema-member/,https://www.rema-eemn.net/join-us/,REMA,"By becoming a REMA member, you can take part in all REMA events and boost your own activities!",early music,membership call for applications,,,,,,"By becoming a REMA member, you can take part in all REMA events and boost your own activities!",early music,membership call for applications,,,,['Music'],['Open Call'],[],[],[],,,,,,en,Become REMA member,"Since 25 May 2023, REMA has been open to all types of early music players (ensembles, festivals, concert halls, research institutes, labels, agents, conservatoires, etc.). There is only one way to join REMA: each year, a call for applications enables around thirty new organisations to join the REMA network. In 2025, applications are open from 1 July to 8 October: new members will be welcomed on 1 January 2026. The 2026 General Assembly will be held in Malta from 20 to 22 January 2026. CRITERIA FOR JOINING Applicant organisations must have been in existence for a minimum of three years and possess a legal entity status. The Board of Directors will look at: The overall quality of the activities The alignment of the applicants’ values with REMA The criteria and selection process are detailed in the full call. You will be asked to: Provide information about your organisation. Select a main activity: promoter, ensemble, education, research, agent, publisher or other. Once accepted, members can represent all their activities. Answer specific questions related to your main activity and submit relevant documentation (e.g. programme of activities, list of publications, concerts, etc.) Explain your motivation for joining REMA and how your values are in line with the network. Submit a letter of recommendation from a REMA member. Additional information: if you have taken part in a network project in the past, include this information in your application. CODE OF CONDUCT From the moment they apply, all candidates must endorse the network’s code of conduct, established with the members, which ensures adherence to professional ethics among REMA members. The code of conduct delineates the expected or unlawful or inappropriate behavior from members, and outlines the procedure for penalizing such conduct.",Become REMA member,"Since 25 May 2023, REMA has been open to all types of early music players (ensembles, festivals, concert halls, research institutes, labels, agents, conservatoires, etc.). There is only one way to join REMA: each year, a call for applications enables around thirty new organisations to join the REMA network. In 2025, applications are open from 1 July to 8 October: new members will be welcomed on 1 January 2026. The 2026 General Assembly will be held in Malta from 20 to 22 January 2026. CRITERIA FOR JOINING Applicant organisations must have been in existence for a minimum of three years and possess a legal entity status. The Board of Directors will look at: The overall quality of the activities The alignment of the applicants’ values with REMA The criteria and selection process are detailed in the full call. You will be asked to: Provide information about your organisation. Select a main activity: promoter, ensemble, education, research, agent, publisher or other. Once accepted, members can represent all their activities. Answer specific questions related to your main activity and submit relevant documentation (e.g. programme of activities, list of publications, concerts, etc.) Explain your motivation for joining REMA and how your values are in line with the network. Submit a letter of recommendation from a REMA member. Additional information: if you have taken part in a network project in the past, include this information in your application. CODE OF CONDUCT From the moment they apply, all candidates must endorse the network’s code of conduct, established with the members, which ensures adherence to professional ethics among REMA members. The code of conduct delineates the expected or unlawful or inappropriate behavior from members, and outlines the procedure for penalizing such conduct.",08 Oct 2025,2025-10-08,2026-09-23 12:37:25.470611+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_a5a634ac992c,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/gezocht-belgische-fotografen-voor-nieuwe-tentoonstelling-bij-hangar/,https://www.hangar.art/open-call2025,Hangar,"As part of the bicentenary celebration (September 2026 to September 2027) of le Point de vue du gras* , considered the first photographic image in world history, the Centre national des arts plastiques (CNAP) in France has commissioned 15 photographers, focusing on the invention of photography and the relevance of its possible reinvention today. The projects are created using all the techniques that currently allow artists to produce photographic images in innovative forms. Hangar, one of the certified venues of the bicentenary celebration, will host the exhibition of the 15 projects from this commission in September 2026 on the theme “Reinventing Photography”. To complement this exhibition, Hangar has decided to launch a call for applications open to Belgian artists photographers and/or artists photographers residing in Belgium . This call invites artists photographers to explore the same theme: 200 years later, how can photography be reinvented? Is photography a medium that reinvents itself? How do photographic artists, through their practice, keep contemporary photography alive? The call for applications will constitute the Belgian part of the exhibition.",photography,open call,Belgium,,Support for the production costs of the exhibition’s works. Cash prize of 4000€ for each of 5 laureates.,,,"As part of the bicentenary celebration (September 2026 to September 2027) of le Point de vue du gras* , considered the first photographic image in world history, the Centre national des arts plastiques (CNAP) in France has commissioned 15 photographers, focusing on the invention of photography and the relevance of its possible reinvention today. The projects are created using all the techniques that currently allow artists to produce photographic images in innovative forms. Hangar, one of the certified venues of the bicentenary celebration, will host the exhibition of the 15 projects from this commission in September 2026 on the theme “Reinventing Photography”. To complement this exhibition, Hangar has decided to launch a call for applications open to Belgian artists photographers and/or artists photographers residing in Belgium . This call invites artists photographers to explore the same theme: 200 years later, how can photography be reinvented? Is photography a medium that reinvents itself? How do photographic artists, through their practice, keep contemporary photography alive? The call for applications will constitute the Belgian part of the exhibition.",photography,open call,,Belgium,,['Photography'],['Open Call'],[],['Belgium'],"[{'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'support for production costs of the exhibition’s works'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 4000.0, 'amount_max': 4000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'cash prize for each of 5 laureates'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:31.817872+00:00,,,,,en,Open Call: Reinventing Photography by Hangar,"Conditions for participation being over the age of majority (18+) being a Belgian artist photographer and/or artists photographers residing in Belgium should demonstrate at least ONE of these two possibilities: – have a track record of professional practice as an artist (exhibitions, publications) – have an art school degree This call is open ONLY for original and unpublished projects / The works must be conceived, created, and produced specifically for this commission and presented for the first time at Hangar.",Open Call: Reinventing Photography by Hangar,"Conditions for participation being over the age of majority (18+) being a Belgian artist photographer and/or artists photographers residing in Belgium should demonstrate at least ONE of these two possibilities: – have a track record of professional practice as an artist (exhibitions, publications) – have an art school degree This call is open ONLY for original and unpublished projects / The works must be conceived, created, and produced specifically for this commission and presented for the first time at Hangar.",03 Oct 2025,2025-10-03,2026-09-23 12:37:25.473521+00:00
