If a foreign institution involves a guest curator from the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom in the project, then he or she has been professionally active as a curator in the field of contempora",Continuous,,2026-09-23 12:37:34.033163+00:00
mondriaan_fund_158a9874793c,mondriaan_fund,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/protected-cultural-heritage/,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/login/,Mondriaan Fund,"The Protected Cultural Heritage grant is intended for owners and managers of objects and collections that are registered as protected in the Register , within the meaning of the Heritage Act (Erfgoedwet).",cultural heritage,grant,Netherlands,,The Mondriaan Fund will finance up to 60% of the project.,,,"The Protected Cultural Heritage grant is intended for owners and managers of objects and collections that are registered as protected in the Register , within the meaning of the Heritage Act (Erfgoedwet).",cultural heritage,grant,,Netherlands,,['Cultural Heritage'],['Grant/Funding'],[],['Netherlands'],"[{'category': 'Other/Unspecified Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'up to 60% of the project'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:40.895505+00:00,,,,,en,Protected Cultural Heritage,"Applications must be submitted by the owners or managers of a protected object or protected collection. The application must concern an object or collection listed with the Register within the meaning of the Cultural Heritage Act. Constructional provisions, documentation of objects, and storage facilities are not eligible for a Protected Cultural Heritage grant. The applicant is expected to pay for a significant share of the expenses itself. If the application concerns an object which must be renovated or restored, it is expected that this object will be accessible to the public at certain regularly scheduled times of the week, without any need for an appointment. If the application concerns moveable industrial heritage, the renovation or restoration efforts must be designed to restore the object to an operational condition. The applicant must be able to prove that the preservation of the object is guaranteed in the long term due to proper constructional provisions, climate control and security measures. All applications must include a budget covering all expenses which complies with the Mondriaan Fund’s guidelines.",Protected Cultural Heritage,"Applications must be submitted by the owners or managers of a protected object or protected collection. The application must concern an object or collection listed with the Register within the meaning of the Cultural Heritage Act. Constructional provisions, documentation of objects, and storage facilities are not eligible for a Protected Cultural Heritage grant. The applicant is expected to pay for a significant share of the expenses itself. If the application concerns an object which must be renovated or restored, it is expected that this object will be accessible to the public at certain regularly scheduled times of the week, without any need for an appointment. If the application concerns moveable industrial heritage, the renovation or restoration efforts must be designed to restore the object to an operational condition. The applicant must be able to prove that the preservation of the object is guaranteed in the long term due to proper constructional provisions, climate control and security measures. All applications must include a budget covering all expenses which complies with the Mondriaan Fund’s guidelines.",Continuous,,2026-09-23 12:37:34.033496+00:00
mondriaan_fund_af60247339cd,mondriaan_fund,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/voucher-artisan/,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/login/,Mondriaan Fund,Are you a visual artist and do you want to hire an artisan for your research or the production of your work? You may be eligible for the Voucher Artisan.,visual arts,grant,The Netherlands and the Caribbean part of the Kingdom of the Netherlands,,"A maximum of € 8,000.",,,Are you a visual artist and do you want to hire an artisan for your research or the production of your work? You may be eligible for the Voucher Artisan.,visual arts,grant,,The Netherlands and the Caribbean part of the Kingdom of the Netherlands,,['Visual Arts'],['Grant/Funding'],[],['Netherlands'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 8000.0, 'amount_max': 8000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': None}]",2026-09-24 08:57:40.895543+00:00,,,,,en,Voucher Artisan,"Visual artists from the Netherlands and the Caribbean part of the Kingdom of the Netherlands.

Applications may only be submitted by artists who have been active as a professional visual artist for at least 1 year: If you have completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on your diploma will be considered the start of your professional practice. If there is an interim period between your graduation from the Bachelor’s programme with a visual arts curriculum and the start of your Master’s programme, this period will count as part of your professional practice. If you have not completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on which you first presented work in professional art circles will be considered the start of your professional practice. In order to be eligible for support, you must be artistically active within the visual arts field, and in this capacity, part of the professional visual arts practice in the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. You cannot apply for or use a contribution while enrolled to study at educational institutions for e.g. Bachelor’s, Master’s or postdoctoral programmes. This also applies to participation in programmes at postgraduate institutions, and to PhD programmes. The exception is part-time programmes (not Bachelor’s programmes) of less than 20 hours a week. Artisans live in the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom of the Netherlands, and have been working as a professional artisan for at least one year. The Mondriaan Fund considers an artisan to be: Someone who is active in the production, transformation, repair or restoration of objects, who offers services related to manual aspects, whose activities have an authentic character, and who develops knowledge focused on quality, tradition, creation or innovation. The Mondriaan Fund considers Artisan(al) to be more specific than the terms craftsmanship or craftsperson, which solely focus on capably practising a profession. The board may decide not to accept an application if it is of the opinion that the artisan fails to satisfy the above definition. At the heart of this voucher is the exchange between artist and artisan, specifically to preserve, pass on or further develop an artisan from the original tradition. Project plan The Artisan Voucher can only be used to cover payment of the artisan. The application should therefore be supported by a quotation from the artisan. Applications for the Artisan Voucher made during the term of any other financial support from the Mondriaan Fund will not be accepted in the case that the board is of the opinion that the contribution covers the same expenses. Applications for support for regular production expenses such as framing, web design, sound effects and assembly will not be accepted.",Voucher Artisan,"Visual artists from the Netherlands and the Caribbean part of the Kingdom of the Netherlands.

Applications may only be submitted by artists who have been active as a professional visual artist for at least 1 year: If you have completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on your diploma will be considered the start of your professional practice. If there is an interim period between your graduation from the Bachelor’s programme with a visual arts curriculum and the start of your Master’s programme, this period will count as part of your professional practice. If you have not completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on which you first presented work in professional art circles will be considered the start of your professional practice. In order to be eligible for support, you must be artistically active within the visual arts field, and in this capacity, part of the professional visual arts practice in the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. You cannot apply for or use a contribution while enrolled to study at educational institutions for e.g. Bachelor’s, Master’s or postdoctoral programmes. This also applies to participation in programmes at postgraduate institutions, and to PhD programmes. The exception is part-time programmes (not Bachelor’s programmes) of less than 20 hours a week. Artisans live in the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom of the Netherlands, and have been working as a professional artisan for at least one year. The Mondriaan Fund considers an artisan to be: Someone who is active in the production, transformation, repair or restoration of objects, who offers services related to manual aspects, whose activities have an authentic character, and who develops knowledge focused on quality, tradition, creation or innovation. The Mondriaan Fund considers Artisan(al) to be more specific than the terms craftsmanship or craftsperson, which solely focus on capably practising a profession. The board may decide not to accept an application if it is of the opinion that the artisan fails to satisfy the above definition. At the heart of this voucher is the exchange between artist and artisan, specifically to preserve, pass on or further develop an artisan from the original tradition. Project plan The Artisan Voucher can only be used to cover payment of the artisan. The application should therefore be supported by a quotation from the artisan. Applications for the Artisan Voucher made during the term of any other financial support from the Mondriaan Fund will not be accepted in the case that the board is of the opinion that the contribution covers the same expenses. Applications for support for regular production expenses such as framing, web design, sound effects and assembly will not be accepted.",Continuous,,2026-09-23 12:37:34.033856+00:00
mondriaan_fund_b4f100323dba,mondriaan_fund,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/voucher-artist-with-child/,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/login/,Mondriaan Fund,"Are you a visual artist with the responsibility of caring for a child who is not yet of compulsory school age, and do you have to make additional costs to care for your child(ren), for example through the participation in a residency or in the construction phase of an exhibition? You may be eligible for the Artist with Child Voucher.",visual arts,voucher,the Netherlands and the Caribbean part of the Kingdom,,"A maximum of €2,500.",,professional visual artist for at least 1 year,"Are you a visual artist with the responsibility of caring for a child who is not yet of compulsory school age, and do you have to make additional costs to care for your child(ren), for example through the participation in a residency or in the construction phase of an exhibition? You may be eligible for the Artist with Child Voucher.",visual arts,voucher,professional visual artist for at least 1 year,the Netherlands and the Caribbean part of the Kingdom,,['Visual Arts'],['Grant/Funding'],['Established/Professional'],['Netherlands'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 2500.0, 'amount_max': 2500.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': None}]",2026-09-24 08:57:40.895587+00:00,,,,,en,Voucher Artist with Child,"Visual artists from the Netherlands and the Caribbean part of the Kingdom with the responsibility to care for children who are not yet of compulsory school age. NB in the Caribbean part of the Kingdom this applies to children up to 4 years old and in the Netherlands to children up to 5 years old.

Applications may only be submitted by artists who have been active as a professional visual artist for at least 1 year: If you have completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on your diploma will be considered the start of your professional practice. If there is an interim period between your graduation from the Bachelor’s programme with a visual arts curriculum and the start of your Master’s programme, this period will count as part of your professional practice. If you have not completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on which you first presented work in professional art circles will be considered the start of your professional practice. In order to be eligible for support, you must be artistically active within the visual arts field, and in this capacity, part of the professional visual arts practice in the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. You cannot apply for or use a contribution while enrolled to study at educational institutions for e.g. Bachelor’s, Master’s or postdoctoral programmes. This also applies to participation in programmes at postgraduate institutions, and to PhD programmes. The exception is part-time programmes (not Bachelor’s programmes) of less than 20 hours a week.

The Artist with Child Voucher can only be applied for in the case of one-off, temporary and additional care/travel and/or accommodation costs for a child who is not yet of compulsory school age and for whom the applicant is responsible. These costs arise as a result of a multi-day activity of a temporary nature, such as a residency period or construction phase of an exhibition. This must be evident from a registration, commitment or invitation from the institution where the multi-day activity takes place and financial proof such as an agreement and invoice from the childcare agency or the babysitter. NB: if you hire non-professional childcare, such as a family member or someone from your own personal circle, the Mondriaan Fund charges an hourly rate of €10.25 excluding VAT with a maximum of 8 hours per day. The Artist with Child Voucher cannot be applied for during the term of another financial grant from the Mondriaan Fund if the fund board is of the opinion that the contribution covers the same costs. The Artist with Child Voucher cannot be requested for (extra) hours at the Daycare with which a permanent agreement has already been made. The Artist with Child Voucher can be awarded a maximum of 3 times per 12 months, provided that the multi-day activities for which the applications have been requested are separate. It is not possible to request multiple vouchers for costs incurred as a result of the same activity. An Artist with Child Voucher cannot be requested again for additional extra costs that arise as a result of a multi-day activity for which a Voucher has been requested.",Voucher Artist with Child,"Visual artists from the Netherlands and the Caribbean part of the Kingdom with the responsibility to care for children who are not yet of compulsory school age. NB in the Caribbean part of the Kingdom this applies to children up to 4 years old and in the Netherlands to children up to 5 years old.

Applications may only be submitted by artists who have been active as a professional visual artist for at least 1 year: If you have completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on your diploma will be considered the start of your professional practice. If there is an interim period between your graduation from the Bachelor’s programme with a visual arts curriculum and the start of your Master’s programme, this period will count as part of your professional practice. If you have not completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on which you first presented work in professional art circles will be considered the start of your professional practice. In order to be eligible for support, you must be artistically active within the visual arts field, and in this capacity, part of the professional visual arts practice in the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. You cannot apply for or use a contribution while enrolled to study at educational institutions for e.g. Bachelor’s, Master’s or postdoctoral programmes. This also applies to participation in programmes at postgraduate institutions, and to PhD programmes. The exception is part-time programmes (not Bachelor’s programmes) of less than 20 hours a week.

The Artist with Child Voucher can only be applied for in the case of one-off, temporary and additional care/travel and/or accommodation costs for a child who is not yet of compulsory school age and for whom the applicant is responsible. These costs arise as a result of a multi-day activity of a temporary nature, such as a residency period or construction phase of an exhibition. This must be evident from a registration, commitment or invitation from the institution where the multi-day activity takes place and financial proof such as an agreement and invoice from the childcare agency or the babysitter. NB: if you hire non-professional childcare, such as a family member or someone from your own personal circle, the Mondriaan Fund charges an hourly rate of €10.25 excluding VAT with a maximum of 8 hours per day. The Artist with Child Voucher cannot be applied for during the term of another financial grant from the Mondriaan Fund if the fund board is of the opinion that the contribution covers the same costs. The Artist with Child Voucher cannot be requested for (extra) hours at the Daycare with which a permanent agreement has already been made. The Artist with Child Voucher can be awarded a maximum of 3 times per 12 months, provided that the multi-day activities for which the applications have been requested are separate. It is not possible to request multiple vouchers for costs incurred as a result of the same activity. An Artist with Child Voucher cannot be requested again for additional extra costs that arise as a result of a multi-day activity for which a Voucher has been requested.",Continuous,,2026-09-23 12:37:34.034206+00:00
