mondriaan_fund_e52bef22781c,mondriaan_fund,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/voucher-international/,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/login/,Mondriaan Fund,"Are you a visual artist, curator or art observer who is keen to quickly respond to an invitation to participate in a public programme outside of the Netherlands? Voucher International may be able to help.",visual arts,grant,The Netherlands and the Caribbean part of the Kingdom,,"Travel and accommodation costs up to a maximum sum of € 2,500.",,,"Are you a visual artist, curator or art observer who is keen to quickly respond to an invitation to participate in a public programme outside of the Netherlands? Voucher International may be able to help.",visual arts,grant,,The Netherlands and the Caribbean part of the Kingdom,,['Visual Arts'],['Grant/Funding'],[],['Netherlands'],"[{'category': 'Travel Support', 'amount_min': 2500.0, 'amount_max': 2500.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'travel and accommodation costs combined'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:40.895675+00:00,,,,,en,Voucher International,"Visual artists, independent curators, art critics and art observers based in the Netherlands and the Caribbean part of the Kingdom.

The activity associated with the application is part of a publicly accessible programme, such as a lecture, performance, book presentation or participation on a panel. The artist, curator or art observer has received an invitation from a contemporary visual art institution, venue, festival or symposium outside of the Netherlands with demonstrable and internationally recognised programming in the field of contemporary visual art. The invitation shows that the institution, venue, festival or symposium is offering the artist, curator or art observer a realistic fee for their participation in the public programme.

Voucher International can be awarded no more than twice per applicant within a 12-month period.

For artists: You must have been working as a professional visual artist for at least 1 year: If you have completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on your diploma will be considered the start of your professional practice. If there is an interim period between your graduation from the Bachelor’s programme with a visual arts curriculum and the start of your Master’s programme, this period will be considered as part of your professional practice. If you have not completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on which you first presented work in professional art circles will be considered the start of your professional practice. In order to be eligible for a contribution, you must be artistically and substantively active within the visual arts field, and in this capacity, part of the professional art practice in the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. You may not apply for the Voucher International contribution while studying at educational institutions for e.g. Bachelor’s, Master’s or postdoctoral programmes. This also applies to participation in programmes at postgraduate institutions. In the case that a visual artist studies part-time (not a Bachelor’s degree programme) for less than 20 hours a week, a grant may be awarded if: the applicant has been professionally active as an artist for at least 3 years, or has attended a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) at a visual arts educational institution for at least 3 years and has subsequently been professionally active as an artist for at least 1 year.

For curators, critics and art observers: You have been working as a professional curator, art critic or art observer in the field of visual art for at least 2 years, and can support this with publications, exhibitions, research and/or projects. You may not apply for the Voucher International contribution while studying at educational institutions for e.g. Bachelor’s, Master’s or postdoctoral programmes. This also applies to participation in programmes at postgraduate institutions. In order to be eligible for a contribution, you must be artistically and substantively active within the visual arts field, and in this capacity, part of the professional art practice in the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. For curators and art observers, the activity associated with the application must be part of their independent practice.",Voucher International,"Visual artists, independent curators, art critics and art observers based in the Netherlands and the Caribbean part of the Kingdom.

The activity associated with the application is part of a publicly accessible programme, such as a lecture, performance, book presentation or participation on a panel. The artist, curator or art observer has received an invitation from a contemporary visual art institution, venue, festival or symposium outside of the Netherlands with demonstrable and internationally recognised programming in the field of contemporary visual art. The invitation shows that the institution, venue, festival or symposium is offering the artist, curator or art observer a realistic fee for their participation in the public programme.

Voucher International can be awarded no more than twice per applicant within a 12-month period.

For artists: You must have been working as a professional visual artist for at least 1 year: If you have completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on your diploma will be considered the start of your professional practice. If there is an interim period between your graduation from the Bachelor’s programme with a visual arts curriculum and the start of your Master’s programme, this period will be considered as part of your professional practice. If you have not completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on which you first presented work in professional art circles will be considered the start of your professional practice. In order to be eligible for a contribution, you must be artistically and substantively active within the visual arts field, and in this capacity, part of the professional art practice in the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. You may not apply for the Voucher International contribution while studying at educational institutions for e.g. Bachelor’s, Master’s or postdoctoral programmes. This also applies to participation in programmes at postgraduate institutions. In the case that a visual artist studies part-time (not a Bachelor’s degree programme) for less than 20 hours a week, a grant may be awarded if: the applicant has been professionally active as an artist for at least 3 years, or has attended a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) at a visual arts educational institution for at least 3 years and has subsequently been professionally active as an artist for at least 1 year.

For curators, critics and art observers: You have been working as a professional curator, art critic or art observer in the field of visual art for at least 2 years, and can support this with publications, exhibitions, research and/or projects. You may not apply for the Voucher International contribution while studying at educational institutions for e.g. Bachelor’s, Master’s or postdoctoral programmes. This also applies to participation in programmes at postgraduate institutions. In order to be eligible for a contribution, you must be artistically and substantively active within the visual arts field, and in this capacity, part of the professional art practice in the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. For curators and art observers, the activity associated with the application must be part of their independent practice.",Continuous,,2026-09-23 12:37:34.034892+00:00
mondriaan_fund_2f611a04d139,mondriaan_fund,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/art-media/,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/login/,Mondriaan Fund,The Mondriaan Fund offers the Art Media grant to stimulate engagement with and the discourse of contemporary visual art in the Netherlands and the Caribbean part of the Kingdom.,visual art,grant,Netherlands,,"The maximum grant offered by the Mondriaan Fund is 70% of the eligible expenses. The available budget per meeting is € 229,000. ... The standard grant is € 2,480 per month.",,,The Mondriaan Fund offers the Art Media grant to stimulate engagement with and the discourse of contemporary visual art in the Netherlands and the Caribbean part of the Kingdom.,visual art,grant,,Netherlands,,['Visual Arts'],['Grant/Funding'],[],['Netherlands'],"[{'category': 'Other/Unspecified Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'up to 70% of eligible expenses'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 2480.0, 'amount_max': 2480.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'per month', 'note': 'standard grant'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:40.895815+00:00,,,,,en,Art Media,"For platforms such as (online) magazines and other public media, and individuals working as curators, critics, social content creators or journalists. New initiatives and collaborations may also apply. The planned publication must be accessible on at least one public medium or platform with appropriate reach. It is not possible to apply for a grant for regular activities, e.g.: continuing a project that was previously supported by the Fund, such as a new season of an existing (podcast) series. activities that are not distinctly recognisable as a separate project in terms of form and/or substance, such as a column with a new subject, but using a customary method. for individuals who, in addition to working as a visual artist, are also active as a curator, critic, social content creator or journalist, the project for which funding is being requested must clearly form part of their reflective practice, rather than their (regular) artistic practice. Museums, art institutions and heritage institutions can only apply for a grant for individual productions concerning visual art. The project may not be directly linked to the applicant’s existing activities (e.g. an article or publication accompanying an exhibition). It is not possible to apply for a grant for television or film productions. It is not possible to apply for a grant for making profiles or portraits of artists. The applicant is expected to comply with the requirements regarding Fair Pay. Other parties working on the project who are included in the budget therefore must also receive remuneration in line with the applicable collective labour agreements or guidelines.",Art Media,"For platforms such as (online) magazines and other public media, and individuals working as curators, critics, social content creators or journalists. New initiatives and collaborations may also apply. The planned publication must be accessible on at least one public medium or platform with appropriate reach. It is not possible to apply for a grant for regular activities, e.g.: continuing a project that was previously supported by the Fund, such as a new season of an existing (podcast) series. activities that are not distinctly recognisable as a separate project in terms of form and/or substance, such as a column with a new subject, but using a customary method. for individuals who, in addition to working as a visual artist, are also active as a curator, critic, social content creator or journalist, the project for which funding is being requested must clearly form part of their reflective practice, rather than their (regular) artistic practice. Museums, art institutions and heritage institutions can only apply for a grant for individual productions concerning visual art. The project may not be directly linked to the applicant’s existing activities (e.g. an article or publication accompanying an exhibition). It is not possible to apply for a grant for television or film productions. It is not possible to apply for a grant for making profiles or portraits of artists. The applicant is expected to comply with the requirements regarding Fair Pay. Other parties working on the project who are included in the budget therefore must also receive remuneration in line with the applicable collective labour agreements or guidelines.",15.10.2026,2026-10-15,2026-09-23 12:37:34.037408+00:00
nordic_culture_point_8b3a1cf01146,nordic_culture_point,https://www.nkk.org/en/norden-0-30-grant-programme/,https://applicant.nordiskkulturkontakt.org/,The Nordic Committee for Children and Young People,"Norden 0–30 supports Nordic co-operation projects aimed at children and young people up to the age of 30. The projects may relate to culture, social issues and/or politics. The programme has been established by the Nordic Committee for Children and Young People , which advises on and coordinates work relating to children and young people within the Nordic Council of Ministers. Through Norden 0–30, the committee aims to support projects initiated by children and young people themselves that strengthen their participation and influence in political, cultural and social activities.","culture, social issues and/or politics",grant programme,Nordic Region,,"For co-operation between three or more Nordic countries, you may apply for up to EUR 50,000. For co-operation between two Nordic countries, you may apply for up to EUR 10,000.",,,"Norden 0–30 supports Nordic co-operation projects aimed at children and young people up to the age of 30. The projects may relate to culture, social issues and/or politics. The programme has been established by the Nordic Committee for Children and Young People , which advises on and coordinates work relating to children and young people within the Nordic Council of Ministers. Through Norden 0–30, the committee aims to support projects initiated by children and young people themselves that strengthen their participation and influence in political, cultural and social activities.","culture, social issues and/or politics",grant programme,,Nordic Region,,['Other/Non-Arts'],['Grant/Funding'],[],"['Denmark', 'Finland', 'Iceland', 'Norway', 'Sweden']","[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 10000.0, 'amount_max': 50000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'different caps for co-operation between two Nordic countries versus three or more Nordic countries'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:40.895866+00:00,,,,,en,Norden 0–30 grant programme,"Funding can be granted to: organisations local authorities institutions associations networks. You must have corporate identity number in order to apply. The lead applicant must be based in the Nordic Region. The applicant does not need to be a young person but must represent an organisation that either consists of, or has experience of involving, children and young people. Projects must also involve co-operation between two or more Nordic countries. For projects involving two Nordic countries, one of the participating countries must be Greenland, Iceland, the Faroe Islands, or Åland. At least three participating countries must be Nordic countries in projects in which three or more countries are participating. Denmark, the Faroe Islands, Finland, Greenland, Iceland, Norway, Sweden, and Åland are considered as separate countries. Co-operation with organisations from Greenland, the Faroe Islands, Åland, or Sápmi is considered particularly valuable. Only Nordic project partners count towards the minimum partnership requirement. The partner is considered to represent the country or area in which the organisation is registered. A partner organisation is considered to represent the country or territory in which it is registered. Organisations and/or participants from the Baltic countries may take part in both the application and the project’s activities. Please note that the programme is not open to: individuals sports organisations organisations or networks that neither consist of nor have experience of inclusive work with children and young people organisations or networks that are not based in the Nordic countries.",Norden 0–30 grant programme,"Funding can be granted to: organisations local authorities institutions associations networks. You must have corporate identity number in order to apply. The lead applicant must be based in the Nordic Region. The applicant does not need to be a young person but must represent an organisation that either consists of, or has experience of involving, children and young people. Projects must also involve co-operation between two or more Nordic countries. For projects involving two Nordic countries, one of the participating countries must be Greenland, Iceland, the Faroe Islands, or Åland. At least three participating countries must be Nordic countries in projects in which three or more countries are participating. Denmark, the Faroe Islands, Finland, Greenland, Iceland, Norway, Sweden, and Åland are considered as separate countries. Co-operation with organisations from Greenland, the Faroe Islands, Åland, or Sápmi is considered particularly valuable. Only Nordic project partners count towards the minimum partnership requirement. The partner is considered to represent the country or area in which the organisation is registered. A partner organisation is considered to represent the country or territory in which it is registered. Organisations and/or participants from the Baltic countries may take part in both the application and the project’s activities. Please note that the programme is not open to: individuals sports organisations organisations or networks that neither consist of nor have experience of inclusive work with children and young people organisations or networks that are not based in the Nordic countries.",02.10.2026 15:59 (UTC +3),2026-09-24,2026-09-23 12:37:34.059155+00:00
nordic_culture_point_98a22945e2cb,nordic_culture_point,https://www.nkk.org/en/culture-and-art-programme/,https://applicant.nordiskkulturkontakt.org/,Nordic Culture Point,"The programme funds all phases of art and culture projects: preparatory work, production, performance, and dissemination. Funding is available for projects that produce art, culture, and other forms of creativity, as well as to organise and run skills enhancement projects in the fields of art and culture.",art and culture,funding,Nordic Region,,"A project can be granted up to EUR 7,000 without other sources of funding up to EUR 40 000 with at least 30% co-funding up to EUR 100 000 with at least 50% co-funding",,,"The programme funds all phases of art and culture projects: preparatory work, production, performance, and dissemination. Funding is available for projects that produce art, culture, and other forms of creativity, as well as to organise and run skills enhancement projects in the fields of art and culture.",art and culture,funding,,Nordic Region,,['Multidisciplinary'],['Grant/Funding'],[],"['Denmark', 'Finland', 'Iceland', 'Norway', 'Sweden']","[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 7000.0, 'amount_max': 100000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'tiers depend on co-funding: up to 7,000 with no other funding; up to 40,000 with at least 30% co-funding; up to 100,000 with at least 50% co-funding'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:40.895910+00:00,,,,,en,Culture and Art Programme,"Anyone within the field of art and culture can apply, as long as the project meets the programme criteria and is realised by way of co-operation with partners from at least three countries, at least two of which must be Nordic. In this context, Norway, Denmark, Sweden, Iceland, Finland, Åland, the Faroe Islands and Greenland are considered as Nordic countries. Country affiliation is assessed according to the partners’ registered addresses, not nationality. The person submitting the application does not need to be resident in the Nordic Region, as long as the Nordic dimension of the project is met in terms of its partners and content. Example: An applicant from Lithuania or Canada can submit an application for a collaborative project if there are also partners from Finland and Åland.",Culture and Art Programme,"Anyone within the field of art and culture can apply, as long as the project meets the programme criteria and is realised by way of co-operation with partners from at least three countries, at least two of which must be Nordic. In this context, Norway, Denmark, Sweden, Iceland, Finland, Åland, the Faroe Islands and Greenland are considered as Nordic countries. Country affiliation is assessed according to the partners’ registered addresses, not nationality. The person submitting the application does not need to be resident in the Nordic Region, as long as the Nordic dimension of the project is met in terms of its partners and content. Example: An applicant from Lithuania or Canada can submit an application for a collaborative project if there are also partners from Finland and Åland.",Active Next year – the application dates will be published in November,2027-09-24,2026-09-23 12:37:34.065176+00:00
nordic_culture_point_9dc9950cca03,nordic_culture_point,https://www.nkk.org/en/demos/,https://applicant.nordiskkulturkontakt.org/,Nordic Culture Point,"The aim with Demos is to facilitate networks and meetings between civil society organisations in the Nordics. A strong and dynamic civil society is a cornerstone of Nordic democracy. The funding programme promotes the ability of stakeholders in Nordic civil society to work together, to influence, and to strengthen their voice. The partnerships will help the Nordic Region on its way to becoming the most sustainable and integrated region in the world by 2030.",all areas of society,funding programme,Nordic Region,,"A project can be granted a maximum of EUR 50,000 in funding from Demos.",,,"The aim with Demos is to facilitate networks and meetings between civil society organisations in the Nordics. A strong and dynamic civil society is a cornerstone of Nordic democracy. The funding programme promotes the ability of stakeholders in Nordic civil society to work together, to influence, and to strengthen their voice. The partnerships will help the Nordic Region on its way to becoming the most sustainable and integrated region in the world by 2030.",all areas of society,funding programme,,Nordic Region,,['Other/Non-Arts'],['Grant/Funding'],[],"['Denmark', 'Finland', 'Iceland', 'Norway', 'Sweden']","[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 50000.0, 'amount_max': 50000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'maximum funding from Demos'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:40.895990+00:00,,,,,en,Demos,"Please note that only civil society organisations can apply for funding.

Funding can be applied for by non-profit civil society organisations in all areas of society . These organisations include associations, foundations, charities, citizens organisations, interest groups, labour market organisations, religious communities, social enterprises, and NGOs. Demos funds projects with participation from at least three (3) different Nordic countries. Denmark, the Faroe Islands, Finland, Greenland, Iceland, Norway, Sweden, and Åland are considered as separate countries in this context. To be eligible, the applicant organisation must be established and registered in the Nordic Region. Denmark, the Faroe Islands, Finland, Greenland, Iceland, Norway, Sweden, and Åland are considered as Nordic countries in this context. Although the project may cover additional partners who do not operate in the Nordic Region, at least three Nordic countries must be represented. The partner is considered to represent the country or area in which the organisation is registered. The organisation and partners must have a democratic structure and operations. The organisation and partners must not pursue making a profit. The organisation must not owe taxes or fees to the state and must not have applied for bankruptcy or be in liquidation. Please note that individuals cannot apply for funding.",Demos,"Please note that only civil society organisations can apply for funding.

Funding can be applied for by non-profit civil society organisations in all areas of society . These organisations include associations, foundations, charities, citizens organisations, interest groups, labour market organisations, religious communities, social enterprises, and NGOs. Demos funds projects with participation from at least three (3) different Nordic countries. Denmark, the Faroe Islands, Finland, Greenland, Iceland, Norway, Sweden, and Åland are considered as separate countries in this context. To be eligible, the applicant organisation must be established and registered in the Nordic Region. Denmark, the Faroe Islands, Finland, Greenland, Iceland, Norway, Sweden, and Åland are considered as Nordic countries in this context. Although the project may cover additional partners who do not operate in the Nordic Region, at least three Nordic countries must be represented. The partner is considered to represent the country or area in which the organisation is registered. The organisation and partners must have a democratic structure and operations. The organisation and partners must not pursue making a profit. The organisation must not owe taxes or fees to the state and must not have applied for bankruptcy or be in liquidation. Please note that individuals cannot apply for funding.",Next year – the application dates will be published in November,2027-09-24,2026-09-23 12:37:34.071660+00:00
nordic_culture_point_c76ae887354b,nordic_culture_point,https://www.nkk.org/en/funding-for-artist-residencies/,https://applicant.nordiskkulturkontakt.org/,Nordic–Baltic Mobility Programme for Culture,"Funding for artist residencies is part of the Nordic–Baltic Mobility Programme for Culture, which promotes artistic and cultural co-operation across the Nordic and Baltic regions.",all areas of art and culture,funding,"Nordic Region (Denmark, Finland, the Faroe Islands, Greenland, Iceland, Norway, Sweden, Åland) or the Baltic countries (Estonia, Latvia, Lithuania)",,"Funding for artist residencies can amount to EUR 50,000.",,,"Funding for artist residencies is part of the Nordic–Baltic Mobility Programme for Culture, which promotes artistic and cultural co-operation across the Nordic and Baltic regions.",all areas of art and culture,funding,,"Nordic Region (Denmark, Finland, the Faroe Islands, Greenland, Iceland, Norway, Sweden, Åland) or the Baltic countries (Estonia, Latvia, Lithuania)",,['Multidisciplinary'],['Grant/Funding'],[],"['Denmark', 'Finland', 'Faroe Islands', 'Greenland', 'Iceland', 'Norway', 'Sweden', 'Åland Islands', 'Estonia', 'Latvia', 'Lithuania']","[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 50000.0, 'amount_max': 50000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'for artist residencies'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:40.896014+00:00,,,,,en,Funding for artist residencies,"Funding is available to established residency centres, organisations, and institutions with at least one year’s documented experience of organising artist residencies within the arts and cultural sector. Residency centres applying for funding must be located in the Nordic Region (Denmark, Finland, the Faroe Islands, Greenland, Iceland, Norway, Sweden, Åland) or the Baltic countries (Estonia, Latvia, Lithuania) and the invited artists must have a permanent address in one of these countries. However, they do not need to be a Nordic or Baltic citizen. Individual practitioners of art and culture cannot get funding for artist residencies.",Funding for artist residencies,"Funding is available to established residency centres, organisations, and institutions with at least one year’s documented experience of organising artist residencies within the arts and cultural sector. Residency centres applying for funding must be located in the Nordic Region (Denmark, Finland, the Faroe Islands, Greenland, Iceland, Norway, Sweden, Åland) or the Baltic countries (Estonia, Latvia, Lithuania) and the invited artists must have a permanent address in one of these countries. However, they do not need to be a Nordic or Baltic citizen. Individual practitioners of art and culture cannot get funding for artist residencies.","15:59, Finnish time.",2026-09-24,2026-09-23 12:37:34.074308+00:00
nordic_culture_point_8e6618f7a6eb,nordic_culture_point,https://www.nkk.org/en/long-term-network-funding/,https://applicant.nordiskkulturkontakt.org/,Nordic Culture Point,"Long-term network funding is part of the Nordic–Baltic Mobility Programme for Culture, which promotes artistic and cultural co-operation across the Nordic and Baltic regions. The focus of the programme is on increasing the exchange of knowledge, contacts, and interest in Nordic and Baltic art and culture.",all forms of art and culture,funding,"Nordic Region (Denmark, Finland, the Faroe Islands, Greenland, Iceland, Norway, Sweden, or Åland) or the Baltic countries (Estonia, Latvia, or Lithuania)",,"Networks planning to co-operate for up to three years may apply for funding of up to EUR 100,000. The requested funding may cover a maximum of 50% of the total project budget.",,professional artists or cultural practitioners,"Long-term network funding is part of the Nordic–Baltic Mobility Programme for Culture, which promotes artistic and cultural co-operation across the Nordic and Baltic regions. The focus of the programme is on increasing the exchange of knowledge, contacts, and interest in Nordic and Baltic art and culture.",all forms of art and culture,funding,professional artists or cultural practitioners,"Nordic Region (Denmark, Finland, the Faroe Islands, Greenland, Iceland, Norway, Sweden, or Åland) or the Baltic countries (Estonia, Latvia, or Lithuania)",,['Multidisciplinary'],['Grant/Funding'],['Established/Professional'],"['Denmark', 'Finland', 'Faroe Islands', 'Greenland', 'Iceland', 'Norway', 'Sweden', 'Åland Islands', 'Estonia', 'Latvia', 'Lithuania']","[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 100000.0, 'amount_max': 100000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'up to three years; maximum 50% of total project budget'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:40.896038+00:00,,,,,en,Long-term network funding,"Funding is available for groups of at least three organisations and/or professional artists or cultural practitioners (such as curators, producers, literary translators, cultural editors or researchers) in all forms of art and culture. It is assumed that you have confirmed such collaboration with the network partners before submitting your application. “Professional” means that there is documented experience of work in the field of art and culture and/or training in art or culture. To apply for network funding, you must be a resident of the Nordic Region (Denmark, Finland, the Faroe Islands, Greenland, Iceland, Norway, Sweden, or Åland) or the Baltic countries (Estonia, Latvia, or Lithuania), although you do not need to be a Nordic or Baltic citizen. The network must consist of partners from: at least three Nordic and/or Baltic countries (Denmark, Estonia, Finland, the Faroe Islands, Greenland, Iceland, Latvia, Lithuania, Norway, Sweden, and Åland.) The network may cover additional partners who do not operate in the Nordic or Baltic region.",Long-term network funding,"Funding is available for groups of at least three organisations and/or professional artists or cultural practitioners (such as curators, producers, literary translators, cultural editors or researchers) in all forms of art and culture. It is assumed that you have confirmed such collaboration with the network partners before submitting your application. “Professional” means that there is documented experience of work in the field of art and culture and/or training in art or culture. To apply for network funding, you must be a resident of the Nordic Region (Denmark, Finland, the Faroe Islands, Greenland, Iceland, Norway, Sweden, or Åland) or the Baltic countries (Estonia, Latvia, or Lithuania), although you do not need to be a Nordic or Baltic citizen. The network must consist of partners from: at least three Nordic and/or Baltic countries (Denmark, Estonia, Finland, the Faroe Islands, Greenland, Iceland, Latvia, Lithuania, Norway, Sweden, and Åland.) The network may cover additional partners who do not operate in the Nordic or Baltic region.","15:59, Finnish time",2026-09-24,2026-09-23 12:37:34.077618+00:00
nordic_culture_point_68739869a8ce,nordic_culture_point,https://www.nkk.org/en/mobility-funding/,https://applicant.nordiskkulturkontakt.org/,Nordic Culture Point,"Mobility funding gives individual applicants access to contacts, expertise and knowledge from different parts of the region. Funding can also be used to present art and culture productions and to raise interest in Nordic and Baltic art and culture.",all forms of art and culture,funding,"Denmark, Estonia, Finland, the Faroe Islands, Greenland, Iceland, Latvia, Lithuania, Norway, Sweden and Åland",,Funding is based on a fixed travel cost and/or a fixed allowance per day which is calculated according to the length of the stay and destination.,,professional artists and cultural practitioners,"Mobility funding gives individual applicants access to contacts, expertise and knowledge from different parts of the region. Funding can also be used to present art and culture productions and to raise interest in Nordic and Baltic art and culture.",all forms of art and culture,funding,professional artists and cultural practitioners,"Denmark, Estonia, Finland, the Faroe Islands, Greenland, Iceland, Latvia, Lithuania, Norway, Sweden and Åland",,['Multidisciplinary'],['Grant/Funding'],['Established/Professional'],"['Denmark', 'Estonia', 'Finland', 'Faroe Islands', 'Greenland', 'Iceland', 'Latvia', 'Lithuania', 'Norway', 'Sweden', 'Åland Islands']","[{'category': 'Travel Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'fixed travel cost and/or fixed allowance per day based on length of stay and destination'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:40.896079+00:00,,,,,en,Mobility funding,"Funding is available for professional artists and cultural practitioners (such as curators, producers, literary translators, cultural editors or researchers) in all forms of art and culture. “Professional” means that there is documented experience of work in the field of art and culture and/or training in art or culture. Mobility funding can only be granted to individuals. You cannot apply on behalf of another person, i.e. organisations cannot apply for funding to invite artists. If you apply as part of a group traveling together within the framework of the same project, all group members must submit individual applications. The user account that you create in our application system must be for an individual applicant in order to apply for mobility funding. To be able to apply for mobility funding, the applicant must be a resident of the Nordic Region (Denmark, Finland, the Faroe Islands, Greenland, Iceland, Norway, Sweden, Åland) or the Baltic countries (Estonia, Latvia, or Lithuania), although the applicant does not have to be a Nordic or Baltic citizen. Students are not granted mobility funding. However, professional artists and cultural practitioners can apply for funding in some cases, if the purpose of the trip is not linked to studies, but is part of the artist’s continued professional work. Trips within one and the same country/area Trips to or from countries outside the Nordic/Baltic region Trips which are a part of the applicant’s formal studies Organisational or company travel Official travel for employees in public administration – e.g. state authorities, municipalities, regions or the equivalent. Activities that have already been carried out.",Mobility funding,"Funding is available for professional artists and cultural practitioners (such as curators, producers, literary translators, cultural editors or researchers) in all forms of art and culture. “Professional” means that there is documented experience of work in the field of art and culture and/or training in art or culture. Mobility funding can only be granted to individuals. You cannot apply on behalf of another person, i.e. organisations cannot apply for funding to invite artists. If you apply as part of a group traveling together within the framework of the same project, all group members must submit individual applications. The user account that you create in our application system must be for an individual applicant in order to apply for mobility funding. To be able to apply for mobility funding, the applicant must be a resident of the Nordic Region (Denmark, Finland, the Faroe Islands, Greenland, Iceland, Norway, Sweden, Åland) or the Baltic countries (Estonia, Latvia, or Lithuania), although the applicant does not have to be a Nordic or Baltic citizen. Students are not granted mobility funding. However, professional artists and cultural practitioners can apply for funding in some cases, if the purpose of the trip is not linked to studies, but is part of the artist’s continued professional work. Trips within one and the same country/area Trips to or from countries outside the Nordic/Baltic region Trips which are a part of the applicant’s formal studies Organisational or company travel Official travel for employees in public administration – e.g. state authorities, municipalities, regions or the equivalent. Activities that have already been carried out.",Next year – the application dates will be published in November,2027-09-24,2026-09-23 12:37:34.083129+00:00
nordic_culture_point_99a3ce7db217,nordic_culture_point,https://www.nkk.org/en/short-term-network-funding/,https://applicant.nordiskkulturkontakt.org/,Nordic Culture Point,"Network funding facilitates meetings, the exchange of ideas and knowledge between professional artists and cultural practitioners in the Nordic and/or Baltic region, which in this context is the countries of Denmark, Estonia, Finland, Faroe Islands, Greenland, Iceland, Latvia, Lithuania, Norway, Sweden, and Åland.",all forms of art and culture,funding,"Denmark, Estonia, Finland, Faroe Islands, Greenland, Iceland, Latvia, Lithuania, Norway, Sweden, and Åland",,"For networks that will work together for up to one year, you can get funding of up to EUR 20,000. The contribution from Nordic Culture Point can make up a maximum of 70% of the project’s budget.",,,"Network funding facilitates meetings, the exchange of ideas and knowledge between professional artists and cultural practitioners in the Nordic and/or Baltic region, which in this context is the countries of Denmark, Estonia, Finland, Faroe Islands, Greenland, Iceland, Latvia, Lithuania, Norway, Sweden, and Åland.",all forms of art and culture,funding,,"Denmark, Estonia, Finland, Faroe Islands, Greenland, Iceland, Latvia, Lithuania, Norway, Sweden, and Åland",,['Multidisciplinary'],['Grant/Funding'],[],"['Denmark', 'Estonia', 'Finland', 'Faroe Islands', 'Greenland', 'Iceland', 'Latvia', 'Lithuania', 'Norway', 'Sweden', 'Åland Islands']","[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': 20000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'up to one year; contribution may cover max 70% of project budget'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:45.633823+00:00,,,,,en,Short-term network funding,"Funding is available for professional artists and cultural practitioners (such as curators, producers, literary translators, cultural editors or researchers) in all forms of art and culture. Applications may be submitted by individuals or organisations. “Professional” means that there is documented experience of work in the field of art and culture and/or training in art or culture. To apply for network funding, you must be a resident of the Nordic Region (Denmark, Finland, the Faroe Islands, Greenland, Iceland, Norway, Sweden, or Åland) or the Baltic countries (Estonia, Latvia, or Lithuania), although you do not need to be a Nordic or Baltic citizen. Groups, organisations, and institutions must be registered in a Nordic or Baltic country in order to apply. The network must consist of partners from: at least three Nordic and/or Baltic countries (Denmark, Estonia, Finland, the Faroe Islands, Greenland, Iceland, Latvia, Lithuania, Norway, Sweden, and Åland.) The network may include additional partners who do not operate in the Nordic or Baltic region.",Short-term network funding,"Funding is available for professional artists and cultural practitioners (such as curators, producers, literary translators, cultural editors or researchers) in all forms of art and culture. Applications may be submitted by individuals or organisations. “Professional” means that there is documented experience of work in the field of art and culture and/or training in art or culture. To apply for network funding, you must be a resident of the Nordic Region (Denmark, Finland, the Faroe Islands, Greenland, Iceland, Norway, Sweden, or Åland) or the Baltic countries (Estonia, Latvia, or Lithuania), although you do not need to be a Nordic or Baltic citizen. Groups, organisations, and institutions must be registered in a Nordic or Baltic country in order to apply. The network must consist of partners from: at least three Nordic and/or Baltic countries (Denmark, Estonia, Finland, the Faroe Islands, Greenland, Iceland, Latvia, Lithuania, Norway, Sweden, and Åland.) The network may include additional partners who do not operate in the Nordic or Baltic region.","15:59, Finnish time",2026-09-24,2026-09-23 12:37:34.085983+00:00
nordic_culture_point_e5ff586e656e,nordic_culture_point,https://www.nkk.org/en/volt/,https://applicant.nordiskkulturkontakt.org/,Nordic Culture Point,projects relating to the cultural and artistic creativity of children and young people.,"all areas of the arts, including film, literature, the performing arts, the visual arts, and cultural heritage",funding,Nordic Region,,"Project funding from Volt up to EUR 35,000 is available. Funding of up to EUR 7,000 may be awarded with full funding. For applications requesting higher sums, funding from Volt may account for a maximum of 70% of the project’s costs.",,,projects relating to the cultural and artistic creativity of children and young people.,"all areas of the arts, including film, literature, the performing arts, the visual arts, and cultural heritage",funding,,Nordic Region,,"['Film/Video', 'Literature/Writing', 'Performing Arts', 'Visual Arts', 'Cultural Heritage']",['Grant/Funding'],[],"['Denmark', 'Finland', 'Iceland', 'Norway', 'Sweden']","[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': 35000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'project funding up to this amount; for applications requesting higher sums, funding may cover max 70% of project costs'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': 7000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'may be awarded with full funding'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:45.633873+00:00,,,,,en,Volt,"Eligible applicants are: Individuals Organisations, associations, and institutions Applicants do not need to belong to the target group themselves but should have experience of working with children and young people. If you are under the age of 18, you can present your idea for a project to an association or organisation, or to an adult who can help you develop and implement the project. To be granted funding from Volt, the project must be conducted in collaboration with participants from at least three Nordic countries (Denmark, Finland, the Faroe Islands, Greenland, Iceland, Norway, Sweden, or Åland). Projects can be implemented in one or more of these countries. Although projects are welcome to have partners that don’t live in the Nordic Region, the programme will not cover their costs. The applicant must be resident in the Nordic Region but does not require Nordic citizenship.",Volt,"Eligible applicants are: Individuals Organisations, associations, and institutions Applicants do not need to belong to the target group themselves but should have experience of working with children and young people. If you are under the age of 18, you can present your idea for a project to an association or organisation, or to an adult who can help you develop and implement the project. To be granted funding from Volt, the project must be conducted in collaboration with participants from at least three Nordic countries (Denmark, Finland, the Faroe Islands, Greenland, Iceland, Norway, Sweden, or Åland). Projects can be implemented in one or more of these countries. Although projects are welcome to have partners that don’t live in the Nordic Region, the programme will not cover their costs. The applicant must be resident in the Nordic Region but does not require Nordic citizenship.",the application window closes at 15:59 Finnish time.,2026-09-24,2026-09-23 12:37:34.088557+00:00
rijksakademie_355e23d52adb,rijksakademie,https://rijksakademie.nl/en/residency-apply,https://rijksakademie.nl/en/residency-apply/apply,Rijksakademie,"The Rijksakademie is a two-year residency programme that annually offers 50 artists space for research, experiment and for the production of new work.",visual arts,residency,The Netherlands,Amsterdam,"Residents are supported with a studio, a work budget and a stipend",,,"The Rijksakademie is a two-year residency programme that annually offers 50 artists space for research, experiment and for the production of new work.",visual arts,residency,,The Netherlands,Amsterdam,['Visual Arts'],['Residency'],[],['Netherlands'],"[{'category': 'Accommodation/Housing', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'studio provided'}, {'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'work budget provided'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'stipend provided'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:45.633911+00:00,,,,,en,Residency,"The Rijksakademie is a two-year residency programme that annually offers 50 artists space for research, experiment and for the production of new work.",Residency,"The Rijksakademie is a two-year residency programme that annually offers 50 artists space for research, experiment and for the production of new work.",,,2026-09-23 12:37:34.088589+00:00
u_jazdowski_warsaw_ea8781efb99b,u_jazdowski_warsaw,https://u-jazdowski.pl/en/programme/residencies/open-calls/cwiczenia-ze-wspolistnienia,,Ujazdowski Castle Centre for Contemporary Art,"We invite you to apply for the open call entitled Practicing Togetherness for an artistic residency at the Ujazdowski Castle Centre for Contemporary Art in Warsaw . In 2026 , Ujazdowski residencies will become a space for activities focused on reflecting on togetherness , collaboration , and the relationship in post - human world in the face of contemporary crises . We invite artists and researchers of various disciplines , whose work explores possible strategies of coexistence and regeneration . We are interested in how our everyday practices can become a starting point for building more sustainable and solidaristic futures . Projects developed within the Ujazdowski residencies often take an intimate , small - scale form , unfold over time , and remain open to process , uncertainty , and failure . While working at Ujazdowski , residents draw on its resources and engage with the surrounding environment , frequently uncovering new meanings through attentive and context - sensitive approaches . Projects developed in collaboration with artists , researchers , and local communities create a space for experimentation , knowledge exchange , and shared experience , both within Ujazdowski and beyond its walls .","visual arts , performance , literature , music , etc .",artistic residency,Poland,Warsaw,"Monthly per diems of 5 , 000 PLN ( gross ) 5 , 000 PLN project budget Travel tickets ( roundtrip ) Accommodation Studio with living space , kitchenette , and bathroom + common spaces ( fully equipped kitchen and common room ) Working space Wood workshop with essential tools , conference room , meeting room , theatre room with a professional dance floor , possibility of borrowing audiovisual equipment and technical tools",,,"We invite you to apply for the open call entitled Practicing Togetherness for an artistic residency at the Ujazdowski Castle Centre for Contemporary Art in Warsaw . In 2026 , Ujazdowski residencies will become a space for activities focused on reflecting on togetherness , collaboration , and the relationship in post - human world in the face of contemporary crises . We invite artists and researchers of various disciplines , whose work explores possible strategies of coexistence and regeneration . We are interested in how our everyday practices can become a starting point for building more sustainable and solidaristic futures . Projects developed within the Ujazdowski residencies often take an intimate , small - scale form , unfold over time , and remain open to process , uncertainty , and failure . While working at Ujazdowski , residents draw on its resources and engage with the surrounding environment , frequently uncovering new meanings through attentive and context - sensitive approaches . Projects developed in collaboration with artists , researchers , and local communities create a space for experimentation , knowledge exchange , and shared experience , both within Ujazdowski and beyond its walls .","visual arts , performance , literature , music , etc .",artistic residency,,Poland,Warsaw,"['Visual Arts', 'Performing Arts', 'Literature/Writing', 'Music']",['Residency'],[],['Poland'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 5000.0, 'amount_max': 5000.0, 'currency': 'PLN', 'period': 'per month', 'note': 'gross per diems'}, {'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': 5000.0, 'amount_max': 5000.0, 'currency': 'PLN', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'project budget'}, {'category': 'Travel Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'roundtrip travel tickets'}, {'category': 'Accommodation/Housing', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'accommodation provided with studio/living space and facilities'}, {'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'working space and access to workshop, rooms, and equipment'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:45.633916+00:00,,,,,en,Practising Togetherness,"Open call for Palestinian artists , cultural practitioners , theorists , curators , and people working at the intersection of education / art / activism
We encourage applications from individuals whose practice is based on artistic research , regardless of the medium they use ( visual arts , performance , literature , music , etc . ) .
Target group Artists , cultural practitioners , theorists , curators , and people working at the intersection of education / art / activism; and those engaged in participatory work with communities who recognize themselves as Palestinians .
Collectives Yes , max two people",Practising Togetherness,"Open call for Palestinian artists , cultural practitioners , theorists , curators , and people working at the intersection of education / art / activism
