can_serrat_bda1091bdb89,can_serrat,https://canserrat.org/collective-creation2027_internationalresidency,https://forms.gle/KxfqCEwRnwvGfqNNA,Can Serrat,"These laboratory-format residencies invite artists, writers, and researchers from diverse disciplines to explore walking as an artistic and research methodology through an intensive process of collective work situated within the landscape of Montserrat.","artists, writers, and researchers from diverse disciplines",Art Residency Program,,,"Thanks to the support of the Department of Culture, participants benefit from a reduced participation fee.",,,"These laboratory-format residencies invite artists, writers, and researchers from diverse disciplines to explore walking as an artistic and research methodology through an intensive process of collective work situated within the landscape of Montserrat.","artists, writers, and researchers from diverse disciplines",Art Residency Program,,,,"['Multidisciplinary', 'Literature/Writing']",['Residency'],[],[],"[{'category': 'Fee Waiver', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'reduced participation fee'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:55.338035+00:00,,,,,en,Collective Creation Laboratory 2027,"People of any background and age (minors with authorization). It is not necessary to be an artist or writer. The laboratory welcomes anyone interested in research, creative practice, and collaborative ways of working. Individual, duo, or collective applications are accepted. Group Residencies The Collective Creation programme is designed to support creative processes developed through collaboration, exchange, and shared research. We welcome artistic collectives, research groups, and other collaborative initiatives. To encourage collective participation and respond to the specific needs of group-based processes, we offer dedicated conditions for applications from groups of 4 or more participants attending the residency during the same period.",Collective Creation Laboratory 2027,"People of any background and age (minors with authorization). It is not necessary to be an artist or writer. The laboratory welcomes anyone interested in research, creative practice, and collaborative ways of working. Individual, duo, or collective applications are accepted. Group Residencies The Collective Creation programme is designed to support creative processes developed through collaboration, exchange, and shared research. We welcome artistic collectives, research groups, and other collaborative initiatives. To encourage collective participation and respond to the specific needs of group-based processes, we offer dedicated conditions for applications from groups of 4 or more participants attending the residency during the same period.","Application period: March 27 – October 3, 2026.",2026-10-03,2026-09-23 13:53:09.977091+00:00
deutscher_uebersetzerfonds_fd2461c9db20,deutscher_uebersetzerfonds,https://www.uebersetzerfonds.de/files/Workshop_post-kolonial_afriCOLOGNE.pdf,,africologneFESTIVAL,Das africologneFESTIVAL lädt im Herbst 2026 zu einem dreitägigen Workshop für post-koloniale Theaterübersetzung nach Köln ein.,Theaterübersetzung,Workshop,Germany,Köln,Die Teilnahme am Workshop ist kostenfrei. Für Verpflegung und Vorstellungsbesuch fallen insgesamt 30 € an.,Die Teilnahme am Workshop ist kostenfrei. Für Verpflegung und Vorstellungsbesuch fallen insgesamt 30 € an.,,africologneFESTIVAL invites you to Cologne in autumn 2026 for a three-day workshop on post-colonial theatre translation.,theater translation,Workshop,,Germany,Cologne,"['Theatre', 'Literature/Writing']",['Workshop/Training'],[],['Germany'],"[{'category': 'Fee Waiver', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'Workshop participation is free'}, {'category': 'Other/Unspecified Support', 'amount_min': 30.0, 'amount_max': 30.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'Covers food and screening/visiting the performance'}, {'category': 'Fee Waiver', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'Participation in the workshop is free'}]",2026-09-24 08:57:59.946102+00:00,False,,,,de,Workshop „Post-koloniale Theaterübersetzung“,"Er richtet sich an Übersetzer*innen, Theatermacher*innen und kulturpolitisch Interessierte aus NRW, die sich mit den besonderen Herausforderungen der Übersetzung afrikanischer und afrodiasporischer Dramatik auseinandersetzen möchten. Besonders willkommen sind BIPOC-Bewerber*innen sowie Personen mit unterschiedlichen Hintergründen in Übersetzung, Theaterpraxis, Aktivismus oder Kulturkritik. Englisch- und Französischkenntnisse sind willkommen. Noch wichtiger ist jedoch die Bereitschaft zur kollektiven Arbeit und zur kritischen Auseinandersetzung mit Sprache, Macht und Repräsentation.",Workshop “Postcolonial Theatre Translation”,"It is aimed at translators, theatre practitioners, and those interested in cultural policy from NRW who would like to engage with the particular challenges of translating African and Afrodiasporic drama. BIPOC applicants as well as people with diverse backgrounds in translation, theatre practice, activism, or cultural criticism are especially welcome. Knowledge of English and French is welcome. However, even more important is the willingness to work collectively and to engage critically with language, power, and representation.",bis zum 5. September,2027-09-05,2026-09-23 13:53:11.774816+00:00
