institut_francais_programs_0fe835a45001,institut_francais_programs,https://www.institutfrancais.com/en/programme/project-support/french-language-fund,https://espace-reseau.institutfrancais.com/fr/offre/fonds-langue-francaise,Institut français,"The French Language Fund aims to support pilot projects designed to promote the French language and make it attractive. These projects must take place within local educational, cultural and economic ecosystems, in conjunction with French-speaking partners.",French language,Project support,,,support compris entre 7000 € et 15000€,,,"The French Language Fund aims to support pilot projects designed to promote the French language and make it attractive. These projects must take place within local educational, cultural and economic ecosystems, in conjunction with French-speaking partners.",French language,Project support,,,,['Other/Non-Arts'],['Grant/Funding'],[],[],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 7000.0, 'amount_max': 15000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': None}]",2026-09-24 08:58:03.013995+00:00,,,,,en,French Language Fund,"Open to members of the French cultural network abroad, it supports thematic projects benefiting the following audiences: learners and future learners of French, teachers and future teachers of French, educational executives and the general public.

Les projets déposés devront :
Les projets déposés devront : S’adresser exclusivement aux apprenants et futurs apprenants de français, de l’école maternelle à l’université, des tout-petits aux jeunes adultes ; S’inscrire dans un temps fort national ou international : Journée européenne des langues, Printemps de l’esprit critique, Semaine du goût, Nuit des idées, semaine de la presse et des médias, 15 ans du label labelFranceÉducation, festivals et salons (musique, cinéma, littérature, jeu vidéo, sport, etc.).",French Language Fund,"Open to members of the French cultural network abroad, it supports thematic projects benefiting the following audiences: learners and future learners of French, teachers and future teachers of French, educational executives and the general public.

Les projets déposés devront :
Les projets déposés devront : S’adresser exclusivement aux apprenants et futurs apprenants de français, de l’école maternelle à l’université, des tout-petits aux jeunes adultes ; S’inscrire dans un temps fort national ou international : Journée européenne des langues, Printemps de l’esprit critique, Semaine du goût, Nuit des idées, semaine de la presse et des médias, 15 ans du label labelFranceÉducation, festivals et salons (musique, cinéma, littérature, jeu vidéo, sport, etc.).",30 October 2026,2026-10-30,2026-09-23 13:53:40.033270+00:00
institut_francais_programs_7df741699916,institut_francais_programs,https://www.institutfrancais.com/en/programme/project-support/aoca-support-cultural-operators-africa,https://ifprog.emundus.fr/fr/campagne-info?view=programme&cid=339,Institut français,"AOCA is a program of the Institut français that supports cultural operators and artists based on the African continent by assisting with creative and dissemination projects, as well as events taking place in Africa, and by contributing to the development of cultural ecosystems and international cooperation. The program supports projects that strengthen international dynamics on the African continent and encourage collaborations between African artists and cultural operators, the French cultural network, and French cultural actors.",Visual Arts / Photography Digital creation Performing arts / Music,Project support,Africa,,"The committee may award grants ranging from €5,000 to €15,000. A selection committee will meet to award grants that may cover up to 50% of the project’s total budget.",,,"AOCA is a program of the Institut français that supports cultural operators and artists based on the African continent by assisting with creative and dissemination projects, as well as events taking place in Africa, and by contributing to the development of cultural ecosystems and international cooperation. The program supports projects that strengthen international dynamics on the African continent and encourage collaborations between African artists and cultural operators, the French cultural network, and French cultural actors.",Visual Arts / Photography Digital creation Performing arts / Music,Project support,,Africa,,"['Visual Arts', 'Photography', 'Digital/New Media Arts', 'Performing Arts', 'Music']",['Grant/Funding'],[],['Other/Unspecified'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 5000.0, 'amount_max': 15000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': ""committee may award grants; may also cover up to 50% of the project's total budget""}]",2026-09-24 08:58:03.014041+00:00,,,,,en,AOCA - Support for cultural operators in Africa,"Program open to the following applicants African cultural institutions or organizations based in Africa that are undertaking a creative or outreach project, or organizing an event with an international scope taking place in Africa. Members of the French cultural network abroad (cultural services of embassies, Instituts français, Alliances Françaises, binational cultural centers). When projects are not led by the French cultural network, they must be accompanied by a letter of support issued by the French cultural network abroad (cultural services of embassies, Instituts français, Alliances Françaises, or binational cultural centers). Relevant disciplines Visual Arts Digital Art Photography Music Theater Dance Street Arts / Circus / Puppetry Types of Projects Supported AOCA can support the following projects taking place between March and December 2027: Regional Tours AOCA can support tours and exhibitions by African artists on the African continent . Tours must include a t least 5 scheduled performances in a minimum of 3 African countries (excluding the applicant’s country of residence) and at least 3 dates must be organized in collaboration with an Institut français or an Alliance française . Exhibition tours must include at least 3 stops in a minimum of 3 African countries (excluding the applicant’s country of residence) and at least 3 activities must be organized in collaboration with an Institut français or an Alliance française (exhibitions, conferences, training workshops, etc.). Events AOCA can support two types of events : Events (festivals, biennials, etc.) featuring a lineup of artists or companies from at least 3 African countries (excluding the applicant’s country of residence). Events (festivals, biennials, etc.) featuring a program of at least 2 French artists or companies and at least 2 African artists or companies . Artistic Creation and Collaborations AOCA can support two types of projects : Creative projects bringing together artists from at least three African countries (excluding the applicant’s country of residence) Artistic collaboration or co-production projects between an African artistic team and one or more French artists, companies, or cultural organizations . Amount of Support The committee may award grants ranging from €5,000 to €15,000. A selection committee will meet to award grants that may cover up to 50% of the project’s total budget. Special attention will be given to projects that highlight the youth, emerging scenes, and new artistic practices in the field of contemporary African creation. projects that prioritize an eco-responsible approach in their implementation and that allocate ample time for each stop on their tours (e.g., performances + meet-and-greet sessions + related workshops + training, etc.). Projects that are sensitive to gender issues: projects led by women working in the cultural sector, projects that highlight women artists, or projects that promote gender diversity and equality. While it is possible to use artificial intelligence tools to improve the drafting and presentation of applications for calls for proposals or calls for projects, the applicant or submitter must ensure that their application retains its originality and unique identity.",AOCA - Support for cultural operators in Africa,"Program open to the following applicants African cultural institutions or organizations based in Africa that are undertaking a creative or outreach project, or organizing an event with an international scope taking place in Africa. Members of the French cultural network abroad (cultural services of embassies, Instituts français, Alliances Françaises, binational cultural centers). When projects are not led by the French cultural network, they must be accompanied by a letter of support issued by the French cultural network abroad (cultural services of embassies, Instituts français, Alliances Françaises, or binational cultural centers). Relevant disciplines Visual Arts Digital Art Photography Music Theater Dance Street Arts / Circus / Puppetry Types of Projects Supported AOCA can support the following projects taking place between March and December 2027: Regional Tours AOCA can support tours and exhibitions by African artists on the African continent . Tours must include a t least 5 scheduled performances in a minimum of 3 African countries (excluding the applicant’s country of residence) and at least 3 dates must be organized in collaboration with an Institut français or an Alliance française . Exhibition tours must include at least 3 stops in a minimum of 3 African countries (excluding the applicant’s country of residence) and at least 3 activities must be organized in collaboration with an Institut français or an Alliance française (exhibitions, conferences, training workshops, etc.). Events AOCA can support two types of events : Events (festivals, biennials, etc.) featuring a lineup of artists or companies from at least 3 African countries (excluding the applicant’s country of residence). Events (festivals, biennials, etc.) featuring a program of at least 2 French artists or companies and at least 2 African artists or companies . Artistic Creation and Collaborations AOCA can support two types of projects : Creative projects bringing together artists from at least three African countries (excluding the applicant’s country of residence) Artistic collaboration or co-production projects between an African artistic team and one or more French artists, companies, or cultural organizations . Amount of Support The committee may award grants ranging from €5,000 to €15,000. A selection committee will meet to award grants that may cover up to 50% of the project’s total budget. Special attention will be given to projects that highlight the youth, emerging scenes, and new artistic practices in the field of contemporary African creation. projects that prioritize an eco-responsible approach in their implementation and that allocate ample time for each stop on their tours (e.g., performances + meet-and-greet sessions + related workshops + training, etc.). Projects that are sensitive to gender issues: projects led by women working in the cultural sector, projects that highlight women artists, or projects that promote gender diversity and equality. While it is possible to use artificial intelligence tools to improve the drafting and presentation of applications for calls for proposals or calls for projects, the applicant or submitter must ensure that their application retains its originality and unique identity.",30 October 2026,2026-10-30,2026-09-23 13:53:40.037263+00:00
konstepidemin_74501beabeca,konstepidemin,https://konstepidemin.se/en/international-work/apply-for-artist-in-residence/,,Konstepidemin,"Konstepidemin’s five guest studios can be rented for periods of one to six months, and a minimum of one month is required.",artistic work,artist-in-residence,Sweden,Göteborg,"The current rent is 8500 SEK / month (Studio Robert is 8000 SEK / month), electricity, water and WIFI included.",,,"Konstepidemin’s five guest studios can be rented for periods of one to six months, and a minimum of one month is required.",artistic work,artist-in-residence,,Sweden,Göteborg,['Multidisciplinary'],['Residency'],[],['Sweden'],"[{'category': 'Accommodation/Housing', 'amount_min': 8500.0, 'amount_max': 8500.0, 'currency': 'SEK', 'period': 'per month', 'note': 'Studio Robert is 8000 SEK/month; electricity, water and WIFI included'}]",2026-09-24 08:58:03.014075+00:00,,,,,en,Apply for artist-in-residence,The application can be made as a group or as an individual. We are accepting applications for this year and the coming year. Please plan ahead and make sure to apply with some flexibility regarding your desired dates for residency.,Apply for artist-in-residence,The application can be made as a group or as an individual. We are accepting applications for this year and the coming year. Please plan ahead and make sure to apply with some flexibility regarding your desired dates for residency.,,,2026-09-23 13:53:40.037319+00:00
