kunstlerhaus_bethanien_25455ce5e85d,kunstlerhaus_bethanien,https://creativenz.govt.nz/funding-and-support/all-opportunities/berlin-visual-arts-residency,https://portal.creativenz.govt.nz/,Creative New Zealand,"An opportunity for a New Zealand visual artist with a strong national reputation to undertake a 12-month residency at the International Studio Programme at the Künstlerhaus Bethanien, Berlin.",Visual arts,residency,New Zealand,Berlin,"$45,000 plus accommodation and studio",,established,"An opportunity for a New Zealand visual artist with a strong national reputation to undertake a 12-month residency at the International Studio Programme at the Künstlerhaus Bethanien, Berlin.",Visual arts,residency,established,New Zealand,Berlin,['Visual Arts'],['Residency'],['Established/Professional'],['New Zealand'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 45000.0, 'amount_max': 45000.0, 'currency': 'USD', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'plus accommodation and studio'}, {'category': 'Accommodation/Housing', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'accommodation and studio'}]",2026-09-24 08:58:13.097743+00:00,,,,,en,Berlin Visual Arts Residency,"To apply, you must: be a New Zealand citizen or permanent resident have a strong national reputation as a visual artist, which means you have: - received critical recognition for your work, or - completed a body of work acknowledged for its artistic excellence You must be available to base yourself in Berlin between 15 January and 15 December 2027.

Who cannot apply
Previous recipients of the Residency are not eligible to apply. The previous recipients are Peter Robinson, Michael Stevenson, Ronnie van Hout, Mladen Bizumic, Sara Hughes, Alicia Frankovich, Ben Cauchi, Greg Semu, Oscar Enberg, Biljana Popovic, Ella Sutherland and most recently Areez Katki.",Berlin Visual Arts Residency,"To apply, you must: be a New Zealand citizen or permanent resident have a strong national reputation as a visual artist, which means you have: - received critical recognition for your work, or - completed a body of work acknowledged for its artistic excellence You must be available to base yourself in Berlin between 15 January and 15 December 2027.

Who cannot apply
Previous recipients of the Residency are not eligible to apply. The previous recipients are Peter Robinson, Michael Stevenson, Ronnie van Hout, Mladen Bizumic, Sara Hughes, Alicia Frankovich, Ben Cauchi, Greg Semu, Oscar Enberg, Biljana Popovic, Ella Sutherland and most recently Areez Katki.","1:00 PM (NZ time) on Monday, 2 March 2026",2026-09-24,2026-09-23 13:54:55.036597+00:00
kunstlerhaus_bethanien_ad1d16a215d9,kunstlerhaus_bethanien,https://www.konstnarsnamnden.se/en/scholarships-and-grants/residency-in-berlin-bethanien/,http://www.konstnarsnamnden.se/stipendier-och-bidrag/sa-har-soker-du/ansok-pa-papper/,"The Swedish Arts Grants Committee’s International Programme for Visual and Applied Artists, IASPIS","The Swedish Arts Grants Committee’s International Programme for Visual and Applied Artists, IASPIS, collaborates with a range of residency programmes around the world. In addition to a workspace or studio, the artist-in-residence will get access to housing and a stipend to cover travel and living expenses during their stay.","visual arts, photography, design, crafts, illustration, textile art or architecture",residency,Sweden,,130 000 SEK. This grant is intended to cover travel and living expenses as well as some material costs during the residency.,,,"The Swedish Arts Grants Committee’s International Programme for Visual and Applied Artists, IASPIS, collaborates with a range of residency programmes around the world. In addition to a workspace or studio, the artist-in-residence will get access to housing and a stipend to cover travel and living expenses during their stay.","visual arts, photography, design, crafts, illustration, textile art or architecture",residency,,Sweden,,"['Visual Arts', 'Photography', 'Design/Architecture', 'Craft']",['Residency'],[],['Sweden'],"[{'category': 'Travel Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'travel and living expenses covered'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 130000.0, 'amount_max': 130000.0, 'currency': 'SEK', 'period': None, 'note': 'living expenses and some material costs during the residency'}, {'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'some material costs during the residency'}]",2026-09-24 08:58:13.097791+00:00,,,,,en,"Residency in Berlin, Bethanien","Basic criteria
You must be a professional artist in the field of visual arts or design. You have an artistic practice in, for example, the visual arts, photography, design, crafts, illustration, textile art or architecture. To be considered a professional artist, you must earn a living entirely or partly from your artistic activities and regularly present your art to an audience or in an artistic context. You must be a resident in Sweden or practice most of your art here. You can be a foreign citizen and apply for our stipends and grants, but you must be a resident in Sweden or primarily practice your art here. If you are a Swedish citizen but live abroad, you must be able to demonstrate that most of your artistic activity takes place in Sweden. You must not be a student for more than 50 per cent of your time when an award decision is made. This means being enrolled in any type of studies, from undergraduate studies to doctoral studies and post-graduate education. You can be studying when you submit your application, but when a decision is made you cannot be enrolled for more than 50 per cent for a course or programme. You may not have any debts to the state or municipality that have been transferred for collection to the Swedish Enforcement Authority (Kronofogdemyndigheten), nor be declared bankrupt. You may not have tax or fee debts, or any other debts, that have been transferred to the Swedish Enforcement Authority and are being handled as a public collection matter. You must not have received de minimis aid exceeding a total of 300,000 euros during the last three-year period. Stipends and grants from the Swedish Arts Grants Committee are subject to the provisions of the European Commission Regulation (EU) 2023/2031 on state funding, also known as de minimis aid.","Residency in Berlin, Bethanien","Basic criteria
You must be a professional artist in the field of visual arts or design. You have an artistic practice in, for example, the visual arts, photography, design, crafts, illustration, textile art or architecture. To be considered a professional artist, you must earn a living entirely or partly from your artistic activities and regularly present your art to an audience or in an artistic context. You must be a resident in Sweden or practice most of your art here. You can be a foreign citizen and apply for our stipends and grants, but you must be a resident in Sweden or primarily practice your art here. If you are a Swedish citizen but live abroad, you must be able to demonstrate that most of your artistic activity takes place in Sweden. You must not be a student for more than 50 per cent of your time when an award decision is made. This means being enrolled in any type of studies, from undergraduate studies to doctoral studies and post-graduate education. You can be studying when you submit your application, but when a decision is made you cannot be enrolled for more than 50 per cent for a course or programme. You may not have any debts to the state or municipality that have been transferred for collection to the Swedish Enforcement Authority (Kronofogdemyndigheten), nor be declared bankrupt. You may not have tax or fee debts, or any other debts, that have been transferred to the Swedish Enforcement Authority and are being handled as a public collection matter. You must not have received de minimis aid exceeding a total of 300,000 euros during the last three-year period. Stipends and grants from the Swedish Arts Grants Committee are subject to the provisions of the European Commission Regulation (EU) 2023/2031 on state funding, also known as de minimis aid.",Applications must be submitted by 14.00 CET on the application deadline.,,2026-09-23 13:54:55.041534+00:00
kunstlerhaus_bethanien_8fd8bff07672,kunstlerhaus_bethanien,https://www.berlin.de/sen/kultur/en/funding/funding-programmes/weltoffenes-berlin/fellowship-program-weltoffenes-berlin/,https://fms.verwalt-berlin.de/egokuef/egokuefservice/main,Berlin.de Senate Department for Culture and Social Cohesion Department of Culture,"Berlin-based cultural institutions and initiatives can apply for the fellowships in 2025 (maximum duration is one year), and should enable the fellows to gain access to work opportunities in Berlin.","art, media, and culture",fellowships,Berlin,Berlin,"For each fellowship, a monthly sum of up to €2,500 will be paid for a maximum of 12 months to finance project-related costs.",,professional artists,"Berlin-based cultural institutions and initiatives can apply for the fellowships in 2025 (maximum duration is one year), and should enable the fellows to gain access to work opportunities in Berlin.","art, media, and culture",fellowships,professional artists,Berlin,Berlin,['Multidisciplinary'],['Fellowship'],['Established/Professional'],['Germany'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 2500.0, 'amount_max': 2500.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'per month', 'note': 'up to 12 months; project-related costs'}]",2026-09-24 08:58:13.097817+00:00,,,,,en,"Fellowship Program ""Weltoffenes Berlin""","Berlin-based cultural institutions and initiatives are eligible to apply. In case of funding, the cultural institution or initiative (host) is obliged to sign a contract (grant, employment or other contract) with the fellow. The contract can be negotiated between the institution and the fellow depending on individual needs. The professional artist must have completed a relevant professional education and have worked, or is currently working in art, media, and culture on a professional level. A proof must be submitted (application form).","Fellowship Program ""Weltoffenes Berlin""","Berlin-based cultural institutions and initiatives are eligible to apply. In case of funding, the cultural institution or initiative (host) is obliged to sign a contract (grant, employment or other contract) with the fellow. The contract can be negotiated between the institution and the fellow depending on individual needs. The professional artist must have completed a relevant professional education and have worked, or is currently working in art, media, and culture on a professional level. A proof must be submitted (application form).",,,2026-09-23 13:54:55.041597+00:00
lithuanian_culture_institute_7b6066cf58b8,lithuanian_culture_institute,https://english.lithuanianculture.lt/translation-grant-programme/,https://english.lithuanianculture.lt/books-translation-grant-programme/funding-competition/,Lithuanian Culture Institute,"The aim of this programme is to support the translation, publication, and dissemination of Lithuanian literature globally, and to make the most valued and interesting works of Lithuanian prose, poetry, drama, documentary, and children’s literature accessible and known outside Lithuania.",Lithuanian literature,funding competition,Lithuania,,"The amount allocated for projects to promote translations of Lithuanian literature is EUR 100,000 per year.",,,"The aim of this programme is to support the translation, publication, and dissemination of Lithuanian literature globally, and to make the most valued and interesting works of Lithuanian prose, poetry, drama, documentary, and children’s literature accessible and known outside Lithuania.",Lithuanian literature,funding competition,,Lithuania,,['Literature/Writing'],['Grant/Funding'],[],['Lithuania'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 100000.0, 'amount_max': 100000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'per year', 'note': 'allocated for projects to promote translations of Lithuanian literature'}]",2026-09-24 08:58:13.097843+00:00,,,,,en,Translation Grant Funding Competition,Submission of applications and participation in the competition is open to publishers of Lithuania or foreign countries or other legal entities engaged in publishing activities abroad who intend to publish a translation of a work of Lithuanian literature in their countries.,Translation Grant Funding Competition,Submission of applications and participation in the competition is open to publishers of Lithuania or foreign countries or other legal entities engaged in publishing activities abroad who intend to publish a translation of a work of Lithuanian literature in their countries.,,,2026-09-23 13:54:55.041705+00:00
lithuanian_culture_institute_32dcb2a9ae26,lithuanian_culture_institute,https://english.lithuanianculture.lt/news/2025/07/29/lithuanian-literature-translators-residency-in-vilnius-2025/,,"Vilnius, a UNESCO City of Literature, in cooperation with the Lithuanian Culture Institute",invites translators of Lithuanian literature living outside Lithuania to apply for a 3-4 week residency in Vilnius.,Lithuanian literature translation,residency,Lithuania,Vilnius,"The residency participant(s) will have their travel expenses covered, receive a daily allowance, and be provided with suitable living and working conditions.",,,invites translators of Lithuanian literature living outside Lithuania to apply for a 3-4 week residency in Vilnius.,Lithuanian literature translation,residency,,Lithuania,Vilnius,['Literature/Writing'],['Residency'],[],['Lithuania'],"[{'category': 'Travel Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'travel expenses covered'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': 'per day', 'note': 'daily allowance'}, {'category': 'Accommodation/Housing', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'suitable living and working conditions'}]",2026-09-24 08:58:13.097863+00:00,,,,,en,Lithuanian Literature Translators’ Residency in Vilnius 2025,invites translators of Lithuanian literature living outside Lithuania to apply for a 3-4 week residency in Vilnius. Priority will be given to translators who have specific translation plans and contracts with publishers.,Lithuanian Literature Translators’ Residency in Vilnius 2025,invites translators of Lithuanian literature living outside Lithuania to apply for a 3-4 week residency in Vilnius. Priority will be given to translators who have specific translation plans and contracts with publishers.,Applications will be accepted until August 15. (inclusive).,2027-08-15,2026-09-23 13:54:55.045174+00:00
lux_moving_image_6f82a70c5ebe,lux_moving_image,https://lux.org.uk/lva50-call-for-conference-papers-london-video-arts-an-oppositional-practice-perspectives-on-video-art-activism-networks-technology-then-and-now/,https://lux.org.uk/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection,LUX,"MIRAJ, in partnership with LUX, invites abstracts to debate these questions and reflect on the legacy of LVA at a two-day conference at the University of Westminster and associated exhibition at gallery Ambika P3 on 26-27 February 2027.",video art; artists’ moving image and media artworks,conference papers,United Kingdom,London,,,,"MIRAJ, in partnership with LUX, invites abstracts to debate these questions and reflect on the legacy of LVA at a two-day conference at the University of Westminster and associated exhibition at gallery Ambika P3 on 26-27 February 2027.",video art; artists’ moving image and media artworks,conference papers,,United Kingdom,London,"['Film/Video', 'Digital/New Media Arts']",['Other'],[],['United Kingdom'],[],,,,,,en,"LVA50 Call for Conference Papers: LONDON VIDEO ARTS: ‘An Oppositional Practice.’ Perspectives on Video: Art, Activism, Networks, Technology, then and now","We invite 20 minute papers and pre-constituted panels with a maximum of 4 speakers that: consider the definition of video art since its inception and the major transformations the concept has gone through; review and reframe existing video histories; examine the organisational model of the video collective, and its modes of circulation and distribution; explore the international and regional video networks of which LVA was part, share new research into underacknowledged video histories and figures; address the heterogeneous and intersecting ecologies of video practice: whether conceptual documentation and modernist experiment, radical campaigning and community engagement, and the later return to representational form; address how technological changes have determined video practices, cultures and ecologies; examine how London Video Arts addressed the hegemony of broadcast TV; explore the determining role of televisual culture and production in the development of video practice: it’s forms and address. consider what contemporary collective, activist or community-based video practices, in the UK and internationally, share with or depart from LVA’s model of artist-led organising consider how video art explored the limits of its material, processes and forms; discuss the role of video to address political and social urgencies and injustices; question the legacy of analogue video technology in the digital age; address the challenges of how to archive, conserve and exhibit fragile historic video technologies; explore how museums and galleries understand video art today.","LVA50 Call for Conference Papers: LONDON VIDEO ARTS: ‘An Oppositional Practice.’ Perspectives on Video: Art, Activism, Networks, Technology, then and now","We invite 20 minute papers and pre-constituted panels with a maximum of 4 speakers that: consider the definition of video art since its inception and the major transformations the concept has gone through; review and reframe existing video histories; examine the organisational model of the video collective, and its modes of circulation and distribution; explore the international and regional video networks of which LVA was part, share new research into underacknowledged video histories and figures; address the heterogeneous and intersecting ecologies of video practice: whether conceptual documentation and modernist experiment, radical campaigning and community engagement, and the later return to representational form; address how technological changes have determined video practices, cultures and ecologies; examine how London Video Arts addressed the hegemony of broadcast TV; explore the determining role of televisual culture and production in the development of video practice: it’s forms and address. consider what contemporary collective, activist or community-based video practices, in the UK and internationally, share with or depart from LVA’s model of artist-led organising consider how video art explored the limits of its material, processes and forms; discuss the role of video to address political and social urgencies and injustices; question the legacy of analogue video technology in the digital age; address the challenges of how to archive, conserve and exhibit fragile historic video technologies; explore how museums and galleries understand video art today.","CFP submission deadline: 17.00 (GMT), November 2 nd 2026",2026-11-02,2026-09-23 13:54:55.051544+00:00
min_kulture_croatia_03f95761dc0d,min_kulture_croatia,https://min-kulture.gov.hr/natjecaji-16274/javni-pozivi-404/javni-poziv-za-predlaganje-javnih-potreba-u-kulturi-republike-hrvatske-za-2027-godinu-rok-9-listopada-2026/30631,https://e-prijavnice.min-kulture.hr/e-pisarnica,Ministarstvo kulture i medija Republike Hrvatske,"Sredstva iz proračuna Republike Hrvatske osigurana za financiranje javnih potreba u kulturi namijenjena su potpori programima i projektima, aktivnostima i manifestacijama u kulturi od interesa za Republiku Hrvatsku, a dodjeljuju se na temelju provedenog javnog poziva (u daljnjem tekstu: Javni poziv) koji se objavljuje na mrežnim stranicama Ministarstva kulture i medija.","muzejske djelatnosti; knjižnične djelatnosti; monografija iz područja kulture i umjetnosti; potpore izdavanju knjiga; potpore inozemnim nakladnicima za objavljivanje prijevoda djela hrvatskih autora; izdavanja časopisa i periodičkih elektroničkih publikacija; književnih manifestacija; književnih programa u okviru knjižarske djelatnosti; dramske i plesne umjetnosti te izvedbenih umjetnosti; glazbene i glazbeno-scenske umjetnosti; vizualnih umjetnosti; interdisciplinarnih i novih umjetničkih i kulturnih praksi; kulturno-umjetničkog amaterizma (glazbenog i folklornog); međunarodne kulturne suradnje; redovite djelatnosti udruga u kulturi; gradnje, rekonstrukcije i opremanja kulturne infrastrukture; digitalizacije kulturne baštine; zaštite i očuvanja kopnene arheološke baštine; zaštite i očuvanja podvodne arheološke baštine; zaštite i očuvanja nepokretnih kulturnih dobara; zaštite i očuvanja pokretnih kulturnih dobara; zaštite i očuvanja nematerijalnih kulturnih dobara",Javni poziv,Republike Hrvatske,,Sredstva iz proračuna Republike Hrvatske,,,"Funds from the budget of the Republic of Croatia secured for financing public needs in culture are intended to support programs and projects, activities and manifestations in culture of interest to the Republic of Croatia, and are awarded on the basis of a conducted public call (hereinafter: Public Call) which is published on the websites of the Ministry of Culture and Media.","museum activities; library activities; monograph in the field of culture and art; support for book publishing; support for foreign publishers to publish translations of works by Croatian authors; publishing of journals and periodic electronic publications; literary events; literary programs within bookselling activity; drama and dance arts and performing arts; musical and musical-stage arts; visual arts; interdisciplinary and new artistic and cultural practices; amateur cultural and artistic activity (musical and folkloric); international cultural cooperation; regular activities of cultural associations; construction, reconstruction and equipping of cultural infrastructure; digitization of cultural heritage; protection and preservation of land archaeological heritage; protection and preservation of underwater archaeological heritage; protection and preservation of immovable cultural property; protection and preservation of movable cultural property; protection and preservation of intangible cultural property",pilot project / public call,,of the Republic of Croatia,,"['Cultural Heritage', 'Literature/Writing', 'Performing Arts', 'Music', 'Visual Arts', 'Multidisciplinary']",['Open Call'],[],['Croatia'],[],2026-09-24 08:58:13.097867+00:00,,,,,hr,Javni poziv za predlaganje javnih potreba u kulturi Republike Hrvatske za 2027. godinu (Rok: 9. listopada 2026.),"Na ovaj Javni poziv mogu se prijaviti ustanove u kulturi, umjetničke organizacije, umjetnici, udruge, druge fizičke i pravne osobe te jedinice lokalne i područne (regionalne) samouprave u sljedećim djelatnostima i područjima: muzejske djelatnosti knjižnične djelatnosti monografija iz područja kulture i umjetnosti potpore izdavanju knjiga potpore inozemnim nakladnicima za objavljivanje prijevoda djela hrvatskih autora izdavanja časopisa i periodičkih elektroničkih publikacija književnih manifestacija književnih programa u okviru knjižarske djelatnosti dramske i plesne umjetnosti te izvedbenih umjetnosti glazbene i glazbeno-scenske umjetnosti vizualnih umjetnosti interdisciplinarnih i novih umjetničkih i kulturnih praksi kulturno-umjetničkog amaterizma (glazbenog i folklornog) međunarodne kulturne suradnje redovite djelatnosti udruga u kulturi gradnje, rekonstrukcije i opremanja kulturne infrastrukture digitalizacije kulturne baštine zaštite i očuvanja kopnene arheološke baštine zaštite i očuvanja podvodne arheološke baštine zaštite i očuvanja nepokretnih kulturnih dobara zaštite i očuvanja pokretnih kulturnih dobara zaštite i očuvanja nematerijalnih kulturnih dobara.",Public Call for the Proposal of Public Needs in Culture of the Republic of Croatia for 2027 (Deadline: 9 October 2026),"Applications may be submitted to this Public Call by cultural institutions, artistic organizations, artists, associations, other natural and legal persons, and units of local and regional self-government in the following activities and areas: museum activities library activities monographs in the field of culture and the arts support for book publishing support for foreign publishers for the publication of translations of works by Croatian authors publishing journals and periodical electronic publications literary events literary programs within bookselling activities dramatic and dance arts and performing arts musical and music-stage arts visual arts interdisciplinary and new artistic and cultural practices cultural and artistic amateurism (musical and folkloric) international cultural cooperation regular activities of cultural associations construction, reconstruction and equipping of cultural infrastructure digitization of cultural heritage protection and preservation of terrestrial archaeological heritage protection and preservation of underwater archaeological heritage protection and preservation of immovable cultural property protection and preservation of movable cultural property protection and preservation of intangible cultural property.",9. listopada 2026.,2026-10-09,2026-09-23 13:54:57.052962+00:00
min_kulture_croatia_638345cf7201,min_kulture_croatia,https://min-kulture.gov.hr/natjecaji-16274/javni-pozivi-404/javni-poziv-za-financiranje-oglednih-prijevoda-djela-hrvatskih-autora-na-strane-jezike-u-2026-godini-rok-10-studenoga-2026/29130,https://min-kulture.gov.hr/UserDocsImages/dokumenti/2026 Dokumenti/Ogledni prijevodi prijavnica 2026.doc?vel=195584,Ministarstvo kulture i medija Republike Hrvatske,Javni poziv za financiranje oglednih prijevoda djela hrvatskih autora na strane jezike u 2026. godini,književnost,Javni poziv,Hrvatska,Zagreb,Putem ovog Javnog poziva financirat će se isključivo troškovi autorskog djela prevoditelja u maksimalnom iznosu do 1.000 € bruto po jednom oglednom prijevodu te troškovi tiska promidžbene knjižice koja će sadržavati ogledni prijevod ako je prijavitelj namjerava otisnuti u maksimalnom iznosu do 300 € kn bruto po jednom oglednom prijevodu.,,,Public call for financing sample translations of works by Croatian authors into foreign languages in 2026,literature,pilot project / public call,,Croatia,Zagreb,['Literature/Writing'],['Open Call'],[],['Croatia'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 1000.0, 'amount_max': 1000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'bruto po jednom oglednom prijevodu; author/translator work'}, {'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': 300.0, 'amount_max': 300.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'printing of promotional booklet, bruto po jednom oglednom prijevodu'}]",2026-09-24 08:58:13.097880+00:00,,,,,hr,Javni poziv za financiranje oglednih prijevoda djela hrvatskih autora na strane jezike u 2026. godini,"Na Javni se poziv mogu prijaviti fizičke i pravne osobe registrirane za izdavačku djelatnost, zastupanje/posredovanje i/ili prodaju autorskih prava koji su do sada zaključili najmanje 5 ugovora za prodaju izdavačkih prava hrvatskih autora. Prijavitelji moraju biti nositelji autorskih prava za djela koja prijavljuju na ovaj Javni poziv ili moraju posjedovati pisanu izjavu nositelja autorskih prava da su suglasni s izradom i korištenjem oglednog prijevoda u skladu s ciljevima Javnog poziva. Ako posjeduju pisanu suglasnost najmanje pet autora za financiranje oglednih prijevoda mogu se prijaviti udruge i umjetničke organizacije, odnosno autorske strukovne udruge zainteresirane za promidžbu hrvatske književnosti u inozemstvu.",Public Call for Funding Sample Translations of Works by Croatian Authors into Foreign Languages in 2026,"Natural and legal persons registered for publishing activities, representation/intermediation and/or the sale of copyright may apply to the Public Call if they have so far concluded at least 5 contracts for the sale of publishing rights of Croatian authors. Applicants must be holders of the copyright to the works they submit to this Public Call, or they must possess a written statement from the copyright holder that they agree to the preparation and use of a sample translation in accordance with the objectives of the Public Call. Associations and artistic organizations, or professional authors’ associations interested in promoting Croatian literature abroad, may apply if they possess written consent from at least five authors for the funding of sample translations.",10. studenoga 2026.,2026-11-10,2026-09-23 13:54:58.943475+00:00
min_kulture_croatia_4e437d2f979f,min_kulture_croatia,https://min-kulture.gov.hr/natjecaji-16274/javni-pozivi-404/javni-poziv-za-iskaz-interesa-za-sudjelovanje-u-pilot-projektu-kulturna-iskaznica/29151,https://kulturnaiskaznica.gov.hr/javni_poziv,Ministarstvo kulture i medija Republike Hrvatske,"Cilj pilot-projekta Kulturna iskaznica jest promicanje univerzalnog i raznovrsnog pristupa kulturi za mlade, stvaranje navika korištenja kulturnih sadržaja, stvaranje nove publike te jačanje postojećih kulturnih potreba koje će doprinijeti daljnjem razvoju kulturnog i medijskog sektora.",kulturni i medijski sadržaji,pilot-projekt / javni poziv,Republika Hrvatska,,"Mladi koji od 1. siječnja do 31. prosinca 2026. godine navrše 18 godina ostvaruju pravo na izdavanje kulturne iskaznice, odnosno pristup kulturnim i medijskim sadržajima u doznačenom iznosu, koju mogu koristiti do navršenih 19 godina.",,Mladi koji od 1. siječnja do 31. prosinca 2026. godine navrše 18 godina,"The aim of the pilot project Cultural Pass is to promote universal and diverse access to culture for young people, the creation of habits of using cultural contents, the creation of a new audience, and the strengthening of existing cultural needs that will contribute to the further development of the cultural and media sector.",cultural and media content,scholarship,Young people who turn 18 years old from 1 January to 31 December 2026,Republic of Croatia,,['Other/Non-Arts'],['Grant/Funding'],['Any/Open to All'],['Croatia'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'access to cultural and media content in an allocated amount via cultural card until age 19'}]",2026-09-24 08:58:13.097934+00:00,,,,,hr,Javni poziv za iskaz interesa za sudjelovanje u pilot-projektu Kulturna iskaznica,Pozivaju se zainteresirani pružatelji usluga pristupa kulturnim i medijskim sadržajima da iskažu interes za sudjelovanje u pilot-projektu Kulturna iskaznica kako bi dobili priliku za povećanje vidljivosti kulturnih i medijskih sadržaja. Prihvaćeni pružatelji usluga pristupa kulturnim i medijskim sadržajima postat će sastavnim dijelom pilot-projekta Kulturna iskaznica .,Public call for expressions of interest for participation in the pilot project Cultural Card,Interested providers of access to cultural and media content are invited to express interest in participating in the pilot project Cultural Card in order to get the opportunity to increase the visibility of cultural and media content. Accepted providers of access to cultural and media content will become an integral part of the pilot project Cultural Card.,,,2026-09-23 13:55:00.144356+00:00
min_kulture_croatia_029819d1ab57,min_kulture_croatia,https://min-kulture.gov.hr/javni-poziv-za-predlaganje-programa-koji-poticu-razvoj-publike-u-kulturi-u-republici-hrvatskoj-za-2026-godinu-rok-8-prosinca-2025/28828,https://e-prijavnice.min-kulture.hr/e-pisarnica,Ministarstvo kulture i medija Republike Hrvatske,"Na temelju članka 7. Zakona o kulturnim vijećima i financiranju javnih potreba u kulturi („Narodne novine“, broj 83/22) Ministarstvo kulture i medija Republike Hrvatske objavljuje Javni poziv za predlaganje programa koji potiču razvoj publike u kulturi u Republici Hrvatskoj za 2026. godinu","izvedbene i vizualne umjetnosti interdisciplinarne i nove kulturne i umjetničke prakse, književnost, kulturna baština i film te programi međunarodne kulturne suradnje",Javni poziv,Republika Hrvatska,,Sredstva će se dodjeljivati za programe kojima je cilj razvoj publike u kulturi.,,,"Pursuant to Article 7 of the Act on Cultural Councils and the Financing of Public Needs in Culture (""Narodne novine"", No. 83/22), the Ministry of Culture and Media of the Republic of Croatia announces a Public Call for proposing programmes that encourage audience development in culture in the Republic of Croatia for 2026.","performing and visual arts interdisciplinary and new cultural and artistic practices, literature, cultural heritage and film, and programs of international cultural cooperation",pilot project / public call,,Republic of Croatia,,"['Performing Arts', 'Visual Arts', 'Multidisciplinary', 'Literature/Writing', 'Cultural Heritage', 'Film/Video']",['Open Call'],[],['Croatia'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'support for programs aimed at audience development in culture'}]",2026-09-24 08:58:13.097938+00:00,,,,,hr,Javni poziv za predlaganje programa koji potiču razvoj publike u kulturi u Republici Hrvatskoj za 2026. godinu,"Pravo podnošenja prijava na temelju ovog Poziva imaju samostalni umjetnici, umjetničke organizacije, ustanove u kulturi, udruge, pravne i fizičke osobe koje obavljaju djelatnost u kulturi, ustanove koje obavljaju djelatnost umjetničkog obrazovanja te jedinice lokalne i područne (regionalne) samouprave. Sve fizičke i pravne osobe registrirane za obavljanje djelatnosti u području kulture u Republici Hrvatskoj prilikom prijave dužne su dostaviti dokaz o djelovanju u području kulture tijekom najmanje dviju godina (registracija, opis dosadašnjega rada i postignuća).",Public call for submitting programs that promote audience development in culture in the Republic of Croatia for 2026,"The right to submit applications under this Call is granted to independent artists, artistic organizations, cultural institutions, associations, legal and natural persons engaged in cultural activities, institutions engaged in artistic education, and local and regional self-government units. All natural and legal persons registered to carry out activities in the field of culture in the Republic of Croatia are required, when applying, to submit proof of activity in the field of culture for at least two years (registration, description of previous work and achievements).",8. prosinca 2025.,2025-12-08,2026-09-23 13:55:02.018403+00:00
min_kulture_croatia_5da9446c017e,min_kulture_croatia,https://min-kulture.gov.hr/natjecaji-16274/javni-pozivi-404/arhiva-2632/javni-pozivi-u-2025-godini/javni-poziv-za-predlaganje-javnih-potreba-u-kulturi-republike-hrvatske-za-2026-godinu/28494,https://e-prijavnice.min-kulture.hr/e-pisarnica,Ministarstvo kulture i medija Republike Hrvatske,"Sredstva iz proračuna Republike Hrvatske osigurana za financiranje javnih potreba u kulturi namijenjena su potpori programima i projektima, aktivnostima i manifestacijama u kulturi od interesa za Republiku Hrvatsku, a dodjeljuju se na temelju provedenog javnog poziva (u daljnjem tekstu: Javni poziv) koji se objavljuje na mrežnim stranicama Ministarstva kulture i medija.",muzejske djelatnosti knjižnične djelatnosti monografija iz područja kulture i umjetnosti potpore izdavanju knjiga potpore inozemnim nakladnicima za objavljivanje prijevoda djela hrvatskih autora izdavanja časopisa i periodičkih elektroničkih publikacija književnih manifestacija književnih programa u okviru knjižarske djelatnosti dramske i plesne umjetnosti te izvedbenih umjetnosti glazbene i glazbeno-scenske umjetnosti vizualnih umjetnosti interdisciplinarnih i novih umjetničkih i kulturn,Javni poziv,Republike Hrvatske,,Sredstva iz proračuna Republike Hrvatske osigurana za financiranje javnih potreba u kulturi,,,"Funds from the budget of the Republic of Croatia secured for the financing of public needs in culture are intended to support programs and projects, activities and manifestations in culture of interest to the Republic of Croatia, and are awarded on the basis of a conducted public call (hereinafter: Public Call) which is published on the websites of the Ministry of Culture and Media.",museum activities library activities monograph in the field of culture and art support for book publishing support for foreign publishers to publish translations of works by Croatian authors publishing of journals and periodic electronic publications literary events literary programs within bookselling activity drama and dance arts and performing arts musical and musical-stage arts visual arts interdisciplinary and new artistic and cultural,pilot project / public call,,of the Republic of Croatia,,"['Cultural Heritage', 'Literature/Writing', 'Performing Arts', 'Music', 'Visual Arts', 'Multidisciplinary']",['Open Call'],[],['Croatia'],[],2026-09-24 08:58:13.097943+00:00,,,,,hr,Javni poziv za predlaganje javnih potreba u kulturi Republike Hrvatske za 2026. godinu,"Na ovaj Javni poziv mogu se prijaviti ustanove u kulturi, umjetničke organizacije, umjetnici, udruge, druge fizičke i pravne osobe te jedinice lokalne i područne (regionalne) samouprave u sljedećim djelatnostima i područjima: muzejske djelatnosti knjižnične djelatnosti monografija iz područja kulture i umjetnosti potpore izdavanju knjiga potpore inozemnim nakladnicima za objavljivanje prijevoda djela hrvatskih autora izdavanja časopisa i periodičkih elektroničkih publikacija književnih manifestacija književnih programa u okviru knjižarske djelatnosti dramske i plesne umjetnosti te izvedbenih umjetnosti glazbene i glazbeno-scenske umjetnosti vizualnih umjetnosti interdisciplinarnih i novih umjetničkih i kulturn",Public Call for Proposals for Public Needs in Culture of the Republic of Croatia for 2026,"The following may apply to this Public Call: cultural institutions, artistic organizations, artists, associations, other natural and legal persons, and local and regional self-government units in the following activities and fields: museum activities, library activities, monographs in the field of culture and the arts, support for the publication of books, support for foreign publishers for the publication of translations of works by Croatian authors, publication of journals and periodic electronic publications, literary events, literary programs within bookselling activities, dramatic and dance arts and performing arts, musical and music-stage arts, visual arts, interdisciplinary and new artistic and cultural",,,2026-09-23 13:55:03.934260+00:00
min_kulture_croatia_029faca5673a,min_kulture_croatia,https://min-kulture.gov.hr/javni-poziv-za-isticanje-kandidature-za-povjerenika-hrvatskog-nastupa-na-venecijanskom-bijenalu-61-medjunarodnoj-izlozbi-vizualnih-umjetnosti-rok-9-listopada-2025/28526,,Ministarstvo kulture i medija Republike Hrvatske,Ministarstvo kulture i medija ovim putem raspisuje Javni poziv za isticanje kandidature za povjerenika hrvatskog nastupa.,vizualnih umjetnosti,Javni poziv,Republika Hrvatska,Zagreb,,,,The Ministry of Culture and Media hereby announces a Public Call for the submission of candidacies for the commissioner of the Croatian presentation.,visual arts,pilot project / public call,,Republic of Croatia,Zagreb,['Visual Arts'],['Open Call'],[],['Croatia'],[],,,,,,hr,Javni poziv za isticanje kandidature za povjerenika hrvatskog nastupa na Venecijanskom bijenalu – 61. Međunarodnoj izložbi vizualnih umjetnosti,Uz kandidaturu za povjerenika potrebno je priložiti biografiju. Kandidati moraju imati iskustvo i stručnost u području suvremene umjetnosti te iskustvo u upravljanj,Public call for nominations for the Commissioner of the Croatian participation at the Venice Biennale – 61st International Exhibition of Visual Arts,"With the nomination for commissioner, it is necessary to submit a biography. Candidates must have experience and expertise in the field of contemporary art and experience in managing",9. listopada 2025.,2025-10-09,2026-09-23 13:55:05.167141+00:00
min_kulture_croatia_2fe7ed5dcd74,min_kulture_croatia,https://min-kulture.gov.hr/javni-poziv-za-financiranje-oglednih-prijevoda-djela-hrvatskih-autora-na-strane-jezike-u-2025-godini-rok-10-studenoga-2025-godine/27158,https://min-kulture.gov.hr/UserDocsImages/dokumenti/2024%20dokumenti/ogledni%20prijevodi/Ogledni%20prijevodi%20prijavnica%202025.doc,Ministarstvo kulture i medija Republike Hrvatske,Ministarstvo kulture i medija na temelju Zakona o kulturnim vijećima i financiranju javnih potreba u kulturi ( NN83/22 ) objavljuje Javni poziv za financiranje oglednih prijevoda djela hrvatskih autora na strane jezike u 2025. godini,književnost,Javni poziv,Republike Hrvatske,,Putem ovog Javnog poziva financirat će se isključivo troškovi autorskog djela prevodite,,,"The Ministry of Culture and Media, on the basis of the Act on Cultural Councils and Financing Public Needs in Culture (NN83/22), announces a Public Call for financing sample translations of works by Croatian authors into foreign languages in 2025.",literature,pilot project / public call,,of the Republic of Croatia,,['Literature/Writing'],['Open Call'],[],['Croatia'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': ""author's work of the translator only; amount not stated""}]",2026-09-24 08:58:13.097947+00:00,,,,,hr,Javni poziv za financiranje oglednih prijevoda djela hrvatskih autora na strane jezike u 2025. godini,"Na Javni se poziv mogu prijaviti fizičke i pravne osobe registrirane za izdavačku djelatnost, zastupanje/posredovanje i/ili prodaju autorskih prava koji su do sada zaključili najmanje 5 ugovora za prodaju izdavačkih prava hrvatskih autora. Prijavitelji moraju biti nositelji autorskih prava za djela koja prijavljuju na ovaj Javni poziv ili moraju posjedovati pismenu izjavu nositelja autorskih prava da su suglasni s izradom i korištenjem oglednog prijevoda u skladu s ciljevima Javnog poziva.",Public call for financing sample translations of works by Croatian authors into foreign languages in 2025,"Physical and legal persons registered for publishing activities, representation/intermediation and/or the sale of copyright who have so far concluded at least 5 contracts for the sale of publishing rights of Croatian authors may apply to the Public Call. Applicants must be holders of the copyright to the works they submit to this Public Call, or they must possess a written statement from the copyright holder that they agree to the creation and use of a sample translation in accordance with the objectives of the Public Call.",10. studenoga 2025. godine,2025-11-10,2026-09-23 13:55:06.695013+00:00
mk_statni_fond_kultury_cz_209b9ce5a11b,mk_statni_fond_kultury_cz,https://www.mk.gov.cz/statni-fond-kultury-cr-cs-42/zadosti-o-dotace-sfk-na-rok-2027,https://dpmkportal.mk.gov.cz/,Státní fond kultury ČR,Rada SFK vyhlašuje pro rok 2027 opět 3 výzvy k přijímání žádostí o podporu projektů s následujícími termíny:,"profesionální umění, literatura a knihovny",grant,Česká republika,,,,,The SFK Council announces again for the year 2027 3 calls for the submission of applications for support of projects with the following deadlines:,"professional art, literature and libraries",grant,,Czech Republic,,"['Literature/Writing', 'Other/Non-Arts']",['Grant/Funding'],[],['Czech Republic'],[],,,,,,cs,Žádosti o dotace SFK na rok 2027,"Rozhodujícím kritériem pro výběr termínu k podání žádosti je datum zahájení klíčového výstupu, čímž se rozumí zahájení festivalu, premiéra, vernisáž, křest knihy nebo CD apod. Jeden žadatel může podat maximálně tři žádosti ročně. Na dotace SFK není právní nárok. K úhradě poskytnutých dotací dojde až po schválení státního rozpočtu na rok 2027, tj. po 1. 1. 2027. Bude-li zjištěna závažná chyba anebo nesrovnalost v žádosti nebo v některé z povinných příloh v průběhu posuzování žádosti, rada SFK si vyhrazuje právo tuto žádost dodatečně vyloučit bez nároku na vrácení poplatku (to se týká zejména formuláře rozpočtu projektu či jeho harmonogramu). Ve výzvě se objevuje kategorie „ celoroční činnost “. Ta je určena pro subjekty, jejichž projekt spočívá v realizaci celoroční kontinuální činnosti (tj. zejména celoroční činnost institucí/ souborů nebo kontinuální vydávání periodik, obsahující dílčí výstupy celoročně probíhajícího projektu. Žadatel předkládající tuto žádost nemůže již předkládat další žádosti, které by se týkaly jednotlivých dílčích výstupů/ projektů obsažených v této celoroční činnosti. Žádosti o podporu celoroční činnosti by měly předkládat zejména ty subjekty , jež mají opravdu dlouhodobý a konkrétní plán své činnosti a realizují svůj projekt po celý kalendářní rok. Jinými slovy subjekty, jež mají definitivně stanovený celoroční vydavatelský plán (časopisy, nakladatelství) anebo uzavřený plán výstav, koncertů, vzniku nových představení včetně termínů a podmínek jejich uvedení. Kategorie „celoroční činnosti“ neslouží k podávání žádostí o podporu celoročních provozů souborů či institucí anebo na reprízování již existujících děl. Tato kategorie má posloužit ke snížení celkového počtu žádostí předkládaných SFK a dále pro snížení administrativní zátěže na obou stranách (tj. žadatelů i SFK). Vzhledem k tomu, že SFK neumožňuje následné podstatné změny v podpořených projektech , podávejte takovéto žádosti pouze, pokud je plán Vašeho projektu definitivní a bude možné jej realizovat i v případě, kdy podpora SFK nedosáhne Vámi požadované výše. Pokud navrhovaná podpora SFK neumožňuje realizaci projektu ve Vámi specifikovaném rozsahu (tj. dle popisu projektu v žádosti o dotaci), doporučujeme návrh smlouvy o poskytnutí účelové dotace nepodepisovat a dotaci písemně odmítnout. Nebude-li projekt realizován v rozsahu odpovídajícím popisu v žádosti o dotaci, bude SFK nucen požadovat vrácení celé přidělené dotace. Podstatnou změnou v projektu se rozumí: - změna termínu realizace, resp. posun do dalšího kalendářního roku anebo mimo původně plánované období (tj. mimo příslušnou třetinu roku), na které žadatel svou žádost podal - změna počtu indikátorů , tj. výstupů projektu uvedených v žádosti (počet realizací pro veřejnost) - zásadní snížení předpokládané kvality projektu Nově se ve formuláři objevuje seznam výstupů projektu = indikátory . Takto uvedený počet výstupů (indikátorů) je pro žadatele závazný i v případech, kdy neobdrží 100% požadované podpory od SFK. Výstupy projektů = počet premiér, počet repríz/uvedení vč. work in progress , počet koncertů anebo workshopů, počet rezidencí, počet realizovaných výstav, počet nově vydávaných titulů knih, čísel časopis",Applications for SFK grants for 2027,"The decisive criterion for selecting the application submission deadline is the date of commencement of the key output, by which is meant the start of the festival, premiere, opening, book launch or CD launch, etc. One applicant may submit a maximum of three applications per year. There is no legal entitlement to SFK grants. Payment of the granted subsidies will take place only after the approval of the state budget for 2027, i.e. after 1 January 2027. If a serious error or discrepancy is found in the application or in any of the mandatory attachments during the assessment of the application, the SFK Council reserves the right to subsequently exclude this application without entitlement to reimbursement of the fee (this applies especially to the project budget form or its timetable). The call includes the category ""year-round activity"". It is intended for entities whose project consists of the implementation of year-round continuous activity (i.e. especially year-round activity of institutions/ensembles or continuous publication of periodicals, containing partial outputs of a year-round project). An applicant submitting this application may no longer submit other applications that would relate to individual partial outputs/projects contained in this year-round activity. Applications for support of year-round activity should be submitted especially by those entities that have a truly long-term and concrete plan for their activity and implement their project throughout the calendar year. In other words, entities that have a definitively established year-round publishing plan (magazines, publishing houses) or a closed plan of exhibitions, concerts, creation of new performances including the dates and conditions of their presentation. The category ""year-round activity"" is not intended for applications for support of year-round operation of ensembles or institutions or for re-staging already existing works. This category is intended to reduce the total number of applications submitted to SFK and further to reduce the administrative burden on both sides (i.e. applicants and SFK). Given that SFK does not allow subsequent substantial changes in supported projects, submit such applications only if your project plan is final and it will be possible to implement it even if the SFK support does not reach the amount you requested. If the proposed SFK support does not allow the project to be implemented in the scope specified by you (i.e. according to the project description in the grant application), we recommend not signing the draft contract for the provision of the earmarked grant and refusing the grant in writing. If the project is not implemented in the scope corresponding to the description in the grant application, SFK will be forced to require the return of the entire allocated grant. A substantial change in the project means: - a change in the implementation date, i.e. a shift to the next calendar year or outside the originally planned period (i.e. outside the relevant third of the year) for which the applicant submitted the application - a change in the number of indicators, i.e. project outputs stated in the application (number of public realizations) - a major reduction in the expected quality of the project Newly, the form includes a list of project outputs = indicators. The number of outputs (indicators) stated in this way is binding for the applicant even in cases where they do not receive 100% of the requested support from SFK. Project outputs = number of premieres, number of reprises/presentations incl. work in progress, number of concerts or workshops, number of residencies, number of realized exhibitions, number of newly published book titles, magazine issues",od 4. do 12. února 2027,2027-02-12,2026-09-23 13:55:11.863391+00:00
mk_statni_fond_kultury_cz_67d96aededd5,mk_statni_fond_kultury_cz,https://www.mk.gov.cz/zadosti-o-dotace-sfk-na-rok-2026,https://dpmkportal.mk.gov.cz/,Státní fond kultury ČR,Rada SFK vyhlašuje pro rok 2026 opět 3 výzvy k přijímání žádostí o podporu projektů s následujícími termíny:,"profesionální umění, literatura a knihovny, média a audiovize",grant,Česká republika,,podporu projektů,,,The SFK Council announces again for the year 2026 3 calls for the submission of applications for support of projects with the following deadlines:,"professional art, literature and libraries, media and audiovisual",grant,,Czech Republic,,"['Literature/Writing', 'Other/Non-Arts', 'Film/Video']",['Grant/Funding'],[],['Czech Republic'],"[{'category': 'Other/Unspecified Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'подporu projektů (support for projects)'}]",2026-09-24 08:58:13.097953+00:00,,,,,cs,Žádosti o dotace SFK na rok 2026,"Jeden žadatel může podat maximálně tři žádosti ročně. Na dotace SFK není právní nárok. Vzhledem k tomu, že SFK neumožňuje následné podstatné změny v podpořených projektech , podávejte takovéto žádosti pouze, pokud je plán Vašeho projektu definitivní a bude možné jej realizovat i v případě, kdy podpora SFK nedosáhne Vámi požadované výše. Pokud navrhovaná podpora SFK neumožňuje realizaci projektu ve Vámi specifikovaném rozsahu (tj. dle popisu projektu v žádosti o dotaci), doporučujeme návrh smlouvy o poskytnutí účelové dotace nepodepisovat a dotaci písemně odmítnout. Nebude-li projekt realizován v rozsahu odpovídajícím popisu v žádosti o dotaci, bude SFK nucen požadovat vrácení celé přidělené dotace. Podstatnou změnou v projektu se rozumí: - změna termínu realizace, resp. posun do dalšího kalendářního roku anebo mimo původně plánované období (tj. mimo příslušnou třetinu roku), na které žadatel svou žádost podal - změna počtu indikátorů , tj. výstupů projektu uvedených v žádosti (počet realizací pro veřejnost) - zásadní snížení předpokládané kvality projektu Nově se ve formuláři objevuje seznam výstupů projektu = indikátory . Takto uvedený počet výstupů (indikátorů) je pro žadatele závazný i v případech, kdy neobdrží 100% požadované podpory od SFK. Výstupy projektů = počet premiér, počet repríz/uvedení vč. work in progress , počet koncertů anebo workshopů, počet rezidencí, počet realizovaných výstav, počet nově vydávaných titulů knih, čísel časopisů,",SFK grant applications for 2026,"One applicant may submit a maximum of three applications per year. There is no legal entitlement to SFK grants. Given that SFK does not allow subsequent substantial changes to supported projects, submit such applications only if your project plan is final and it will be possible to implement it even if SFK support does not reach the amount requested by you. If the proposed SFK support does not make it possible to implement the project in the scope specified by you (i.e. according to the project description in the grant application), we recommend not signing the draft agreement on the provision of the designated grant and rejecting the grant in writing. If the project is not implemented to an extent corresponding to the description in the grant application, SFK will be forced to demand the return of the entire allocated grant. A substantial change in the project means: - a change in the implementation date, i.e. a shift to the following calendar year or outside the originally planned period (i.e. outside the relevant third of the year) for which the applicant submitted the application - a change in the number of indicators, i.e. project outputs listed in the application (number of public presentations) - a significant reduction in the expected quality of the project A list of project outputs = indicators has newly appeared in the form. The number of outputs (indicators) stated in this way is binding for the applicant even in cases where they do not receive 100% of the requested support from SFK. Project outputs = number of premieres, number of repeat performances/presentations incl. work in progress, number of concerts or workshops, number of residencies, number of realized exhibitions, number of newly published book titles, issues of magazines,",od 25. do 31. srpna 2025,2025-09-25,2026-09-23 13:55:14.741536+00:00
norwegian_crafts_ec6cbcf93e7d,norwegian_crafts,https://norwegiancrafts.no/opportunities/support-scheme-for-international-craft-projects,https://grants.norwegianartsabroad.no/utlysning/F23E7754-6017-4D70-A20C-2CF5A3E09924?25,Norwegian Crafts,The support scheme for international craft projects is funded by the Norwegian Ministry of Foreign Affairs and administered by Norwegian Crafts.,crafts / duodji,support scheme,Norway,,"Annual budget: 1,200,000 NOK",,,The support scheme for international craft projects is funded by the Norwegian Ministry of Foreign Affairs and administered by Norwegian Crafts.,crafts / duodji,support scheme,,Norway,,['Craft'],['Grant/Funding'],[],['Norway'],[],2026-09-24 08:58:13.097956+00:00,,,,,en,Support Scheme for International Craft Projects,"You can apply for this scheme if you work in the field of crafts and are: craft artist or duojár part of an artist group a curator a writer/critic Applicants must be: Norwegian citizens or residents of Norway, and the project must be realised abroad. Registered as a sole proprietorship with an organisation number You cannot apply on behalf of or as a representative of: exhibition venues institutions other organisers",Support Scheme for International Craft Projects,"You can apply for this scheme if you work in the field of crafts and are: craft artist or duojár part of an artist group a curator a writer/critic Applicants must be: Norwegian citizens or residents of Norway, and the project must be realised abroad. Registered as a sole proprietorship with an organisation number You cannot apply on behalf of or as a representative of: exhibition venues institutions other organisers","15 February, 15 May and 15 October at 14:00 CET",2027-02-15,2026-09-23 13:55:14.760132+00:00
norwegian_crafts_ec6807d7b33a,norwegian_crafts,https://norwegiancrafts.no/opportunities/isgies,https://grants.norwegianartsabroad.no/utlysning/90CDFF90-179A-4D8B-A552-F62D2CFE3060,OCA – Office for Contemporary Art Norway on behalf of OCA and Norwegian Crafts (NC),"The purpose of the ISGIES scheme is to enhance the participation of Norway-based galleries, independent exhibition spaces and art book publishers at international art fairs. ISGIES aims to stimulate international participation, especially in major art fairs, and increase the demand for contemporary visual art from Norway.",contemporary visual art,Funding,Norway,,Annual budget (2026): 4 072 571 NOK,,,"The purpose of the ISGIES scheme is to enhance the participation of Norway-based galleries, independent exhibition spaces and art book publishers at international art fairs. ISGIES aims to stimulate international participation, especially in major art fairs, and increase the demand for contemporary visual art from Norway.",contemporary visual art,Funding,,Norway,,['Visual Arts'],['Grant/Funding'],[],['Norway'],[],2026-09-24 08:58:13.097958+00:00,,,,,en,International Support for Galleries and Independent Exhibition Spaces,"Norwegian galleries and independent exhibition spaces that are invited to participate in one of the listed art fairs
Norwegian art book publishers that are invited to participate in one of the listed art book fairs
Eligibility requirements for galleries and independent exhibition spaces Applicants
 must present at least one Norwegian or Norway-based contemporary artist
 at one of the international art fairs included in the list of eligible 
art fairs. Artists involved in the operation of the gallery are not 
included in this minimum requirement. The ISGIES scheme does not cover Kunsthalles, art societies, art centres, or individual artists.
Eligibility requirements for art book publishers Applicants
 must present at least three publications about or featuring Norwegian 
or Norway-based contemporary artists at one of the international art book fairs included in the list of eligible art fairs. Of these 
publications, at least three must be registered with an ISBN. 
Publications that present artists involved in the publishing company are
 not included in this minimum requirement. The ISGIES scheme 
does not cover individual artists working with printed matter.",International Support for Galleries and Independent Exhibition Spaces,"Norwegian galleries and independent exhibition spaces that are invited to participate in one of the listed art fairs
Norwegian art book publishers that are invited to participate in one of the listed art book fairs
Eligibility requirements for galleries and independent exhibition spaces Applicants
 must present at least one Norwegian or Norway-based contemporary artist
 at one of the international art fairs included in the list of eligible 
art fairs. Artists involved in the operation of the gallery are not 
included in this minimum requirement. The ISGIES scheme does not cover Kunsthalles, art societies, art centres, or individual artists.
Eligibility requirements for art book publishers Applicants
 must present at least three publications about or featuring Norwegian 
or Norway-based contemporary artists at one of the international art book fairs included in the list of eligible art fairs. Of these 
publications, at least three must be registered with an ISBN. 
Publications that present artists involved in the publishing company are
 not included in this minimum requirement. The ISGIES scheme 
does not cover individual artists working with printed matter.",10 December 2025,2025-12-10,2026-09-23 13:55:14.762939+00:00
