rannis_iceland_8c97d0bb99e2,rannis_iceland,https://en.rannis.is/funding/art-culture/support-for-the-publication-of-books-in-icelandic/,https://sjodir.rannis.is/menu/api/oauth2_callback.php,The Icelandic Centre for Research,To support the publication of books in Icelandic by providing temporary financial aid to publishers in the form of a partial reimbursement of costs incurred in the publication of books in Icelandic.,Art and Culture,support,Iceland,Reykjavík,"The 25% reimbursement only pertains to costs related to the publication of a book, costs without VAT.",,,To support the publication of books in Icelandic by providing temporary financial aid to publishers in the form of a partial reimbursement of costs incurred in the publication of books in Icelandic.,Art and Culture,support,,Iceland,Reykjavík,['Multidisciplinary'],['Grant/Funding'],[],['Iceland'],"[{'category': 'Other/Unspecified Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': '25% reimbursement of eligible publication costs only, excluding VAT'}]",2026-09-24 08:58:15.705930+00:00,,,,,en,Support for the publication of books in Icelandic,"Target group Book publishers, i.e. an individual, group or legal person financially responsible for the publication of a book, registered as a party subject to value added tax pursuant to Article 5 of the Value Added Tax Act, No 50/1988, under code 58.11.0 Book publishing according to the classification of economic activities published by Statistics Iceland. Foreign applicants mustprovide evidence of similar registration of their activities in another country.",Support for the publication of books in Icelandic,"Target group Book publishers, i.e. an individual, group or legal person financially responsible for the publication of a book, registered as a party subject to value added tax pursuant to Article 5 of the Value Added Tax Act, No 50/1988, under code 58.11.0 Book publishing according to the classification of economic activities published by Statistics Iceland. Foreign applicants mustprovide evidence of similar registration of their activities in another country.",Open for applications all year round. An application must be received no later than nine months after the publication of the book concerned.,2027-06-24,2026-09-23 13:55:18.318829+00:00
roberto_cimetta_fund_23ba036056c8,roberto_cimetta_fund,https://www.cimettafund.org/en/blog/2026/09/22/emergency-mobility-grants-2027-roberto-cimetta-fund-opens-an-emergency-call/,https://www.cimettafund.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/RCF-Emergency-Mobility-Grants-2027-Application-Form-EN.docx,Roberto Cimetta Fund,"The Roberto Cimetta Fund is opening a call to fund professional travel for artists and cultural professionals from Lebanon, Syria, Palestine, Yemen and Sudan.",performing arts and multidisciplinary practices,grant,,,"Each grant can reach €600 and covers international and national travel, visa and consular processing fees, and a basic daily allowance.",,"If you are at the start of your career and do not have a body of work yet, showing the project you are working on now is enough.","The Roberto Cimetta Fund is opening a call to fund professional travel for artists and cultural professionals from Lebanon, Syria, Palestine, Yemen and Sudan.",performing arts and multidisciplinary practices,grant,"If you are at the start of your career and do not have a body of work yet, showing the project you are working on now is enough.",,,"['Performing Arts', 'Multidisciplinary']",['Grant/Funding'],['Emerging/Early-Career'],[],"[{'category': 'Travel Support', 'amount_min': 600.0, 'amount_max': 600.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'covers international and national travel, visa and consular processing fees'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'basic daily allowance included, amount not stated'}]",2026-09-24 08:58:15.705934+00:00,,,,,en,Emergency Mobility Grants 2027,"The call is open to artists and cultural professionals from Lebanon, Syria, Palestine, Yemen and Sudan, whether they live in those countries or come from them and live elsewhere. Individual artists and constituted groups are both eligible. Cultural structures can take part only as hosts or inviting partners, within a professional collaboration. There is no age limit. The call is restricted to performing arts and multidisciplinary practices. Three types of activity are supported: professional training, creation and residency, dissemination and networking.",Emergency Mobility Grants 2027,"The call is open to artists and cultural professionals from Lebanon, Syria, Palestine, Yemen and Sudan, whether they live in those countries or come from them and live elsewhere. Individual artists and constituted groups are both eligible. Cultural structures can take part only as hosts or inviting partners, within a professional collaboration. There is no age limit. The call is restricted to performing arts and multidisciplinary practices. Three types of activity are supported: professional training, creation and residency, dissemination and networking.",1 November 2026,2026-11-01,2026-09-23 13:55:18.322318+00:00
acc_galerie_weimar_0f141ef27564,acc_galerie_weimar,https://acc-weimar.de/getmedia.php/_media/202609/122074v0-orig.pdf,,ACC Galerie Weimar and the City of Weimar,"The 33rd International Studio Program of the ACC Galerie Weimar and the City of Weimar invites artists of all nationalities and disciplines to submit proposals for projects that explore absence and the absent through art, rethink absence in radically new ways, challenge it aesthetically, or use it as a tool for social critique.",artists of all nationalities and disciplines,International Studio Program,Germany,Weimar,The support provided includes the provision of a combination artist's studio/apartment in the Municipal Studio Building.,,,"The 33rd International Studio Program of the ACC Galerie Weimar and the City of Weimar invites artists of all nationalities and disciplines to submit proposals for projects that explore absence and the absent through art, rethink absence in radically new ways, challenge it aesthetically, or use it as a tool for social critique.",artists of all nationalities and disciplines,International Studio Program,,Germany,Weimar,['Multidisciplinary'],['Residency'],[],['Germany'],"[{'category': 'Accommodation/Housing', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': ""combination artist's studio/apartment in the Municipal Studio Building""}]",2026-09-24 09:59:00.165390+00:00,,,,,en,33rd International Studio Program of the ACC Galerie Weimar and the City of Weimar OPEN CALL 2026: On Absence,"The 33rd International Studio Program of the ACC Galerie Weimar and the City of Weimar invites artists of all nationalities and disciplines to submit proposals for projects that explore absence and the absent through art, rethink absence in radically new ways, challenge it aesthetically, or use it as a tool for social critique.",33rd International Studio Program of the ACC Galerie Weimar and the City of Weimar OPEN CALL 2026: On Absence,"The 33rd International Studio Program of the ACC Galerie Weimar and the City of Weimar invites artists of all nationalities and disciplines to submit proposals for projects that explore absence and the absent through art, rethink absence in radically new ways, challenge it aesthetically, or use it as a tool for social critique.",,,2026-09-24 09:56:27.484709+00:00
arts_council_wales_21e3fea04b22,arts_council_wales,https://arts.wales/funding/individuals/create-and-engage,https://portal.arts.wales/?_gl=1*opjewb*_ga*MTk4NjQ0NjQxLjE3NzQyNTkzMjY.*_ga_QKYVV0TTMM*czE3NzQyNzg0NzUkbzIkZzEkdDE3NzQyNzkzODQkajQ1JGwwJGgw&_ga=2.198074031.1818258139.1774259329-198644641.1774259326,Arts Council of Wales,"funds the development, creation and delivery of high-quality arts experiences that help creative individuals and organisations engage with and connect to the public.",arts,fund,Wales,,"There are two levels of award: small, up to £10,000 and large, up to £60,000. In exceptional circumstances, organisations can apply for up to £100,000 by prior agreement with a Relationship Manager.",,,"funds the development, creation and delivery of high-quality arts experiences that help creative individuals and organisations engage with and connect to the public.",arts,fund,,Wales,,['Multidisciplinary'],['Grant/Funding'],[],['United Kingdom'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 10000.0, 'amount_max': 10000.0, 'currency': 'GBP', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'small award, up to £10,000'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 60000.0, 'amount_max': 60000.0, 'currency': 'GBP', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'large award, up to £60,000'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 100000.0, 'amount_max': 100000.0, 'currency': 'GBP', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'exceptional circumstances, up to £100,000 by prior agreement'}]",2026-09-24 09:59:00.165413+00:00,,,,,en,Create and Engage,"Organisations and individuals can apply. Take a look at our eligibility criteria for organisations and our eligibility criteria for individuals to see if you are eligible. Please note: For individuals looking to develop their own practice rather than make work, please see our Creative Practice fund . If you are an organisation applying for a Festival, please click here . If you are applying for Research and Development, please click here . If you are applying for a Major Production, please click here . Applications must be focussed on the artforms that we support . Your project must take place mainly in Wales We can only fund activities or events taking place outside of Wales where you can demonstrate longer-term benefit to individuals and communities within Wales. We can consider funding some international activity as part of a wider project if a clear rationale is given. Your project must complement and enhance your usual programme of activity This means it should not be part of your core activity or include core costs. This is particularly the case with Multi Year Funded Organisations. Your proposal should be for new activity, or work linked to an upcoming opportunity (such as a specific commission, collaboration, presentation, development period, or public engagement activity). This funding should enable you to do more than you would be able to without it, like reaching more people or expanding the quality or scale of your work. Your project must involve working with others The best projects happen when partners are involved. We’ll expect to see you working with at least one other individual or organisation who’ll support you to develop and deliver your project. This could be: a partner organisation artistic collaborator critical friend artistic mentor community group Your project must be time limited This means it has a definite start and end date. It’s a good idea to allow yourself some extra time in case you need to send us more information following an award being made. You must have other funding to contribute to the overall costs of your project We can only support 90% of the project costs. At least 10% of your project income should come from a non-Arts Council or National Lottery source. This other funding can include Support in Kind. Take a look at our Budget help notes for more information. You must allow adequate lead time We’ll expect to see sufficient time built into your project to deliver the work effectively. This is particularly important when it comes to any promotional, audience development or outreach work. It is important to plan your project carefully, including costs, timescales and getting support for your project before you start to fill out an application. You can only apply to one fund at a time, we cannot accept another application until you have received a decision. The exception to this rule is when we might launch targeted strategic funds. We will consider the number of live projects you have when assessing the distribution of funding to organisations and individuals.",Create and Engage,"Organisations and individuals can apply. Take a look at our eligibility criteria for organisations and our eligibility criteria for individuals to see if you are eligible. Please note: For individuals looking to develop their own practice rather than make work, please see our Creative Practice fund . If you are an organisation applying for a Festival, please click here . If you are applying for Research and Development, please click here . If you are applying for a Major Production, please click here . Applications must be focussed on the artforms that we support . Your project must take place mainly in Wales We can only fund activities or events taking place outside of Wales where you can demonstrate longer-term benefit to individuals and communities within Wales. We can consider funding some international activity as part of a wider project if a clear rationale is given. Your project must complement and enhance your usual programme of activity This means it should not be part of your core activity or include core costs. This is particularly the case with Multi Year Funded Organisations. Your proposal should be for new activity, or work linked to an upcoming opportunity (such as a specific commission, collaboration, presentation, development period, or public engagement activity). This funding should enable you to do more than you would be able to without it, like reaching more people or expanding the quality or scale of your work. Your project must involve working with others The best projects happen when partners are involved. We’ll expect to see you working with at least one other individual or organisation who’ll support you to develop and deliver your project. This could be: a partner organisation artistic collaborator critical friend artistic mentor community group Your project must be time limited This means it has a definite start and end date. It’s a good idea to allow yourself some extra time in case you need to send us more information following an award being made. You must have other funding to contribute to the overall costs of your project We can only support 90% of the project costs. At least 10% of your project income should come from a non-Arts Council or National Lottery source. This other funding can include Support in Kind. Take a look at our Budget help notes for more information. You must allow adequate lead time We’ll expect to see sufficient time built into your project to deliver the work effectively. This is particularly important when it comes to any promotional, audience development or outreach work. It is important to plan your project carefully, including costs, timescales and getting support for your project before you start to fill out an application. You can only apply to one fund at a time, we cannot accept another application until you have received a decision. The exception to this rule is when we might launch targeted strategic funds. We will consider the number of live projects you have when assessing the distribution of funding to organisations and individuals.",Wednesday 29 April 2026 Wednesday 29 July 2026 Wednesday 30 September 2026 Wednesday 16 December 2026,2026-12-26,2026-09-24 09:56:27.876711+00:00
arts_council_wales_d3407bbb0781,arts_council_wales,https://arts.wales/funding/individuals/creative-practice,https://arts.wales/start,Arts Council of Wales,"Creative Practice grants are designed to support you as an artist or creative professional, investing in your growth and future. They allow you to dedicate time and space for creative experimentation, professional development and to work in new ways. Rather than funding predetermined outcomes, these grants encourage exploration and innovation—whether that means testing new ideas, developing fresh approaches, or engaging in opportunities such as mentoring and training.","Visual or applied artists and curators Theatre practitioners including directors, producers etc Dancers and dance professionals including choreographers and movement directors Musicians, composers and music creators Circus performers and practitioners Multidisciplinary artists Community arts practitioners",grant,Wales,,"You can apply for between £500 and £10,000.",,,"Creative Practice grants are designed to support you as an artist or creative professional, investing in your growth and future. They allow you to dedicate time and space for creative experimentation, professional development and to work in new ways. Rather than funding predetermined outcomes, these grants encourage exploration and innovation—whether that means testing new ideas, developing fresh approaches, or engaging in opportunities such as mentoring and training.","Visual or applied artists and curators Theatre practitioners including directors, producers etc Dancers and dance professionals including choreographers and movement directors Musicians, composers and music creators Circus performers and practitioners Multidisciplinary artists Community arts practitioners",grant,,Wales,,"['Visual Arts', 'Theatre', 'Dance', 'Music', 'Circus/Street Arts', 'Multidisciplinary']",['Grant/Funding'],[],['United Kingdom'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 500.0, 'amount_max': 10000.0, 'currency': 'GBP', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'between £500 and £10,000'}]",2026-09-24 09:59:00.166199+00:00,,,,,en,Creative Practice,"Individual artists and creative professionals working in the arts can apply. Take a look at our eligibility criteria for individuals to see if you are eligible. Those eligible to apply include but are not limited to: Visual or applied artists and curators Theatre practitioners including directors, producers etc Dancers and dance professionals including choreographers and movement directors Musicians, composers and music creators Circus performers and practitioners Multidisciplinary artists Community arts practitioners Examples of creative practitioners we can’t support include: Commercial professionals. e.g. designers or retail-focussed makers, musicians making commercial music Filmmakers (please see Ffilm Cymru) Literary writers (please see Literature Wales) Please note - The aim of this fund is to support the development of your creative practice and not commercial activities / ventures. You must have a track record as an artist or creative professional in one of the areas we support . You may have had breaks, and your creative practice does not have to be your main source of income, but you must have demonstrable artistic or creative experience.",Creative Practice,"Individual artists and creative professionals working in the arts can apply. Take a look at our eligibility criteria for individuals to see if you are eligible. Those eligible to apply include but are not limited to: Visual or applied artists and curators Theatre practitioners including directors, producers etc Dancers and dance professionals including choreographers and movement directors Musicians, composers and music creators Circus performers and practitioners Multidisciplinary artists Community arts practitioners Examples of creative practitioners we can’t support include: Commercial professionals. e.g. designers or retail-focussed makers, musicians making commercial music Filmmakers (please see Ffilm Cymru) Literary writers (please see Literature Wales) Please note - The aim of this fund is to support the development of your creative practice and not commercial activities / ventures. You must have a track record as an artist or creative professional in one of the areas we support . You may have had breaks, and your creative practice does not have to be your main source of income, but you must have demonstrable artistic or creative experience.",Wednesday 20th May 2026 Wednesday 9th September 2026 All deadlines are 1pm on the dates stated.,2026-09-20,2026-09-24 09:56:28.254935+00:00
arts_council_wales_ed6fc62d20dc,arts_council_wales,https://arts.wales/funding/individuals/creative-steps-for-individuals,https://arts.wales/eligibility-individuals,Arts Council of Wales,"Creative Steps funds the professional, business and organisational development of artists who have experienced barriers to careers within the arts.",Music and Opera Visual and Applied Arts Dance Theatre and Performing Arts Digital/Immersive and/or interdisciplinary arts Engagement and Community Young People and Skills Circus and Outdoor Arts Health and Wellbeing,funding,Wales,,"Applicants can apply for between £500 and £7,500 (plus access costs)",,,"Creative Steps funds the professional, business and organisational development of artists who have experienced barriers to careers within the arts.",Music and Opera Visual and Applied Arts Dance Theatre and Performing Arts Digital/Immersive and/or interdisciplinary arts Engagement and Community Young People and Skills Circus and Outdoor Arts Health and Wellbeing,funding,,Wales,,"['Music', 'Dance', 'Theatre', 'Visual Arts', 'Digital/New Media Arts', 'Multidisciplinary', 'Circus/Street Arts']",['Grant/Funding'],[],['United Kingdom'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 500.0, 'amount_max': 7500.0, 'currency': 'GBP', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'between £500 and £7,500'}, {'category': 'Other/Unspecified Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'plus access costs'}]",2026-09-24 09:59:00.166227+00:00,,,,,en,Creative Steps for Individuals,"Creative Steps for Individuals is open to individual artists and creatives who identify as being Ethnically and Culturally diverse, D/deaf, disabled or neurodivergent. Research shows that these groups are underrepresented within our funding programmes due to barriers to entry. You must have demonstratable experience as an artist or creative professional. If you do not have this experience, we may still be able to support you if you submit a portfolio, CV or examples of your work with your application. We may decide to fund you based on your artistic potential. You can discuss this with a Relationship Manager.",Creative Steps for Individuals,"Creative Steps for Individuals is open to individual artists and creatives who identify as being Ethnically and Culturally diverse, D/deaf, disabled or neurodivergent. Research shows that these groups are underrepresented within our funding programmes due to barriers to entry. You must have demonstratable experience as an artist or creative professional. If you do not have this experience, we may still be able to support you if you submit a portfolio, CV or examples of your work with your application. We may decide to fund you based on your artistic potential. You can discuss this with a Relationship Manager.",21 October 2026,2026-10-21,2026-09-24 09:56:28.261844+00:00
arts_council_wales_f8da4d62c750,arts_council_wales,https://arts.wales/funding/creative-learning/have-a-go,https://portal.arts.wales/?_ga=2.115818561.650259225.1730367273-1807098631.1730367273&_gl=1*1lqjs6l*_ga*MTgwNzA5ODYzMS4xNzMwMzY3Mjcz*_ga_QKYVV0TTMM*MTczMDM3ODEyNS4yLjEuMTczMDM3OTEzMi44LjAuMA..,Arts Council of Wales,Have a Go is designed to provide learners aged 3 – 16 with opportunities to have a go at a one-off hands-on activity or workshop to support schools with the delivery of the Expressive Arts Area of Learning and Experience.,"art, dance, drama, film and digital media and music",grant,Wales,,"The fund offers grants of up to £1,500",,,Have a Go is designed to provide learners aged 3 – 16 with opportunities to have a go at a one-off hands-on activity or workshop to support schools with the delivery of the Expressive Arts Area of Learning and Experience.,"art, dance, drama, film and digital media and music",grant,,Wales,,"['Visual Arts', 'Dance', 'Theatre', 'Film/Video', 'Music']",['Grant/Funding'],[],['United Kingdom'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 1500.0, 'amount_max': 1500.0, 'currency': 'USD', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'up to $1,500'}]",2026-09-24 09:59:00.166251+00:00,,,,,en,Have a Go,"Have a Go is available to support: All state-maintained schools in Wales for pupils aged 3 – 16years. Pupil referral units in Wales for pupils aged 3 – 16 years. We are unable to support post 16 education, including FE Colleges and Sixth Form. Have a Go applications can be submitted by: A state-maintained school. A pupil referral unit. An arts/cultural organisation based in Wales.",Have a Go,"Have a Go is available to support: All state-maintained schools in Wales for pupils aged 3 – 16years. Pupil referral units in Wales for pupils aged 3 – 16 years. We are unable to support post 16 education, including FE Colleges and Sixth Form. Have a Go applications can be submitted by: A state-maintained school. A pupil referral unit. An arts/cultural organisation based in Wales.",,,2026-09-24 09:56:28.261905+00:00
arts_council_wales_b3ec3ab6ac65,arts_council_wales,https://arts.wales/funding/creative-learning/go-and-see,https://portal.arts.wales/?_ga=2.51267822.650259225.1730367273-1807098631.1730367273&_gl=1*6vhbb9*_ga*MTgwNzA5ODYzMS4xNzMwMzY3Mjcz*_ga_QKYVV0TTMM*MTczMDM3ODEyNS4yLjEuMTczMDM3OTk0My42MC4wLjA.,Arts Council of Wales,"The Go and See Fund offers grants up to £1,000 to enable teachers in state-maintained schools in Wales to take their learners to see high-quality art in venues across Wales.","drama, dance, music, art, a cultural festival or any other high-quality arts experience",grant,Wales,,"grants up to £1,000",,,"The Go and See Fund offers grants up to £1,000 to enable teachers in state-maintained schools in Wales to take their learners to see high-quality art in venues across Wales.","drama, dance, music, art, a cultural festival or any other high-quality arts experience",grant,,Wales,,"['Dance', 'Music', 'Visual Arts', 'Other/Non-Arts']",['Grant/Funding'],[],['United Kingdom'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 1000.0, 'amount_max': 1000.0, 'currency': 'USD', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'up to $1,000'}]",2026-09-24 09:59:00.166268+00:00,,,,,en,Go and See,"Go and See applications can only be submitted by: State-maintained schools in Wales for learners aged 3 – 16years. Pupil referral units in Wales for learners aged 3 – 16 years. Unfortunately, we cannot support applications from applicants outside of state-maintained schools or pupil referral units. Schools and pupil referral units can apply to the Go and See Fund more than once throughout the year but must submit completion reports before reapplying.",Go and See,"Go and See applications can only be submitted by: State-maintained schools in Wales for learners aged 3 – 16years. Pupil referral units in Wales for learners aged 3 – 16 years. Unfortunately, we cannot support applications from applicants outside of state-maintained schools or pupil referral units. Schools and pupil referral units can apply to the Go and See Fund more than once throughout the year but must submit completion reports before reapplying.",01/09/2026,2026-01-09,2026-09-24 09:56:28.267716+00:00
arts_council_wales_5ee8a82ba7a5,arts_council_wales,https://arts.wales/funding/creative-learning/extend-creative-leadership-programme,https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfLUpCImungWfxNaV6LBlh5dOcIHeP_gFlr59iAmP8a46CQmg/viewform,Arts Council of Wales and Welsh Government,"Funded opportunity to join the Creative Leadership Programme, a partnership between the Arts Council of Wales and Welsh Government",creative learning,programme,Wales,,"Each school leader will receive supply cover costs to attend the training, networking meetings and sharing event.",,middle/senior school leaders,"Funded opportunity to join the Creative Leadership Programme, a partnership between the Arts Council of Wales and Welsh Government",creative learning,programme,middle/senior school leaders,Wales,,['Other/Non-Arts'],['Other'],['Other/Unspecified'],['United Kingdom'],"[{'category': 'Other/Unspecified Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'supply cover costs for school leaders to attend training, networking meetings and sharing event'}, {'category': 'Mentorship/Training', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'training, networking meetings and sharing event'}]",2026-09-24 09:59:00.166283+00:00,,,,,en,Extend: Creative Leadership Programme,"This provision is predominantly for those in or aspiring to middle or senior leadership roles, though we encourage the awareness of leadership in every role. It is for leaders of learning in all Areas of Learning Experience and not just the Expressive Arts. You must be a state maintained early years or school setting in Wales to be eligible. We would particularly welcome expressions of interest from applicants from culturally and ethnically diverse backgrounds.",Extend: Creative Leadership Programme,"This provision is predominantly for those in or aspiring to middle or senior leadership roles, though we encourage the awareness of leadership in every role. It 