can_serrat_7af35b9c036f,can_serrat,https://canserrat.org/programa-de-residencia,https://canserrat.org/en-visual-art-residency-open-call-2027,Can Serrat,"The international residency program invites writers and contemporary artists from around the world to take part in short- and medium-term residencies. Can Serrat opens calls throughout the year, some of which include one or two full grants and several partial grants.",writers and contemporary artists,residency,Spain,El Bruc - Barcelona,some of which include one or two full grants and several partial grants.,,,"The international residency program invites writers and contemporary artists from around the world to take part in short- and medium-term residencies. Can Serrat opens calls throughout the year, some of which include one or two full grants and several partial grants.",writers and contemporary artists,residency,,Spain,El Bruc - Barcelona,"['Literature/Writing', 'Visual Arts']",['Residency'],[],['Spain'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'one or two full grants and several partial grants; no amounts stated'}]",2026-09-24 09:59:00.166288+00:00,,,,,en,Art Residency Program,The international residency program invites writers and contemporary artists from around the world to take part in short- and medium-term residencies.,Art Residency Program,The international residency program invites writers and contemporary artists from around the world to take part in short- and medium-term residencies.,,,2026-09-24 09:56:28.276415+00:00
culture_gouv_fr_1pct_36fcf9b8113a,culture_gouv_fr_1pct,https://www.culture.gouv.fr/catalogue-des-demarches-et-subventions/appels-a-projets-candidatures/prix-du-1-artistique,https://demarche.numerique.gouv.fr/commencer/arts-plastiques_prix-1-artistique,Ministère de la Culture / DGCA > Pôle de la commande artistique,"Le Prix du 1% artistique, qui s’inscrit dans la continuité de l’engagement de l’Etat en faveur de la commande publique artistique, récompensera des œuvres exemplaires et récentes réalisées dans le cadre de l’obligation de décoration des constructions publiques.",Arts plastiques,Prix,France,Paris,Le Prix récompense au total trois œuvres installées dans l’espace public,,,"The 1% artistic Prize, which is part of the continuity of the State's commitment in favor of public artistic commissions, will reward exemplary and recent works carried out within the framework of the obligation to decorate public buildings.",Fine arts,Price,,France,Paris,['Visual Arts'],[],[],['France'],"[{'category': 'Exhibition/Presentation Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'award for three works installed in public space'}]",2026-09-24 09:59:00.166292+00:00,,,,,fr,Prix du 1% artistique,"Qui peut déposer un dossier ?
Communes
Départements
EPCI à fiscalité propre
Établissements publics / Services de l'État soumis au 1% artistique

Critères d'éligibilité du projet
Les œuvres originales éligibles à cette récompense devront respecter l’ensemble des critères suivants :
Être issues d’une commande réalisée dans les conditions de passation des marchés ayant pour objet de satisfaire l’obligation de décoration des constructions publiques ;
Être portées par une collectivité publique soumise à l’obligation de décoration des constructions publiques ou par une collectivité ou un établissement public ayant appliqué l’une des procédures décrites aux articles R. 2172-9 à R. 2172.14 du code de la commande publique ;
Relever strictement des arts plastiques ou graphiques et entrant dans les catégories définies aux 7° à 10° de l'article L. 112-2 du code de la propriété intellectuelle, ou relever des œuvres numériques ou faisant appel à d’autres créations artistiques pour l’aménagement d’espaces paysagers.
Sont éligibles les œuvres dont le commencement d’exécution est postérieur au 1 er janvier 2018 à 00h00 et dont l’achèvement est intervenu, au plus tard le 15 octobre 2026 à 23h59.
Lorsqu’une opération immobilière a donné lieu :
A l’installation de plusieurs œuvres au titre d’une même procédure du fait d’un allotissement, chacune d’elle doit faire l’objet d’une candidature distincte et sera examinée individuellement ;
A la désignation d’un groupement ou collectif d’artistes pour une ou plusieurs œuvres réalisées dans le cadre d’un même allotissement, une seule candidature est admise et le Prix pourra être attribuée au groupement ou au collectif.

Critères de non-éligibilité du projet
Ne sont pas éligibles les interventions artistiques de nature évènementielle et relevant strictement de la manifestation artistique.",Prix of the 1% artistic,"Who can submit an application?
Communes
Departments
EPCI with their own taxation
Public establishments / State services subject to the 1% artistic

Project eligibility criteria
The original works eligible for this prize must meet all of the following criteria:
Be the result of a commission carried out under the conditions for awarding contracts intended to satisfy the obligation to decorate public buildings;
Be carried by a public authority subject to the obligation to decorate public buildings or by a local authority or a public establishment having applied one of the procedures described in articles R. 2172-9 to R. 2172.14 of the public procurement code;
Strictly fall within the plastic or graphic arts and come under the categories defined in 7° to 10° of article L. 112-2 of the Intellectual Property Code, or be digital works or works using other artistic creations for the development of landscaped spaces.
Eligible are works whose commencement of execution is after 1 January 2018 at 00:00 and whose completion occurred no later than 15 October 2026 at 23:59.
Where a real estate operation has given rise:
To the installation of several works under the same procedure because of a lot division, each of them must be the subject of a separate application and will be examined individually;
To the designation of a grouping or collective of artists for one or more works carried out within the framework of the same lot division, only one application is admitted and the Prize may be awarded to the grouping or the collective.

Project non-eligibility criteria
Artistic interventions of an event-based nature and strictly relating to the artistic event are not eligible.",2 novembre 2026,2026-11-02,2026-09-24 09:56:30.858762+00:00
dansateliers_rotterdam_e3404a6adf78,dansateliers_rotterdam,https://dansateliers.nl/en/news/open-call-choreographic-encounters/,,Dansateliers and choreographer Amparo González Sola,Dansateliers and choreographer Amparo González Sola invite choreographers to apply for the first edition of the Choreographic Encounters Laboratory. This edition will explore choreographic procedures and strategies of attention in a peer-to-peer environment.,choreography / dance,laboratory,The Netherlands,Rotterdam,"• Shared accommodation with the other artists (private bedroom)
• Travel costs in The Netherlands: public transport to and from Rotterdam will be covered.
• EU: up to €400 for travel to and from Rotterdam. We encourage travelling by train.
• Artist fee including per diem",,,Dansateliers and choreographer Amparo González Sola invite choreographers to apply for the first edition of the Choreographic Encounters Laboratory. This edition will explore choreographic procedures and strategies of attention in a peer-to-peer environment.,choreography / dance,laboratory,,The Netherlands,Rotterdam,['Dance'],['Other'],[],['Netherlands'],"[{'category': 'Accommodation/Housing', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'shared accommodation with private bedroom'}, {'category': 'Travel Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'public transport to and from Rotterdam covered in The Netherlands'}, {'category': 'Travel Support', 'amount_min': 400.0, 'amount_max': 400.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'EU travel to and from Rotterdam, up to €400'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'artist fee including per diem'}]",2026-09-24 09:59:00.166296+00:00,,,,,en,Open Call Choreographic Encounters,"Who can apply? The application is open to artists with a grounded artistic movement practice and an established body of work. Artists are interested in choreographic procedures, tools and audience strategies in relation to their own work. They have experience with peer-to-peer feedback and are interested in and comfortable with sharing their practice and work with others. Please note: We are open to artists with specific access needs. The Dansateliers building is currently not wheelchair accessible. Participants need to be able to climb stairs to reach the studios.

