kunststiftung_nrw_6b36eed08299,kunststiftung_nrw,https://www.kunststiftungnrw.de/visuelle-kunst/foerderung/residenzen/atelier-galata-istanbul/atelier-galata-visuelle-kunst/,https://antragsportal.kunststiftungnrw.de/,Kunststiftung NRW,"Die Kunststiftung NRW vergibt ein Residenzstipendium im Bereich Visuelle Kunst in Istanbul. Ziel des Stipendiums ist es, die Kunstszene vor Ort kennenzulernen, Kontakte zu knüpfen, Ideen auszutauschen und diese Impulse später nach in ihre jeweiligen ihre Arbeitskontexte in Nordrhein-Westfalen einzubringen.",Visuelle Kunst,Residenzstipendium,Turkey,Istanbul,Wohnatelier im Stadtteil Galata Beyoglu Pauschale für Lebenshaltungskosten: monatlich 1.500 Euro Reisekosten bis zu 600 Euro (inkl. MwSt.) Nach vorheriger Absprache: Übernahme von Visagebühren Transport- oder Materialkostenzuschuss Kosten für Übergepäck (Künstlermaterial),,professionelle Kunstschaffende,"Kunststiftung NRW awards a residency scholarship in the field of Visual Arts in Istanbul. The aim of the scholarship is to get to know the local art scene, make contacts, exchange ideas, and later bring these impulses into their respective work contexts in North Rhine-Westphalia.",visual art,residence stipend,professional artists,Turkey,Istanbul,['Visual Arts'],['Grant/Funding'],['Established/Professional'],[],"[{'category': 'Accommodation/Housing', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'residential studio in Galata Beyoglu'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 1500.0, 'amount_max': 1500.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'per month', 'note': 'living expenses allowance'}, {'category': 'Travel Support', 'amount_min': 600.0, 'amount_max': 600.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'travel costs, including VAT'}, {'category': 'Other/Unspecified Support', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'possible visa fees coverage by prior arrangement'}, {'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'transport or materials cost subsidy'}, {'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'excess baggage costs for artist materials'}]",2026-09-24 09:59:19.149003+00:00,,,,,de,Atelier Galata Visuelle Kunst,"Die Ausschreibung ist nicht alterslimitiert. Sie richtet sich an professionelle Kunstschaffende mit Lebensmittelpunkt in Nordrhein-Westfalen, die bereits öffentliche Anerkennung erfahren haben und erste Berufserfolge vorweisen können. Studierende sind ausgeschlossen es besteht Residenzpflicht englische Sprachkenntnisse sind Voraussetzung",Atelier Galata Visual Arts,"The call is not age-limited. It is aimed at professional artists whose center of life is in North Rhine-Westphalia, who have already received public recognition and can demonstrate initial professional success. Students are excluded; residency is mandatory; English language skills are a prerequisite.",Die nächste Antragsfrist wird in Kürze bekannt gegeben.,2026-09-29,2026-09-24 09:58:18.321460+00:00
kunststiftung_nrw_d84895c9fc5f,kunststiftung_nrw,https://www.kunststiftungnrw.de/visuelle-kunst/foerderung/residenzen/tel-aviv/residenzstipendium-tel-aviv/,https://antragsportal.kunststiftungnrw.de/,Kunststiftung NRW,Die Residenz beinhaltet: kostenlose Nutzung einer Wohnung für sechs Monate kostenlose Nutzung eines Ateliers in den Artists’ Studios Pauschale für Lebenshaltungskosten monatlich: 1.500 Euro einmalige Reisekostenpauschale: bis zu 600 Euro,Visuelle Kunst,Residenzstipendium,Israel,Tel Aviv,kostenlose Nutzung einer Wohnung für sechs Monate kostenlose Nutzung eines Ateliers in den Artists’ Studios Pauschale für Lebenshaltungskosten monatlich: 1.500 Euro einmalige Reisekostenpauschale: bis zu 600 Euro,,,"The residency includes: free use of an apartment for six months, free use of a studio in the Artists’ Studios, a flat rate for living expenses per month: 1,500 euros, one-time travel allowance: up to 600 euros",visual art,residence stipend,,Israel,Tel Aviv,['Visual Arts'],['Grant/Funding'],[],[],"[{'category': 'Accommodation/Housing', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'free use of apartment for six months'}, {'category': 'Accommodation/Housing', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'free use of studio in the Artists’ Studios'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 1500.0, 'amount_max': 1500.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'per month', 'note': 'living expenses allowance'}, {'category': 'Travel Support', 'amount_min': 600.0, 'amount_max': 600.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'travel allowance'}]",2026-09-24 09:59:19.149070+00:00,,,,,de,Residenzstipendium Tel Aviv,"Die Ausschreibung richtet sich an professionelle Kunstschaffende mit Lebensmittelpunkt in Nordrhein-Westfalen, die bereits öffentliche Anerkennung erfahren haben oder erste berufliche Erfolge vorweisen können. Studierende sind ausgeschlossen eine erneute Bewerbung ehemaliger Stipendiat:innen ist nicht möglich es besteht Residenzpflicht englische Sprachkenntnisse sind Voraussetzung",Residency Grant Tel Aviv,"The call is open to professional artists with their primary residence in North Rhine-Westphalia, who have already received public recognition or can demonstrate initial professional success. Students are excluded. Reapplication by former scholarship holders is not possible. Residency is mandatory. English language skills are required.",,,2026-09-24 09:58:19.648006+00:00
matadero_madrid_e7f0c61fb700,matadero_madrid,https://www.cinetecamadrid.com/sites/default/files/inline-files/ANIMARIO%202026%20RULES%20AND%20REGULATIONS_INT%20SHORT%20FILM%20COMPETITION.pdf,,Cineteca Madrid,"To open participation to works from all over the world, supporting a diversity of themes, styles and techniques, and placing special emphasis on those works that explore artistic avenues in dialogue with other disciplines, and that use animation in a particularly creative manner.",animation / animated cinema,competition,Spain,Madrid,"• Best Short Film Award, endowed with €5,000
• Jury Special Mention, with no monetary award.",,,"To open participation to works from all over the world, supporting a diversity of themes, styles and techniques, and placing special emphasis on those works that explore artistic avenues in dialogue with other disciplines, and that use animation in a particularly creative manner.",animation / animated cinema,competition,,Spain,Madrid,['Film/Video'],['Competition/Prize'],[],['Spain'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': 5000.0, 'amount_max': 5000.0, 'currency': 'EUR', 'period': 'one-time', 'note': 'Best Short Film Award'}, {'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'Jury Special Mention has no monetary award'}]",2026-09-24 09:59:19.149142+00:00,,,,,en,ANIMARIO 2026 RULES AND REGULATIONS INTERNATIONAL SHORT FILM COMPETITION,"- Any producer and/or director, any natural or legal person, over 18 years old, who hold the rights to the works and have previously undergone the selection process, may participate.
- All the works which are submitted to the competitive sections must have been completed after January 2025.
- The works must not have been released in the Community of Madrid (a première in Madrid is essential), although works that have participated in online festivals in a limited form will be admitted. Films that have been made publicly available online, outside the context of a film festival, are not eligible. Under no circumstances may submitted films have been broadcast on television.
- The works will be presented in their original language. In the event of a version other than Spanish, a subtitled version in Spanish or English must be sent.
- Works produced using any animation technique will be admitted.
- As an exception, the Festival will accept films that are in an advanced editing (rough cut) process. The selection committee may request the most up-to-date version of the work before making a final decision",ANIMARIO 2026 RULES AND REGULATIONS INTERNATIONAL SHORT FILM COMPETITION,"- Any producer and/or director, any natural or legal person, over 18 years old, who hold the rights to the works and have previously undergone the selection process, may participate.
- All the works which are submitted to the competitive sections must have been completed after January 2025.
- The works must not have been released in the Community of Madrid (a première in Madrid is essential), although works that have participated in online festivals in a limited form will be admitted. Films that have been made publicly available online, outside the context of a film festival, are not eligible. Under no circumstances may submitted films have been broadcast on television.
- The works will be presented in their original language. In the event of a version other than Spanish, a subtitled version in Spanish or English must be sent.
- Works produced using any animation technique will be admitted.
- As an exception, the Festival will accept films that are in an advanced editing (rough cut) process. The selection committee may request the most up-to-date version of the work before making a final decision",13 September 2026 at 23:59 (CET),2026-09-13,2026-09-24 09:58:19.661130+00:00
matadero_madrid_25c8a4ecf086,matadero_madrid,https://www.mataderomadrid.org/sites/default/files/media/document/2026/07/Bases%20Convocatoria%20Proyectos%20Investigacio%CC%81n%20Situada%202027%20EN.pdf,,"Madrid Destino, through Medialab Matadero","The aim of these residencies is to host, promote, and lend visibility to experimental and critical projects which, grounded in the principle of ‘learning by doing’, are capable of exploring emerging socio-technical scenarios, addressing contemporary issues, and testing unconventional research methodologies.","contemporary art, design, science, technology and society",residencies,Spain,Madrid,,,,"The aim of these residencies is to host, promote, and lend visibility to experimental and critical projects which, grounded in the principle of ‘learning by doing’, are capable of exploring emerging socio-technical scenarios, addressing contemporary issues, and testing unconventional research methodologies.","contemporary art, design, science, technology and society",residencies,,Spain,Madrid,"['Visual Arts', 'Design/Architecture']",['Residency'],[],['Spain'],[],,,,,,en,5th Medialab Matadero Open Call for the Award of Three (3) Residencies within the Annual Situated Research Programme (2027),"This open call establishes the regulatory framework for the award of three (3) research and creation residencies at Medialab Matadero, It is aimed at individuals, collectives, or cultural, artistic, scientific, technological, or research agents developing projects within the fields of situated research, contemporary creation, and transdisciplinary experimentation.

Submitted projects should engage with Medialab Matadero’s lines of work and operate at the margins or intersections of different disciplines, methodologies, and fields of knowledge. Special consideration will be given to projects which, grounded in the principle of ‘learning by doing’, offer new ways of researching, prototyping, documenting, sharing knowledge, or activating communities around contemporary issues.

Submitted projects must fall within the fields of situated research, contemporary creation, and transdisciplinary experimentation. Whether the applicant is an individual, a collective, or an agent, the submitted project must reflect their own research and creative process, be coherent with their trajectory, and demonstrate the capacity to be developed within the context of an in-person residency at the Matadero Madrid Centre for Artists in Residence (hereinafter, the CRA).    

Submitted projects must be the work of the applicant or, in the case of collective projects, of the members of the collective.

Projects must be developed in dialogue with the context, the lines of work, and the communities linked to Medialab Matadero, and must align with the following fundamental guidelines:
 Thematic coherence.  Projects should explore potential intersections between art, design, science and technology, in such a way that their findings, processes, or methodologies contribute to addressing major contemporary urban and global challenges within the framework of the Sustainable Development Goals of the 2030 Agenda. In particular, all submitted projects should engage with the lines of work of Medialab Matadero, which include the themes addressed in the annual programmes Lab 1 Sentient Media, Lab 2 The Metabolic Sublime, Lab 3 Synthetic Minds, Lab 4 Weird Futures  and Lab 5 The Mechanics of Trust , with the aim of updating and further exploring the lines of research opened up by Medialab in recent years. For more information, please visit the Medialab Matadero website.
 Innovation and critical reflection. Submissions must develop a cultural research and creation project incorporating a critical reflection on the digital revolution, its impact on society, and its effects at different levels. Special consideration will be given to projects that contribute to imagining, testing, or constructing fairer and more inclusive, sustainable, and democratic digital futures.
 Dialogue. Projects must establish links with the rest of Medialab Matadero’s activities, showing their capacity for transformation and enrichment through dialogue with partners, whether individuals or organisations, as well as other researchers, communities, and the general public. Special consideration will be given to those projects that are willing to open themselves to exchange with the cultural, social, scientific, technological, and civic context of both Matadero Madrid and the city of Madrid.
 Initiation of the research process:  The projects must carry out documentation tasks, as well as activities relating to learning, dissemination and the exchange of knowledge with the public.",5th Medialab Matadero Open Call for the Award of Three (3) Residencies within the Annual Situated Research Programme (2027),"This open call establishes the regulatory framework for the award of three (3) research and creation residencies at Medialab Matadero, It is aimed at individuals, collectives, or cultural, artistic, scientific, technological, or research agents developing projects within the fields of situated research, contemporary creation, and transdisciplinary experimentation.

Submitted projects should engage with Medialab Matadero’s lines of work and operate at the margins or intersections of different disciplines, methodologies, and fields of knowledge. Special consideration will be given to projects which, grounded in the principle of ‘learning by doing’, offer new ways of researching, prototyping, documenting, sharing knowledge, or activating communities around contemporary issues.

Submitted projects must fall within the fields of situated research, contemporary creation, and transdisciplinary experimentation. Whether the applicant is an individual, a collective, or an agent, the submitted project must reflect their own research and creative process, be coherent with their trajectory, and demonstrate the capacity to be developed within the context of an in-person residency at the Matadero Madrid Centre for Artists in Residence (hereinafter, the CRA).    

Submitted projects must be the work of the applicant or, in the case of collective projects, of the members of the collective.

Projects must be developed in dialogue with the context, the lines of work, and the communities linked to Medialab Matadero, and must align with the following fundamental guidelines:
 Thematic coherence.  Projects should explore potential intersections between art, design, science and technology, in such a way that their findings, processes, or methodologies contribute to addressing major contemporary urban and global challenges within the framework of the Sustainable Development Goals of the 2030 Agenda. In particular, all submitted projects should engage with the lines of work of Medialab Matadero, which include the themes addressed in the annual programmes Lab 1 Sentient Media, Lab 2 The Metabolic Sublime, Lab 3 Synthetic Minds, Lab 4 Weird Futures  and Lab 5 The Mechanics of Trust , with the aim of updating and further exploring the lines of research opened up by Medialab in recent years. For more information, please visit the Medialab Matadero website.
 Innovation and critical reflection. Submissions must develop a cultural research and creation project incorporating a critical reflection on the digital revolution, its impact on society, and its effects at different levels. Special consideration will be given to projects that contribute to imagining, testing, or constructing fairer and more inclusive, sustainable, and democratic digital futures.
 Dialogue. Projects must establish links with the rest of Medialab Matadero’s activities, showing their capacity for transformation and enrichment through dialogue with partners, whether individuals or organisations, as well as other researchers, communities, and the general public. Special consideration will be given to those projects that are willing to open themselves to exchange with the cultural, social, scientific, technological, and civic context of both Matadero Madrid and the city of Madrid.
 Initiation of the research process:  The projects must carry out documentation tasks, as well as activities relating to learning, dissemination and the exchange of knowledge with the public.",,,2026-09-24 09:58:19.661193+00:00
matadero_madrid_bc5ee263b8a9,matadero_madrid,https://www.mataderomadrid.org/sites/default/files/media/document/2026/04/BASES%20CONVOCATORIA%20LAB5_EN.pdf,,Medialab Matadero,"The primary activity of each LAB is the Collaborative Prototyping Laboratory (LPC), an intensive two (2) -week seminar during which five (5) experimental projects related to the themes proposed within the framework of LAB 5 The Mechanics of Truth, are developed collaboratively.","design, art, architecture, urban planning, economics, film, photography, journalism, digital media, environmental sciences, philosophy, engineering, social studies, political science, programming, materials science, activism, or any other field",open call for projects and collaborators,Spain,Madrid,,,,"The primary activity of each LAB is the Collaborative Prototyping Laboratory (LPC), an intensive two (2) -week seminar during which five (5) experimental projects related to the themes proposed within the framework of LAB 5 The Mechanics of Truth, are developed collaboratively.","design, art, architecture, urban planning, economics, film, photography, journalism, digital media, environmental sciences, philosophy, engineering, social studies, political science, programming, materials science, activism, or any other field",open call for projects and collaborators,,Spain,Madrid,"['Visual Arts', 'Design/Architecture', 'Film/Video', 'Photography', 'Digital/New Media Arts', 'Other/Non-Arts']",['Open Call'],[],['Spain'],[],,,,,,en,LAB 5 The Mechanics of Truth Collaborative Prototyping Laboratory,"This call is aimed at individuals of legal age from Spain and abroad, with any level of qualification and from diverse disciplines such as design, art, architecture, urban planning, economics, film, photography, journalism, digital media, environmental sci ences, philosophy, engineering, social studies, political science, programming, materials science, activism, or any other field. It is essential to have at least a medium-high level of English that allows for fluent communication with other participants and does not require consecutive translation in meetings.",LAB 5 The Mechanics of Truth Collaborative Prototyping Laboratory,"This call is aimed at individuals of legal age from Spain and abroad, with any level of qualification and from diverse disciplines such as design, art, architecture, urban planning, economics, film, photography, journalism, digital media, environmental sci ences, philosophy, engineering, social studies, political science, programming, materials science, activism, or any other field. It is essential to have at least a medium-high level of English that allows for fluent communication with other participants and does not require consecutive translation in meetings.",,,2026-09-24 09:58:19.661243+00:00
matadero_madrid_68fd1c2a018a,matadero_madrid,https://www.mataderomadrid.org/sites/default/files/media/document/2025/09/bases_convocatoria_bandas.pdf,,"Matadero Madrid / Madrid Destino, Cultura, Turismo y Negocio S.A.","promueve la novena edición de una convocatoria abierta dirigida a bandas y artistas solistas emergentes residentes en la Comunidad de Madrid para 2026. La residencia tendrá una duración de seis meses, entre el 13 de enero y el 10 de julio de 2026.",música,residencia,España,Madrid,,,emergentes,"promueve la novena edición de una convocatoria abierta dirigida a bandas y artistas solistas emergentes residentes en la Comunidad de Madrid para 2026. La residencia tendrá una duración de seis meses, entre el 13 de enero y el 10 de julio de 2026.",música,residencia,emergentes,España,Madrid,['Music'],['Residency'],['Emerging/Early-Career'],['Spain'],[],,,,,,en,IX Convocatoria del Centro de Residencias Artísticas de Matadero Madrid para la asignación de una residencia de seis meses dirigida a bandas y solistas emergentes residentes en la Comunidad Madrid 2026,"Esta convocatoria consta de una única modalidad dirigida a bandas o artistas solistas dentro del género del pop-rock, si bien estos estilos se podrán relacionar con otros géneros como el punk, el garage, la electrónica, el folk o el hip-hop, entre otros.

Podrán presentarse a la Convocatoria, conjuntamente, personas físicas o agrupadas, sin exigirse la formalización de relación jurídica alguna entre ellas. En caso de pluralidad de personas físicas presentadas conjuntamente, se deberá señalar un representante al que el resto de los integrantes del colectivo deberán ceder los derechos de representación y con el que se entenderán todas las relaciones obligaciones, todo ello sin perjuicio de las relaciones internas entre ellos para el cumplimiento de los compromisos de la presente convocatoria. En todo caso, los miembros del colectivo responderán solidariamente.

Solo podrán presentarse aquellas personas que tengan su residencia en la Comunidad de Madrid.

Los artistas o bandas no deben tener ningún contrato discográfico, ni editorial ni de management en el momento de concurrir a esta convocatoria.

Podrán presentarse a la presente convocatoria mayores de edad, con capacidad de obrar y residencia legal en España, y que no incurra en ninguna de las prohibiciones de contratar establecidas en el artículo 71 de la Ley de Contratos del Sector Público.

Los proyectos presentados deberán contener al menos un setenta por ciento (70%) de repertorio propio.",IX Convocatoria del Centro de Residencias Artísticas de Matadero Madrid para la asignación de una residencia de seis meses dirigida a bandas y solistas emergentes residentes en la Comunidad Madrid 2026,"Esta convocatoria consta de una única modalidad dirigida a bandas o artistas solistas dentro del género del pop-rock, si bien estos estilos se podrán relacionar con otros géneros como el punk, el garage, la electrónica, el folk o el hip-hop, entre otros.

Podrán presentarse a la Convocatoria, conjuntamente, personas físicas o agrupadas, sin exigirse la formalización de relación jurídica alguna entre ellas. En caso de pluralidad de personas físicas presentadas conjuntamente, se deberá señalar un representante al que el resto de los integrantes del colectivo deberán ceder los derechos de representación y con el que se entenderán todas las relaciones obligaciones, todo ello sin perjuicio de las relaciones internas entre ellos para el cumplimiento de los compromisos de la presente convocatoria. En todo caso, los miembros del colectivo responderán solidariamente.

Solo podrán presentarse aquellas personas que tengan su residencia en la Comunidad de Madrid.

Los artistas o bandas no deben tener ningún contrato discográfico, ni editorial ni de management en el momento de concurrir a esta convocatoria.

Podrán presentarse a la presente convocatoria mayores de edad, con capacidad de obrar y residencia legal en España, y que no incurra en ninguna de las prohibiciones de contratar establecidas en el artículo 71 de la Ley de Contratos del Sector Público.

Los proyectos presentados deberán contener al menos un setenta por ciento (70%) de repertorio propio.",segunda quincena de noviembre de 2025,2025-09-24,2026-09-24 09:58:19.665698+00:00
matadero_madrid_cd982f2fa6f8,matadero_madrid,https://www.medialab-matadero.es/sites/default/files/2025-07/BASES%20PROY%20INVESTIGACION%2025-26_EN.pdf,,"Medialab Matadero / Matadero Madrid / Madrid Destino, Cultura, Turismo y Negocio S.A.","the fourth edition of the Annual Research Projects Program is presented with an open international invitation to participates. The program will host, support, and showcase the development of three research projects able to explore the relationships between contemporary art, design, science, technology and society in an innovative way, particularly at the edges of classic academic spheres and in the interstitial spaces between established disciplines.","design, art, architecture, urban planning, economics, film, photography, journalism, digital media, environmental sciences, philosophy, engineering, social studies, political science, digital tool programming, material sciences, activism",research projects,Spain,Madrid,"Madrid Destino will cover the costs of all learning, dissemination and public feedback activities proposed by the project and approved by the Head of Programming at Medialab Matadero, in line with Medialab’s budget.",,,"the fourth edition of the Annual Research Projects Program is presented with an open international invitation to participates. The program will host, support, and showcase the development of three research projects able to explore the relationships between contemporary art, design, science, technology and society in an innovative way, particularly at the edges of classic academic spheres and in the interstitial spaces between established disciplines.","design, art, architecture, urban planning, economics, film, photography, journalism, digital media, environmental sciences, philosophy, engineering, social studies, political science, digital tool programming, material sciences, activism",research projects,,Spain,Madrid,"['Visual Arts', 'Design/Architecture', 'Film/Video', 'Photography', 'Digital/New Media Arts', 'Other/Non-Arts']",['Other'],[],['Spain'],"[{'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'covers costs of learning, dissemination and public feedback activities within approved project budget'}]",2026-09-24 09:59:19.149167+00:00,,,,,en,IV INVITATION TO PARTICIPATE IN THE SELECTION OF THREE SITUATED RESEARCH PROJECTS AS PART OF THE ANNUAL MEDIALAB MATADERO PROGRAM AT MATADERO MADRID 2025-2026,"This invitation to participate is aimed at individuals or groups who conduct research in fields related to design, art, architecture, urban planning, economics, film, photography, journalism, digital media, environmental sciences, philosophy, engineering, social studies, political science, digital tool programming, material sciences, activism, or any other field that sheds new light on the chosen themes. Participants will be expected to contribute to the creation of an open space for personal and professional exchange with Medialab Matadero’s local and international audiences, learning communities, and professional and academic circles as well as with the city of Madrid in general. As a result, the working languages will be both Spanish and English. Project leaders must be of legal age, capable of acting, and in possession of the necessary administrative authorizations to stay in Spain during the research project, and must not be subject to any of the prohibitions on contracting established in Article 71 of the Public Sector Contracts Law. Any candidate who has an employment or any other current relationship with Madrid Destino will not be eligible to participate.",IV INVITATION TO PARTICIPATE IN THE SELECTION OF THREE SITUATED RESEARCH PROJECTS AS PART OF THE ANNUAL MEDIALAB MATADERO PROGRAM AT MATADERO MADRID 2025-2026,"This invitation to participate is aimed at individuals or groups who conduct research in fields related to design, art, architecture, urban planning, economics, film, photography, journalism, digital media, environmental sciences, philosophy, engineering, social studies, political science, digital tool programming, material sciences, activism, or any other field that sheds new light on the chosen themes. Participants will be expected to contribute to the creation of an open space for personal and professional exchange with Medialab Matadero’s local and international audiences, learning communities, and professional and academic circles as well as with the city of Madrid in general. As a result, the working languages will be both Spanish and English. Project leaders must be of legal age, capable of acting, and in possession of the necessary administrative authorizations to stay in Spain during the research project, and must not be subject to any of the prohibitions on contracting established in Article 71 of the Public Sector Contracts Law. Any candidate who has an employment or any other current relationship with Madrid Destino will not be eligible to participate.",,,2026-09-24 09:58:19.665765+00:00
matadero_madrid_7f9204014413,matadero_madrid,https://www.mataderomadrid.org/sites/default/files/media/document/2025/05/bases_arte_y_educacion_2025-26.pdf,,"Matadero Madrid / Madrid Destino, Cultura, Turismo y Negocio S.A.","promueve una convocatoria abierta de investigación y acción dirigida a creadores, colectivos y agentes culturales que trabajen en torno al arte y la educación.",arte y la educación,residencia,España,Madrid,,,,"promueve una convocatoria abierta de investigación y acción dirigida a creadores, colectivos y agentes culturales que trabajen en torno al arte y la educación.",arte y la educación,residencia,,España,Madrid,['Other/Non-Arts'],['Residency'],[],['Spain'],[],,,,,,en,V Convocatoria del Centro de Residencias Artísticas de Matadero Madrid para la asignación de una residencia en torno al arte y la educación (2025-2026),"Solo podrán presentarse aquellas personas físicas, mayores de edad, con capacidad de obrar y residencia legal en España y que no incurran en ninguna de las prohibiciones de contratar establecidas en el artículo 71 de la Ley de Contratos del Sector Público, y que tengan su residencia o ámbito principal de acción en la Comunidad de Madrid, cuya documentación o trayectoria acredite tal circunstancia.

