royal_court_theatre_344bc55515e5,royal_court_theatre,https://royalcourttheatre.com/write-and-create/writers/script-submissions-invitations/submit-your-play,https://royalcourttheatre.com/write-and-create/writers/script-submissions-invitations/script-submissions-form/,Royal Court Theatre,"We’re dedicated to finding the most exciting new plays, underpinned by our commitment to open script submissions.",theatre,open script submissions,UK and around the world,,,,,"We’re dedicated to finding the most exciting new plays, underpinned by our commitment to open script submissions.",theatre,open script submissions,,UK and around the world,,['Theatre'],['Open Call'],[],"['United Kingdom', 'International/Global']",[],,,,,,en,Submit Your Play,"Anyone writing in English, from the UK and around the world, can send us a play. We’re unable to receive hard copies, but if you have access needs which mean our system is a barrier, please contact literary@royalcourttheatre.com . We do not accept screenplays, novels, poetry or radio plays. We can only accept scripts as a PDF or Word document with a maximum size of 10MB. We only read original, full-length plays (we suggest this would be from around 50 pages or 25-30 pages for a monologue). We are unable to accept more than one submission from a writer at a time, nor consider unsolicited resubmissions or new drafts of plays we have previously read. We do accept scripts for original musicals but cannot accept scores or soundtracks as part of first submission. We’re looking for plays that could be staged at the Royal Court, so encourage writers to understand our work by visiting or exploring our programmes online. We focus on plays that say or do something we haven’t encountered before – in form, content or ideas. We very rarely programme adaptations and therefore do not accept adaptations of novels, films or pre-existing narrative works through our open submissions – we are looking for original plays. Similarly, we are unlikely to programme plays based on histories or biographies, unless handled in a compellingly contemporary way.",Submit Your Play,"Anyone writing in English, from the UK and around the world, can send us a play. We’re unable to receive hard copies, but if you have access needs which mean our system is a barrier, please contact literary@royalcourttheatre.com . We do not accept screenplays, novels, poetry or radio plays. We can only accept scripts as a PDF or Word document with a maximum size of 10MB. We only read original, full-length plays (we suggest this would be from around 50 pages or 25-30 pages for a monologue). We are unable to accept more than one submission from a writer at a time, nor consider unsolicited resubmissions or new drafts of plays we have previously read. We do accept scripts for original musicals but cannot accept scores or soundtracks as part of first submission. We’re looking for plays that could be staged at the Royal Court, so encourage writers to understand our work by visiting or exploring our programmes online. We focus on plays that say or do something we haven’t encountered before – in form, content or ideas. We very rarely programme adaptations and therefore do not accept adaptations of novels, films or pre-existing narrative works through our open submissions – we are looking for original plays. Similarly, we are unlikely to programme plays based on histories or biographies, unless handled in a compellingly contemporary way.",,,2026-09-24 09:58:39.696786+00:00
statens_vaerksteder_for_kunst_a543d1a88fd3,statens_vaerksteder_for_kunst,https://svfk.dk/en/apply-for-residency,https://svfk.dk/en/application-form/,Danish Art Workshops (SVFK),"At the Danish Art Workshops, professional artists, designers, crafts people and art restorers can work in large formats, which their own studios or equipment cannot facilitate.","visual art, crafts and design",residency,Denmark,,"All residencies at SVFK are funded as scholarships from the Danish State as part of its support of the arts. Studio, workshop, accommodation in the guest flat, consultation etc. are free of charge.",free of charge,professional,"At the Danish Art Workshops, professional artists, designers, crafts people and art restorers can work in large formats, which their own studios or equipment cannot facilitate.","visual art, crafts and design",residency,professional,Denmark,,"['Visual Arts', 'Craft', 'Design/Architecture']",['Residency'],['Established/Professional'],['Denmark'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'residencies funded as scholarships from the Danish State'}, {'category': 'Accommodation/Housing', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'guest flat accommodation free of charge'}, {'category': 'Mentorship/Training', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'consultation included free of charge'}, {'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'studio and workshop access free of charge'}]",2026-09-24 09:59:23.960683+00:00,False,,,,en,Apply for residency,"At the Danish Art Workshops, professional artists, designers, crafts people and art restorers can work in large formats, which their own studios or equipment cannot facilitate. Non-Danish applicants may only apply with projects directed towards a specific exhibition or other cultural activity in Denmark, which has already been accepted. However, non-Danish applicants already living in Denmark can apply equally to Danish applicants. The only requirement is, that you have been granted with a residency at the SVFK previously. Make one application together, describing your cooperation, and add CVs for all participants. One of you must be appointed as the contact person for the project. You can apply for a residency of up to six months. The length of the residency has to fit your project. Please state if you are flexible on the exact period of time or the studio you have applied for.",Apply for residency,"At the Danish Art Workshops, professional artists, designers, crafts people and art restorers can work in large formats, which their own studios or equipment cannot facilitate. Non-Danish applicants may only apply with projects directed towards a specific exhibition or other cultural activity in Denmark, which has already been accepted. However, non-Danish applicants already living in Denmark can apply equally to Danish applicants. The only requirement is, that you have been granted with a residency at the SVFK previously. Make one application together, describing your cooperation, and add CVs for all participants. One of you must be appointed as the contact person for the project. You can apply for a residency of up to six months. The length of the residency has to fit your project. Please state if you are flexible on the exact period of time or the studio you have applied for.","The beginning of Feb, May, Aug, and Nov.",2027-11-24,2026-09-24 09:58:39.725968+00:00
wiels_brussels_fcbabea29454,wiels_brussels,https://wiels.org/en/residency-programme,https://wiels.org/en/blog/open-call-residency-2026,WIELS,"an international residency programme focused on artistic practice, critical reflection, dialogue with peers, and engagement with diverse audiences.",artistic practice,residency programme,Belgium,Brussels,Selected artists are offered a six-month residency (January–June or July–December) and access to one of the nine studios at WIELS. Accommodation is not provided for artists based in Belgium.,,,"an international residency programme focused on artistic practice, critical reflection, dialogue with peers, and engagement with diverse audiences.",artistic practice,residency programme,,Belgium,Brussels,['Multidisciplinary'],['Residency'],[],['Belgium'],"[{'category': 'Grant/Stipend', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': 'per month', 'note': 'six-month residency'}, {'category': 'Accommodation/Housing', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'accommodation not provided for artists based in Belgium'}, {'category': 'Materials/Production Costs', 'amount_min': None, 'amount_max': None, 'currency': None, 'period': None, 'note': 'access to one of nine studios at WIELS'}]",2026-09-24 09:59:23.960693+00:00,,,,,en,A residency at WIELS,This call is intended for Belgian artists or artists residing in Belgium who have completed their studies and have been actively contributing to the Belgian art scene for at least three years.,A residency at WIELS,This call is intended for Belgian artists or artists residing in Belgium who have completed their studies and have been actively contributing to the Belgian art scene for at least three years.,published each year in May,2027-05-24,2026-09-24 09:58:39.754620+00:00
